{"level":30,"time":1776973748909,"pid":123,"hostname":"844f2260-bff","step":"review-runs","item":"15.md","index":9,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01Tjy5GACWeCULRYqCvFZsYz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Great! Now I have critical information about the site:\n\nKey Facts:\n- **Zoning:** MF-2 (Multi-Family Residence — Medium Density)\n- **Adjacent Property:** SF-3 parcel (0406100210) immediately adjacent\n- **Compatibility Standards:** LDC Subchapter F triggered by adjacent SF-3 parcel. Within 25 ft of the SF-3 lot line: maximum 2 stories / 30 ft height. Step-up schedule applies for structures beyond 25 ft. Screening/buffer requirements between MF and SF-3 uses apply.\n- **No Waterfront Overlay:** Site is not in a waterfront overlay\n- **No Lake Austin shoreline:** Not applicable\n- **No Hazardous Pipeline:** Not mentioned in the facts\n\nSo for this grouping (ZLU-15 - Setback Requirements and Compatibility Provisions), the key issues are:\n\n1. **Compatibility Standards (Article 10)** - This is relevant because:\n   - Site is MF-2 (which is more restrictive than MF-4, so Article 10 may apply)\n   - The facts mention \"LDC Subchapter F\" compatibility standards triggered by SF-3 adjacency\n   - However, the facts note this is the OLD compatibility framework (Subchapter F with 25 ft band)\n   - The grouping document mentions that Article 10 was completely replaced effective July 15, 2024\n   - Need to check when the site plan was submitted to determine which framework applies\n\n2. **Zoning District Setbacks** - MF-2 district setbacks must be verified\n\n3. **Adjacent SF-3 Property** - Need to verify if this triggers Article 10 under the current framework\n   - Under current Article 10: triggering property is 1-3 dwelling units zoned SF-5 or more restrictive\n   - SF-3 is more restrictive than SF-5 (SF-5 is less restrictive than SF-4B, which is less restrictive than SF-3)\n   - The SF-3 parcel would qualify as a triggering property if it contains 1-3 dwelling units, but the facts don't specify the unit count. The compatibility standards section defines triggering properties as those with 1-3 units zoned SF-5 or more restrictive, and SF-3 clearly meets the zoning requirement.\n\nSince the site plan was submitted May 20, 2025—well after the July 15, 2024 effective date of the new Article 10—the updated framework governs this analysis rather than the previous standards.\n\nNow I need to verify two conditions: whether the adjacent SF-3 parcel qualifies as a triggering property with 1-3 dwelling units, and whether the subject site's MF-2 zoning falls within the applicability threshold. If both conditions are met, I'll need to examine the submitted plans to confirm all required compatibility measures are properly shown.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":13,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8333,"cache_read_input_tokens":37374,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":8333,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d203a61d-b956-4bf7-a62f-71a0e7d71a2a","uuid":"c8230927-69ab-4838-9241-8bb2f25cfedb"}
