{"level":30,"time":1776973749234,"pid":123,"hostname":"844f2260-bff","step":"review-runs","item":"15.md","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01SUxEUGiWFB5t2LvB2whQvL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Excellent. Now I have the context:\n\n**Project Summary:**\n- Valley View Townhomes (SP-2025-0126C)\n- 3759 Valley View Road, Austin, TX 78704\n- Site Area: 2.16 acres (with discrepancies noted in facts.md)\n- Zoning: MF-2 (Multi-Family Residence — Medium Density)\n- Proposed Use: 39 multi-family townhome units, 8 buildings\n- Submitted: May 20, 2025\n- Approval Status: Awaiting Update (first-round comment response pending)\n\n**Key Applicability Determinations for Grouping 15 (Setback Requirements & Compatibility):**\n\n1. **Article 10 Compatibility Triggered?**\n   - facts.md says: \"Compatibility Standards: LDC Subchapter F triggered by adjacent SF-3 parcel (0406100210). Within 25 ft of the SF-3 lot line: maximum 2 stories / 30 ft height. Step-up schedule applies for structures beyond 25 ft. Screening/buffer requirements between MF and SF-3 uses apply.\"\n   - Wait - this says \"Subchapter F\" not \"Article 10\". Let me re-read the grouping. \n   - The grouping is for \"Article 10 — Effective July 15, 2024\" which is about compatibility standards\n   - But the facts.md mentions \"Residential Design Standards (Subchapter F): Active overlay\" at line 57\n   - This is confusing. Let me check the code references in the grouping more carefully.\n   - Looking at the grouping Overview, it says \"Article 10 was completely repealed and replaced by Ord. No. 20240516-004 effective July 15, 2024.\"\n   - However, the facts.md is describing something called \"Subchapter F\" which was the pre-2024 compatibility standards framework\n   - Since the site plan was submitted May 20, 2025—well after the July 15, 2024 effective date—the new Article 10 framework applies. The applicability test requires the site to be zoned MF-4 or less restrictive and within 75 feet of a triggering property. MF-2 meets the zoning threshold, and SF-5 is the adjacent triggering use.\n\nThe facts indicate the SF-3 parcel sits within 25 feet of the site's lot line, satisfying the 75-foot proximity requirement. Article 10 is therefore triggered. Standard zoning setbacks under LDC § 25-2-492 apply to the MF-2 district. The waterfront overlay doesn't apply here since the site lacks a WO designation.\n\nThe site isn't in the Lake Austin district and has no shoreline frontage, so those provisions don't apply. No hazardous pipeline is noted in the facts. Historic district designation, regulating plans, and special overlays like CO/PUD/NCCD aren't mentioned in the zoning information. I should verify whether the property qualifies as a through lot by checking if it fronts two parallel streets—the Valley View Road address suggests single frontage, but I'll confirm when reviewing the site plan sheets.\n\nStarting my document review, I'll examine the cover sheet for project details, the plat for property boundaries, the site plan for setback and building locations, electrical sheets for transformer placement, and the tree and landscape plans for existing and proposed features.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":13,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8253,"cache_read_input_tokens":37389,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":8253,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"33f519bd-bced-4a7a-aae5-831dbf134acc","uuid":"1b0b8c86-ec8b-40db-9709-fdc55775a143"}
