{"level":30,"time":1776973751990,"pid":123,"hostname":"844f2260-bff","step":"review-runs","item":"16.md","index":5,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TR9uPr49bHMDErVMpDmNaM","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Sheet 4 — Existing Conditions Survey\n     2→\n     3→Topographic survey detailing existing structures, trees, and property boundaries.\n     4→\n     5→## Reading Guide\n     6→\n     7→This sheet contains the Boundary, Improvements, Topographic & Tree Survey representing the existing conditions for the Valley View Townhomes project. Its primary purpose is to document the baseline physical state of the site prior to development, detailing topographic contours, existing structures, property boundaries, easements, and a comprehensive tree inventory.\n     8→\n     9→**Key values**:\n    10→* Existing Slab Finished Floor Elevation (F.F.E.): 686.8\n    11→* Survey Coordinate System: Texas Coordinate System of 1983 (NAD83) Central Zone, Grid\n    12→* Largest surveyed trees on site: 36\" Hackberry (Tree #4028), 34\" Live Oak (Tree #4042), and 28\" Live Oaks/Hackberry (Trees #4000, #4025, #4026)\n    13→* Job Number: 20240953 \n    14→* Project Number: RJ3 70496\n    15→\n    16→**Content blocks on this sheet**:\n    17→\n    18→* **Block 1**: Main site plan drawing — Shows the existing property conditions including topographic contours, property lines, existing slabs, fences, utility lines, and surveyed tree locations (marked with '+' and ID numbers). Notable areas include \"LOT 2 MECEY SUBDIVISION\" and adjacent \"VALLEY VIEW ROAD\". Use VISION to examine the spatial layout, topographic contours, and physical site features.\n    19→* **Block 5**: Legend — Defines the symbols and abbreviations used throughout the site plan for pins, monuments, fences, utility lines (water, wastewater, electric), and easements. READ the block content for specific symbol definitions.\n    20→* **Block 12**: Tree Table — A schedule listing the cataloged trees found on the property, detailing their ID number (corresponding to the plan drawing), caliper size in inches, and species (e.g., Live Oak, Hackberry, Pecan). READ for exact values and species of specific trees.\n    21→* **Blocks 2, 4, 10**: Project and Title Blocks — Contains the project name (Valley View Townhomes), site address, sheet title (Existing Conditions Survey), and contact information for Bleyl Engineering and Sinclair Land Surveying. READ for project context and firm details.\n    22→* **Blocks 3, 6, 8**: Survey Data & Document Control — Contains the survey's bearing basis (NAD83), job/project numbers, sheet numbering (Sheet 4 of 39), and CAD/design routing information. READ for specific coordinate system references and document tracking numbers.\n    23→* **Blocks 7, 9, 11**: Boilerplate & Administrative — Contains surveyor certification notes, the Registered Professional Land Surveyor (Ryan T. Lenz) signature and state seal, and a list of Bleyl Engineering office locations. READ the block content for surveyor credentials, certification dates, and legal disclaimers.\n    24→\n    25→---\n    26→\n    27→All other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n    28→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f8d013d8-a941-49c2-99ab-d6f637200362","uuid":"3226ce65-56e6-44f0-a4c9-1818e94bfb3c","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/vercel/sandbox/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-04/guide.md","content":"# Sheet 4 — Existing Conditions Survey\n\nTopographic survey detailing existing structures, trees, and property boundaries.\n\n## Reading Guide\n\nThis sheet contains the Boundary, Improvements, Topographic & Tree Survey representing the existing conditions for the Valley View Townhomes project. Its primary purpose is to document the baseline physical state of the site prior to development, detailing topographic contours, existing structures, property boundaries, easements, and a comprehensive tree inventory.\n\n**Key values**:\n* Existing Slab Finished Floor Elevation (F.F.E.): 686.8\n* Survey Coordinate System: Texas Coordinate System of 1983 (NAD83) Central Zone, Grid\n* Largest surveyed trees on site: 36\" Hackberry (Tree #4028), 34\" Live Oak (Tree #4042), and 28\" Live Oaks/Hackberry (Trees #4000, #4025, #4026)\n* Job Number: 20240953 \n* Project Number: RJ3 70496\n\n**Content blocks on this sheet**:\n\n* **Block 1**: Main site plan drawing — Shows the existing property conditions including topographic contours, property lines, existing slabs, fences, utility lines, and surveyed tree locations (marked with '+' and ID numbers). Notable areas include \"LOT 2 MECEY SUBDIVISION\" and adjacent \"VALLEY VIEW ROAD\". Use VISION to examine the spatial layout, topographic contours, and physical site features.\n* **Block 5**: Legend — Defines the symbols and abbreviations used throughout the site plan for pins, monuments, fences, utility lines (water, wastewater, electric), and easements. READ the block content for specific symbol definitions.\n* **Block 12**: Tree Table — A schedule listing the cataloged trees found on the property, detailing their ID number (corresponding to the plan drawing), caliper size in inches, and species (e.g., Live Oak, Hackberry, Pecan). READ for exact values and species of specific trees.\n* **Blocks 2, 4, 10**: Project and Title Blocks — Contains the project name (Valley View Townhomes), site address, sheet title (Existing Conditions Survey), and contact information for Bleyl Engineering and Sinclair Land Surveying. READ for project context and firm details.\n* **Blocks 3, 6, 8**: Survey Data & Document Control — Contains the survey's bearing basis (NAD83), job/project numbers, sheet numbering (Sheet 4 of 39), and CAD/design routing information. READ for specific coordinate system references and document tracking numbers.\n* **Blocks 7, 9, 11**: Boilerplate & Administrative — Contains surveyor certification notes, the Registered Professional Land Surveyor (Ryan T. Lenz) signature and state seal, and a list of Bleyl Engineering office locations. READ the block content for surveyor credentials, certification dates, and legal disclaimers.\n\n---\n\nAll other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n","numLines":28,"startLine":1,"totalLines":28}}}
{"level":30,"time":1776973751992,"pid":123,"hostname":"844f2260-bff","step":"review-runs","item":"16.md","index":5,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KprSLcMaPhKhsKQEq1SzvB","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Sheet 31 — Landscape Plan\n     2→\n     3→Landscape design plan featuring planting details and irrigation notes.\n     4→\n     5→## Reading Guide\n     6→\n     7→This sheet presents the Landscape Plan for the Valley View Townhomes project, detailing the layout of plantings, open spaces, hardscape features, and site contours. It serves as the primary reference for landscape grading, planting mitigation requirements, and automatic irrigation system specifications.\n     8→\n     9→**Key values:**\n    10→*   **Drawing Scale:** 1\" = 20'-0\"\n    11→*   **Topsoil Placement Depth:** Finished elevation for parking lot islands and similar areas must be at least 6 inches below the finished parking lot/curb elevation.\n    12→*   **Irrigation Spray Limits:** No spray irrigation is permitted on areas less than 10 feet wide (e.g., medians, buffer strips).\n    13→*   **Irrigation Setbacks:** Above-ground irrigation emission devices must be set back at least 6 inches from impervious surfaces.\n    14→*   **Rain Shut-off Threshold:** Automatic rain shut-off devices must trigger after more than 1/2 inch (0.5\") of rainfall.\n    15→*   **Tree Mitigation Size:** Street yard and parking lot trees exceeding 1.5 caliper inches count towards mitigation.\n    16→*   **Site Elevations:** Topographic contour lines indicate site elevations ranging generally from approximately 660 to 690 feet.\n    17→\n    18→**Content blocks on this sheet:**\n    19→\n    20→*   **Block 2: drawing — Main Landscape and Site Plan**\n    21→    A comprehensive site plan illustrating building footprints, parking layouts, sidewalks, utility lines (Water, Storm Drain, Overhead Electric), topographical contours, and the distribution of landscape elements.\n    22→    *Use VISION to examine* the spatial layout of the site, locate specific landscape zones (using H-series key notes), trace contour grading, and identify the placement of mitigation trees.\n    23→\n    24→*   **Block 5: notes — Key Notes & Legend**\n    25→    Defines the hatch patterns and symbols used in the main drawing, including paving (H.1), street yards (H.2, H.3), parking lot landscaping (H.4), common open space (H.5), wooden privacy fences (H.6), and sod (H.7). It also defines abbreviations for tree types (SY, PL, P, M).\n    26→    *READ the block content for* exact definitions of hatch patterns, symbols, and mitigation tree sizing requirements (>1.5 cal. inch) to accurately interpret the main drawing.\n    27→\n    28→*   **Block 3: notes — Irrigation Notes**\n    29→    Technical specifications ensuring the automatic irrigation system complies with TCEQ Chapter 344. It covers hardware requirements (master valves, rain shut-offs), spatial constraints, and deliverables required from the installer (as-built plans, water budgets).\n    30→    *READ the block content for* specific compliance metrics, installation constraints, and administrative requirements for final plumbing inspection.\n    31→\n    32→*   **Block 4: notes — General Landscape Notes**\n    33→    Specific grading and soil requirements for landscaped areas adjacent to paving, detailing the necessary finished elevation offsets to accommodate topsoil placement. Also provides guidance on drought variance procedures.\n    34→    *READ the block content for* exact grading dimensions (6 inches below finished elevation) and supplemental irrigation requirements.\n    35→\n    36→*   **Block 1: diagram — Scale and Orientation**\n    37→    Provides the graphical scale and North arrow for the main drawing.\n    38→    *READ the block content for* the exact scale (1\" = 20'-0\") and *Use VISION to* orient the site layout.\n    39→\n    40→*   **Blocks 6, 7, 8, 9: various — Boilerplate & Administrative**\n    41→    Contains the title block information, including the project name (Valley View Townhomes), location (3759 Valley View Road, Austin, TX), property owner (WM 41 Austin RE, LLC), and the licensed landscape architect's professional seal (dated 02/13/2026).\n    42→    *READ the block content for* general project context, property address, and professional certification details.\n    43→\n    44→---\n    45→\n    46→- `block-3.md` — notes: Irrigation notes detailing requirements for automatic irrigation systems to comply with TCEQ Chapter\n    47→\n    48→All other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n    49→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f8d013d8-a941-49c2-99ab-d6f637200362","uuid":"3d30baec-0e61-4c55-bd57-bb254af23c96","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/vercel/sandbox/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-31/guide.md","content":"# Sheet 31 — Landscape Plan\n\nLandscape design plan featuring planting details and irrigation notes.\n\n## Reading Guide\n\nThis sheet presents the Landscape Plan for the Valley View Townhomes project, detailing the layout of plantings, open spaces, hardscape features, and site contours. It serves as the primary reference for landscape grading, planting mitigation requirements, and automatic irrigation system specifications.\n\n**Key values:**\n*   **Drawing Scale:** 1\" = 20'-0\"\n*   **Topsoil Placement Depth:** Finished elevation for parking lot islands and similar areas must be at least 6 inches below the finished parking lot/curb elevation.\n*   **Irrigation Spray Limits:** No spray irrigation is permitted on areas less than 10 feet wide (e.g., medians, buffer strips).\n*   **Irrigation Setbacks:** Above-ground irrigation emission devices must be set back at least 6 inches from impervious surfaces.\n*   **Rain Shut-off Threshold:** Automatic rain shut-off devices must trigger after more than 1/2 inch (0.5\") of rainfall.\n*   **Tree Mitigation Size:** Street yard and parking lot trees exceeding 1.5 caliper inches count towards mitigation.\n*   **Site Elevations:** Topographic contour lines indicate site elevations ranging generally from approximately 660 to 690 feet.\n\n**Content blocks on this sheet:**\n\n*   **Block 2: drawing — Main Landscape and Site Plan**\n    A comprehensive site plan illustrating building footprints, parking layouts, sidewalks, utility lines (Water, Storm Drain, Overhead Electric), topographical contours, and the distribution of landscape elements.\n    *Use VISION to examine* the spatial layout of the site, locate specific landscape zones (using H-series key notes), trace contour grading, and identify the placement of mitigation trees.\n\n*   **Block 5: notes — Key Notes & Legend**\n    Defines the hatch patterns and symbols used in the main drawing, including paving (H.1), street yards (H.2, H.3), parking lot landscaping (H.4), common open space (H.5), wooden privacy fences (H.6), and sod (H.7). It also defines abbreviations for tree types (SY, PL, P, M).\n    *READ the block content for* exact definitions of hatch patterns, symbols, and mitigation tree sizing requirements (>1.5 cal. inch) to accurately interpret the main drawing.\n\n*   **Block 3: notes — Irrigation Notes**\n    Technical specifications ensuring the automatic irrigation system complies with TCEQ Chapter 344. It covers hardware requirements (master valves, rain shut-offs), spatial constraints, and deliverables required from the installer (as-built plans, water budgets).\n    *READ the block content for* specific compliance metrics, installation constraints, and administrative requirements for final plumbing inspection.\n\n*   **Block 4: notes — General Landscape Notes**\n    Specific grading and soil requirements for landscaped areas adjacent to paving, detailing the necessary finished elevation offsets to accommodate topsoil placement. Also provides guidance on drought variance procedures.\n    *READ the block content for* exact grading dimensions (6 inches below finished elevation) and supplemental irrigation requirements.\n\n*   **Block 1: diagram — Scale and Orientation**\n    Provides the graphical scale and North arrow for the main drawing.\n    *READ the block content for* the exact scale (1\" = 20'-0\") and *Use VISION to* orient the site layout.\n\n*   **Blocks 6, 7, 8, 9: various — Boilerplate & Administrative**\n    Contains the title block information, including the project name (Valley View Townhomes), location (3759 Valley View Road, Austin, TX), property owner (WM 41 Austin RE, LLC), and the licensed landscape architect's professional seal (dated 02/13/2026).\n    *READ the block content for* general project context, property address, and professional certification details.\n\n---\n\n- `block-3.md` — notes: Irrigation notes detailing requirements for automatic irrigation systems to comply with TCEQ Chapter\n\nAll other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n","numLines":49,"startLine":1,"totalLines":49}}}
