: Austin Full Purpose\n    83→\n    84→SP-2025-0126C\n    85→Submittal Date: May 20, 2025\n    86→\n    87→## Block 9: text_block — This block is a disclaimer from Bleyl Engineering stating that they are not responsible for the accuracy of the survey or design errors resulting from survey inaccuracies.\n    88→\n    89→Bleyl Engineering and its associates will not be held responsible for the accuracy of the survey or for design errors or\n    90→omissions resulting from survey inaccuracies.\n    91→\n    92→## Block 10: text_block — This block is a note stating that all detention basins, water quality ponds, and appurtenances must be maintained by the record owner in accordance with the Drainage and Environmental Criteria Manual.\n    93→\n    94→All detention basins, water quality ponds and appurtenances which receive stormwater runoff from commercial or\n    95→multi-family development shall be maintained by the record owner in accordance with the maintenance standards in the\n    96→Drainage and Environmental Criteria Manual.\n    97→\n    98→## Block 11: text_block — This block is a note stating that compliance with the Commercial and Multi-Family Recycling Ordinance is mandatory.\n    99→\n   100→Compliance with the Commercial and Multi-Family Recycling Ordinance is mandatory for multi-family complexes,\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f8d013d8-a941-49c2-99ab-d6f637200362","uuid":"48cd2668-5bf3-4013-9cd7-36272ff6ea45","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/vercel/sandbox/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-01/blocks.md","content":"# Sheet 1 — Content Blocks\n\n## Block 1: drawing — This block shows a map of the project location, highlighting the surrounding streets and intersection. A pointer indicates the specific project location.\n\n[Map showing the project location and surrounding streets.]\n\nN\n\nPROJECT\nLOCATION\n\n## Block 5: table — This block contains data related to the Austin Fire Department's requirements for the project. It includes information such as fire design codes, fire flow demand, occupancy classification, construction classification, building fire area, automatic fire sprinkler system type, reduced fire flow demand, applies to project status, AFD fire hydrant flow test dates and locations, city of Austin pipeline ordinance compliance, high-rise status, international wildland-urban interface code compliance, and alternative method of compliance AMOC.\n\nAustin Fire Department\n\n| Fire Design Codes | 2021 International Fire Code Edition\nwith City of Austin Local Amendments |\n|---|---|\n| Fire Flow Demand @ 20 psi\n(gpm) | 3000 GPM |\n| Occupancy Classification | R3 |\n| Construction Classification | Type V-B |\n| Building Fire Area (s.f.) | 13,344 |\n| Automatic Fire Sprinkler System\nType (If applicable) | NFPA 13D |\n| Reduced Fire Flow Demand @ 20\npsi for having a sprinkler system\n(gpm) | 1500 GPM |\n| AFD Fire Hydrant Flow Test Date | 3/21/2025 |\n| AFD Fire Hydrant Flow Test\nLocation | 3700 Valley View Rd. |\n| City of Austin Pipeline Ordinance\nApplies to Project | No |\n| High-Rise | No |\n| International Wildland-Urban\nInterface Code | N/A |\n| Alternative Method of\nCompliance AMOC (If applicable) | N/A |\n\n## Block 6: table — This block contains the site development data for the Valley View Townhomes project. It includes contact information for the owner, engineer, architect, and landscape architect, as well as the legal description, subdivision file number, zoning case number, and limits of construction.\n\nSite Development Data Valley View Townhomes\nOwner: WM 41 Austin RE, LLC.\nContact Person: Richard D. Agnew\n500 West 5th Street, Ste. 1010\nAustin, Texas 78701\nPhone: 512-565-6159\nEmail: Richard.Agnew@slpops.com\n\nEngineer: Bleyl Engineering\nContact Person: Jason Rodgers\n7701 San Felipe, Suite 200\nAustin, Texas 78729\nPhone: (512) 454-2400\nEmail: jrodgers@bleylengineering.com\n\nArchitect: Danze & Davis Architects, Inc.\nContact Person: Harrison Davis\n4701 Spicewood Springs Rd, Ste 200\nAustin, Texas 78759\nPhone: (512) 343-0714\n\nLandscape Architect: Blu Fish Collaborative, Inc.\nContact Person: Mike Fishbaugh\n3607 S. Lamar Blvd., Suite 104\nAustin, Texas 78704\nPhone: (512) 338-4115\n\nLegal Description: Lot 1 Mecey Subdivision, Volume 73, Page 76, Plat Records of Travis County,\nTexas\n2.16 Acres\nSubdivision File No. C8S-75-160\nZoning Case No. C14-2011-0093\nLimits of Construction: 2.26 Acres\n\n## Block 8: text_block — This block is the title and primary identification information for the site plan. It states the project name, address, jurisdiction, SP number, and submittal date.\n\nSite Plan\nValley View Townhomes\n3759 Valley View Road\nAustin, Texas 78704\nJurisdiction: Austin Full Purpose\n\nSP-2025-0126C\nSubmittal Date: May 20, 2025\n\n## Block 9: text_block — This block is a disclaimer from Bleyl Engineering stating that they are not responsible for the accuracy of the survey or design errors resulting from survey inaccuracies.\n\nBleyl Engineering and its associates will not be held responsible for the accuracy of the survey or for design errors or\nomissions resulting from survey inaccuracies.\n\n## Block 10: text_block — This block is a note stating that all detention basins, water quality ponds, and appurtenances must be maintained by the record owner in accordance with the Drainage and Environmental Criteria Manual.\n\nAll detention basins, water quality ponds and appurtenances which receive stormwater runoff from commercial or\nmulti-family development shall be maintained by the record owner in accordance with the maintenance standards in the\nDrainage and Environmental Criteria Manual.\n\n## Block 11: text_block — This block is a note stating that compliance with the Commercial and Multi-Family Recycling Ordinance is mandatory.\n\nCompliance with the Commercial and Multi-Family Recycling Ordinance is mandatory for multi-family complexes,","numLines":100,"startLine":1,"totalLines":277}}}
{"level":30,"time":1776973755743,"pid":123,"hostname":"844f2260-bff","step":"review-runs","item":"32.md","index":7,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_019TK7MjDT7SaRP95Ks7drn9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Excellent. Now I have the facts and README. Let me analyze applicability based on the project characteristics:\n\n**Project Summary:**\n- Address: 3759 Valley View Road, Austin, TX 78704\n- Zoning: MF-2 (Multi-Family Residence — Medium Density)\n- Use: 39 multi-family townhome units\n- Surrounding: SF-3 parcel (triggers LDC Subchapter F compatibility)\n- Watershed: West Bouldin Creek (Urban)\n- No regulating plans (South Lamar NPA is suspended)\n- Nonconforming Signs Area: Yes\n- No DDBP, no DMU, no CBD\n- No UNO, ETOD, TOD, WO, PUD/MUD, VMU, CS-MU-V\n- No redevelopment exception claimed\n- No vesting rights claimed\n- No historic designation\n- No Community Recreation use\n- Adjacent SF-3 triggers LDC Subchapter F (not Article 10 - which is only for MF-4 or less restrictive next to SF-5 or more restrictive)\n\n**Applicability Analysis for ZLU-32 items:**\n\nLet me go through each item and determine applicability:\n\n1. ZLU-32.1 (CBD DDBP) — NOT APPLICABLE (site is MF-2, not CBD)\n2. ZLU-32.2-10 (DDBP items) — NOT APPLICABLE (no DDBP participation)\n3. ZLU-32.11 (DMU setback) — NOT APPLICABLE (site is MF-2, not DMU)\n4. ZLU-32.12 (TOD Live/Work/Flex) — NOT APPLICABLE (no TOD designation)\n\n\n5. ZLU-32.13 (UNO notation) — NOT APPLICABLE (no UNO)\n6. ZLU-32.14 (TOD items) — NOT APPLICABLE (no TOD designation)\n7. ZLU-32.15 (Waterfront Overlay use) — NOT APPLICABLE (no WO)\n8. ZLU-32.16 (ERC Core Transit Corridor) — NOT APPLICABLE (no ERC)\n9. ZLU-32.17 (Adopted corridor plan) — NOT APPLICABLE (no corridor plan applies per facts.md)\n10. ZLU-32.18 (PUD/MUD) — NOT APPLICABLE (not in a PUD/MUD)\n11. ZLU-32.19 (VMU) — NOT APPLICABLE (no VMU designation)\n12. ZLU-32.20 (CS-MU-V) — NOT APPLICABLE (no CS-MU-V designation)\n13. ZLU-32.21 (Neighborhood plan statement) — APPLICABLE but likely moot since South Lamar NPA is suspended\n14. ZLU-32.22 (Article 10) — NOT APPLICABLE. Article 10 requires MF-4 or less restrictive zoning within 75 feet of a triggering property. The adjacent SF-3 zoning doesn't meet the threshold—Article 10 only applies when adjacent to SF-5, RR, or LA zoning. Since the neighboring property is SF-3, this provision doesn't trigger.\n15. ZLU-32.23 (Compatibility notes) — NOT APPLICABLE given Article 10 doesn't apply\n16. ZLU-32.24 (GO/LR\n\n/CS exterior lighting) — NOT APPLICABLE (site is MF-2, not GO/LR/CS)\n17. ZLU-32.25-29 (Article 10 items) — NOT APPLICABLE if Article 10 doesn't apply\n18. ZLU-32.30 (Article 10 exception) — NOT APPLICABLE if Article 10 doesn't apply\n19. ZLU-32.31 (ETOD) — NOT APPLICABLE (no ETOD designation)\n20. ZLU-32.32 (Townhouse lots) — APPLICABLE (townhome units are part of the proposal)\n21. ZLU-32.33 (ADU accessory to civic use) — NOT APPLICABLE (no ADU proposed as accessory to civic use)\n22. ZLU-32.34-35 (UNO multifamily accessibility) — NOT APPLICABLE (no UNO)\n23. ZLU-32.36 (Multifamily transit proximity) — APPLICABLE (multifamily component is proposed)\n24. ZLU-32.37 (Tenant notification for demolition) — NOT APPLICABLE (no occupied building demolition; the prior assisted living facility was demolished in 2022, before this project commenced)\n25. ZLU-32.38 (Condominium) — NOT APPLICABLE (townhomes proposed, not condominiums)\n26. ZLU-32.39 (Redevelopment exception watershed) — NOT APPLICABLE (no redevelopment exception claimed; while site is in urban watershed, it's within desired development zone and subject to IC cap)\n27. ZLU-32.40 (Redevelopment exception trip generation) — NOT APPLICABLE (no redevelopment exception claimed)\n28. ZLU-32.41 (Trip generation limits) — APPLICABLE? Need to verify whether CO establishes trip limits; facts don't reference any CO.\n29. ZLU-32.42 (Group D nonconforming use expansion) — NOT APPLICABLE (no nonconforming use expansion)\n30. ZLU-32.43 (Vesting rights) — NOT APPLICABLE (no vesting rights claimed per facts)\n31. ZLU-32.44 (Site-specific accommodation letter) — NOT APPLICABLE (no accommodation letter mentioned)\n32. ZLU-32.45 (Sign compliance note) — APPLICABLE (required for all sites per checklist)\n33. ZLU-32.46 (UNO sign district) — NOT APPLICABLE (no UNO designation)\n34. ZLU-32.47 (Scenic Roadway sign) — APPLICABLE if Valley View Road qualifies as scenic roadway (requires verification)\n35. ZLU-32.48 (Nonconforming Signs area) — APPLICABLE (facts.md confirms nonconforming signs area exists)\n\nNow reconsidering Article 10 applicability. The rule states it applies to sites zoned MF-4 or less restrictive AND located within 75 feet of a triggering property, where a triggering property is defined as a site with 1–\n\n3 dwelling units zoned SF-5 or more restrictive. The adjacent property is zoned SF-3, which doesn't meet the SF-5 or more restrictive threshold, so it doesn't trigger Article 10. While the site does have LDC Subchapter F compatibility standards triggered by the adjacent SF-3 parcel per facts.md line 54, that's separate from Article 10. Therefore, Article 10 items (ZLU-32.21-29) are NOT APPLICABLE since the adjacent SF-3 zoning doesn't satisfy the triggering criteria.\n\nNow examining the remaining provisions: ZLU-32.20 regarding the neighborhood plan statement appears inapplicable since the South Lamar NPA is suspended. ZLU-32.40 on trip generation limits requires checking if there's a corresponding city ordinance. ZLU-32.46 about scenic roadways needs verification of whether Valley View Road qualifies. I should review the site plan cover sheet to confirm these details.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":14,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":43094,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c1ccbdc1-20f6-4e62-a4c2-17685db82f6f","uuid":"b241b9f1-0b46-4e22-a323-0069f84fd9b8"}
