{"level":30,"time":1776973757885,"pid":123,"hostname":"844f2260-bff","step":"review-runs","item":"15.md","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01QrUUMsrcqemLyWcYJqFTUP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good. Now let me review specific sheets more carefully. Let me check:\n\n1. Whether setback lines are shown on the site plan (Sheet 9)\n2. Whether there's a compatibility exhibit\n3. Transformer pad locations and clearances\n4. Whether this is a through lot\n\nLet me use the vision tool to examine the site plan drawing more carefully for setback lines and compatibility requirements. First, let me check what sheets exist by looking at Sheet 1 blocks.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":13,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6615,"cache_read_input_tokens":51189,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":6615,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"33f519bd-bced-4a7a-aae5-831dbf134acc","uuid":"74751447-139b-41f3-9bac-272bc263717a"}
{"level":30,"time":1776973757894,"pid":123,"hostname":"844f2260-bff","step":"review-runs","item":"16.md","index":8,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SqNqRSqPnXuN1YegkBMRWB","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Sheet 9 — Site Plan\n     2→\n     3→Detailed site plan layout with associated building and parking data.\n     4→\n     5→## Reading Guide\n     6→\n     7→This sheet contains the primary Site Plan for the Valley View Townhomes project (Sheet 9 of 39). It illustrates the overall site layout, including the arrangement of eight multi-family residential buildings, internal driveways, parking, a detention pond, pedestrian walkways, and retaining walls, while providing comprehensive tabular data to verify compliance with zoning, area, coverage, height, and parking requirements.\n     8→\n     9→**Key values:**\n    10→*   **Site Area:** 94,192 sf (2.162 acres)\n    11→*   **Zoning:** MF-2/Multi-Family Low Density\n    12→*   **Total Units:** 39 units (16 Two Bedroom, 23 Three Bedroom) across 8 buildings\n    13→*   **Maximum Building Height:** 40' allowed; 36' - 1\" is the highest proposed (Building 3)\n    14→*   **Impervious Cover:** 59% proposed (55,502 sf) vs 60% allowable\n    15→*   **Building Coverage:** 34% proposed (32,296 sf) vs 50% allowable\n    16→*   **Gross Floor Area:** 83,986 sf\n    17→*   **Vehicle Parking:** 88 total spaces provided (10 surface, 78 garage)\n    18→*   **Bicycle Parking:** 5 required; 41 provided (39 long term, 2 short term)\n    19→*   **Accessibility Slopes:** Max parking slope 1:50; Max cross-slope 1:50; Max ramp slope 1:12\n    20→*   **Benchmarks (NAVD 88):** BM #1 = 678.52'; BM #2 = 681.08'\n    21→\n    22→**Content blocks on this sheet:**\n    23→\n    24→*   **Block 1: drawing — Main Site Plan**\n    25→    A comprehensive layout drawing of the property. Use VISION to examine the spatial layout of Buildings 1-8, the routing of internal driveways and concrete/decomposed granite walkways, the location of the biofiltration/detention pond in the northeast corner, and the placement of retaining walls around the site perimeter.\n    26→\n    27→*   **Block 16: table — Site Data Table**\n    28→    A summary table of overall site metrics. READ the block content for exact values verifying zoning compliance, including site area, existing vs. proposed impervious cover percentages, allowable vs. proposed building coverage, and gross floor area.\n    29→\n    30→*   **Block 14: table — Building Data Table**\n    31→    A breakdown of metrics per building. READ the block content for individual building types (4-, 5-, or 6-plexes), gross floor areas, building footprints, bedroom configurations, and total unit counts (39 total, maximum 3 stories).\n    32→\n    33→*   **Block 15: table — Building Height Table**\n    34→    A summary of building heights for compliance checking. READ the block content for the average MSL, physical building heights (ranging from 33'-4.75\" to 36'-1\"), and verification that all buildings fall under the 40' allowable height limit.\n    35→\n    36→*   **Block 17: table — Site Area Calculation (MF-2)**\n    37→    A calculation of required area based on unit types. READ the block content to verify that the 94,192 sf provided site area satisfies the 93,600 sf required for the 39 2+ bedroom units.\n    38→\n    39→*   **Block 8: notes — Parking Data**\n    40→    A tabular summary of parking requirements. READ the block content for the breakdown of vehicle parking (surface vs. garage) and the exact counts for short-term and long-term bicycle parking spaces.\n    41→\n    42→*   **Block 10: notes — Site Plan Release Notes**\n    43→    A list of administrative conditions for the site plan. READ the block content for compliance requirements regarding standard building codes, signage, utility providers, demolition, and right-of-way excavation permits.\n    44→\n    45→*   **Block 4: notes — Accessibility Notes**\n    46→    Design constraints for ADA compliance. READ the block content for specific, mandated slope tolerances for accessible parking spaces, cross-slopes, and ramps (e.g., max ramp slope of 1:12).\n    47→\n    48→*   **Block 2: drawing — Lighting Note & Figure 34**\n    49→    Requirements for exterior lighting. READ for the requirement that all exterior lighting must be full cut-off and fully shielded per Subchapter E 2.5. Use VISION to review the four acceptable fixture profiles illustrated in Figure 34.\n    50→\n    51→*   **Block 6: notes — Fence Note**\n    52→    Tree protection requirements. READ the block content for instructions mandating hand-digging of post holes within Critical Root Zones (CRZ) and the required application of 3-inch hardwood mulch.\n    53→\n    54→*   **Block 9: notes — Trash Collection Notes**\n    55→    Rules for waste management. READ the block content for curbside unattended container restrictions and necessary enforcement signage requirements.\n    56→\n    57→*   **Blocks 3, 5, 7, 11, 12, 13: various — Administrative & Boilerplate Data**\n    58→    Standard site plan identifiers and administrative data. READ for the legal description (Block 3), the specific benchmark elevations (Block 5), and general utility liability notes (Block 7). Use VISION to locate the graphic scale showing 1\" = 20' (Block 11), the Texas 811 call-before-you-dig logo (Block 12), and the engineer's seal dated 2/27/26 (Block 13).\n    59→\n    60→---\n    61→\n    62→All other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n    63→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e6519561-0ed8-4293-aa56-db64026a5d93","uuid":"d58b8e99-280b-45f3-85d9-3d9ff7379b90","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/vercel/sandbox/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-09/guide.md","content":"# Sheet 9 — Site Plan\n\nDetailed site plan layout with associated building and parking data.\n\n## Reading Guide\n\nThis sheet contains the primary Site Plan for the Valley View Townhomes project (Sheet 9 of 39). It illustrates the overall site layout, including the arrangement of eight multi-family residential buildings, internal driveways, parking, a detention pond, pedestrian walkways, and retaining walls, while providing comprehensive tabular data to verify compliance with zoning, area, coverage, height, and parking requirements.\n\n**Key values:**\n*   **Site Area:** 94,192 sf (2.162 acres)\n*   **Zoning:** MF-2/Multi-Family Low Density\n*   **Total Units:** 39 units (16 Two Bedroom, 23 Three Bedroom) across 8 buildings\n*   **Maximum Building Height:** 40' allowed; 36' - 1\" is the highest proposed (Building 3)\n*   **Impervious Cover:** 59% proposed (55,502 sf) vs 60% allowable\n*   **Building Coverage:** 34% proposed (32,296 sf) vs 50% allowable\n*   **Gross Floor Area:** 83,986 sf\n*   **Vehicle Parking:** 88 total spaces provided (10 surface, 78 garage)\n*   **Bicycle Parking:** 5 required; 41 provided (39 long term, 2 short term)\n*   **Accessibility Slopes:** Max parking slope 1:50; Max cross-slope 1:50; Max ramp slope 1:12\n*   **Benchmarks (NAVD 88):** BM #1 = 678.52'; BM #2 = 681.08'\n\n**Content blocks on this sheet:**\n\n*   **Block 1: drawing — Main Site Plan**\n    A comprehensive layout drawing of the property. Use VISION to examine the spatial layout of Buildings 1-8, the routing of internal driveways and concrete/decomposed granite walkways, the location of the biofiltration/detention pond in the northeast corner, and the placement of retaining walls around the site perimeter.\n\n*   **Block 16: table — Site Data Table**\n    A summary table of overall site metrics. READ the block content for exact values verifying zoning compliance, including site area, existing vs. proposed impervious cover percentages, allowable vs. proposed building coverage, and gross floor area.\n\n*   **Block 14: table — Building Data Table**\n    A breakdown of metrics per building. READ the block content for individual building types (4-, 5-, or 6-plexes), gross floor areas, building footprints, bedroom configurations, and total unit counts (39 total, maximum 3 stories).\n\n*   **Block 15: table — Building Height Table**\n    A summary of building heights for compliance checking. READ the block content for the average MSL, physical building heights (ranging from 33'-4.75\" to 36'-1\"), and verification that all buildings fall under the 40' allowable height limit.\n\n*   **Block 17: table — Site Area Calculation (MF-2)**\n    A calculation of required area based on unit types. READ the block content to verify that the 94,192 sf provided site area satisfies the 93,600 sf required for the 39 2+ bedroom units.\n\n*   **Block 8: notes — Parking Data**\n    A tabular summary of parking requirements. READ the block content for the breakdown of vehicle parking (surface vs. garage) and the exact counts for short-term and long-term bicycle parking spaces.\n\n*   **Block 10: notes — Site Plan Release Notes**\n    A list of administrative conditions for the site plan. READ the block content for compliance requirements regarding standard building codes, signage, utility providers, demolition, and right-of-way excavation permits.\n\n*   **Block 4: notes — Accessibility Notes**\n    Design constraints for ADA compliance. READ the block content for specific, mandated slope tolerances for accessible parking spaces, cross-slopes, and ramps (e.g., max ramp slope of 1:12).\n\n*   **Block 2: drawing — Lighting Note & Figure 34**\n    Requirements for exterior lighting. READ for the requirement that all exterior lighting must be full cut-off and fully shielded per Subchapter E 2.5. Use VISION to review the four acceptable fixture profiles illustrated in Figure 34.\n\n*   **Block 6: notes — Fence Note**\n    Tree protection requirements. READ the block content for instructions mandating hand-digging of post holes within Critical Root Zones (CRZ) and the required application of 3-inch hardwood mulch.\n\n*   **Block 9: notes — Trash Collection Notes**\n    Rules for waste management. READ the block content for curbside unattended container restrictions and necessary enforcement signage requirements.\n\n*   **Blocks 3, 5, 7, 11, 12, 13: various — Administrative & Boilerplate Data**\n    Standard site plan identifiers and administrative data. READ for the legal description (Block 3), the specific benchmark elevations (Block 5), and general utility liability notes (Block 7). Use VISION to locate the graphic scale showing 1\" = 20' (Block 11), the Texas 811 call-before-you-dig logo (Block 12), and the engineer's seal dated 2/27/26 (Block 13).\n\n---\n\nAll other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n","numLines":63,"startLine":1,"totalLines":63}}}
{"level":30,"time":1776973757895,"pid":123,"hostname":"844f2260-bff","step":"review-runs","item":"16.md","index":8,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HQBdsh3qT8rHw1EQfMj1Uv","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Sheet 3 — General Notes\n     2→\n     3→Comprehensive general notes, sequence of construction, and project legend.\n     4→\n     5→## Reading Guide\n     6→\n     7→This sheet provides a comprehensive collection of general notes, standard specifications, utility capacity approvals, and the site's legend for the Valley View Townhomes project. Its primary purpose is to establish project-wide regulatory constraints, outline the construction sequence, and document the City of Austin's confirmation of sufficient water and wastewater service.\n     8→\n     9→**Key values:**\n    10→*   Project Scope: 39 Condo Units, 28 Living Unit Equivalents (LUE), 3.59 Acres\n    11→*   Water Demand: 60 gpm (Estimated Peak Hour), requiring connection to existing 8-inch main\n    12→*   Fire Flow Requirement: 1,500 gpm\n    13→*   Wastewater Flow: 20 gpm (Estimated Peak Wet Weather), requiring connection to existing 8-inch gravity main\n    14→*   Benchmark 1 (Mag Nail in Asphalt): Elevation = 678.52' NAVD 88\n    15→*   Benchmark 2 (Mag Nail in Asphalt): Elevation = 681.08' NAVD 88\n    16→*   Fire Department Paving Requirement: 80,000 lb. live-vehicle load capability\n    17→*   Fire Apparatus Vertical Clearance: 14 feet\n    18→*   Fire Hydrant Placement: Center of 4-inch opening must be at least 18 inches above finished grade\n    19→*   Electric Transmission Clearances: No digging/grading/trees within 25 feet of transmission structures; 20-foot clearance for aerial equipment/staging\n    20→*   Transmission Easement Road Requirement: Must support a 46,000 lb. tandem axle\n    21→*   ROW Work Zone Peak Hours: 6:00 a.m. to 9:00 a.m. and 4:00 p.m. to 6:00 p.m.\n    22→*   ROW Violation Fee: $250 per specific violation type\n    23→\n    24→**Content blocks on this sheet:**\n    25→\n    26→*   **Blocks 12 & 15:** Austin Water \"Suitable and Sufficient Existing Service\" approval letters for water and wastewater. READ the block content for the approved project specifications, demand calculations, and the specific existing 8-inch mains designated for the tap.\n    27→*   **Block 17:** Benchmark data. READ for exact elevations and locations to be used as control points for the site.\n    28→*   **Block 19:** Sequence of Construction. READ the block content for the strict 13-step chronological order of operations, particularly regarding when erosion controls and pond grading must occur.\n    29→*   **Block 6:** Project Legend. READ for the text descriptions of utilities, and use VISION to familiarize yourself with the symbol shapes (e.g., property lines, utility lines, tree protection zones) to interpret subsequent plan sheets accurately.\n    30→*   **Block 9:** Fire Department requirements. READ for strict design constraints regarding emergency access, pavement load ratings, and fire hydrant placement.\n    31→*   **Block 16:** Electric Transmission Notes. READ for critical safety clearances, structural load requirements for roads in easements, and barricade rules required by Austin Energy.\n    32→*   **Block 7:** Right-of-Way Management Standard Notes. READ for traffic control rules, restricted working hours, and permit violation penalties.\n    33→*   **Block 8:** General Construction Notes and Developer Information. READ to identify the property owner (WM 41 Austin RE LLC) and general engineering responsibilities.\n    34→*   **Blocks 14 & 18:** Electric Notes and Austin Energy standard requirements. READ for tree pruning, easement access, and code compliance constraints.\n    35→*   **Block 11:** Site Plan Release Notes. READ for general City of Austin demolition and utility relocation policies. \n    36→*   **Block 20:** Legal Description. READ to verify the exact lot and subdivision references (Lot 1, Mecey Subdivision).\n    37→*   **Blocks 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 10, 13:** Various administrative and boilerplate content (Title block info, Engineer's seal, Texas 811 logo, ADA disclaimers). READ the block content briefly for project tracking metadata, otherwise these can be safely skipped.\n    38→\n    39→---\n    40→\n    41→- `block-6.md` — table: Legend for existing utility and feature symbols used on the site plan.\n    42→- `block-9.md` — text_block: Standard notes for managing construction within the Right-Of-Way, covering violations, permitting, t\n    43→- `block-10.md` — text_block: List of 13 steps detailing the construction sequence, from installing temporary erosion controls to \n    44→- `block-13.md` — text_block: List of 16 notes detailing restrictions and requirements for work near electric transmission lines a\n    45→- `block-14.md` — text_block: Copy of a letter from Austin Water confirming that the existing wastewater main has adequate capacit\n    46→- `block-16.md` — text_block: Copy of a letter from Austin Water confirming that the existing water main has adequate capacity for\n    47→- `block-17.md` — text_block: Additional notes outlining requirements from Austin Energy regarding easements, tree work, erosion c\n    48→- `block-19.md` — text_block: List of 5 notes regarding electric utilities, specifically referencing Austin Energy's requirements \n    49→\n    50→All other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n    51→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e6519561-0ed8-4293-aa56-db64026a5d93","uuid":"ed7c9bb5-7eba-4539-8a70-13c98c39c7ef","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":