{"level":30,"time":1776973760522,"pid":123,"hostname":"844f2260-bff","step":"review-runs","item":"16.md","index":2,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QEF8QRgTeDBtHkrFmF4Coh","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Sheet 9 — Site Plan\n     2→\n     3→Detailed site plan layout with associated building and parking data.\n     4→\n     5→## Reading Guide\n     6→\n     7→This sheet contains the primary Site Plan for the Valley View Townhomes project (Sheet 9 of 39). It illustrates the overall site layout, including the arrangement of eight multi-family residential buildings, internal driveways, parking, a detention pond, pedestrian walkways, and retaining walls, while providing comprehensive tabular data to verify compliance with zoning, area, coverage, height, and parking requirements.\n     8→\n     9→**Key values:**\n    10→*   **Site Area:** 94,192 sf (2.162 acres)\n    11→*   **Zoning:** MF-2/Multi-Family Low Density\n    12→*   **Total Units:** 39 units (16 Two Bedroom, 23 Three Bedroom) across 8 buildings\n    13→*   **Maximum Building Height:** 40' allowed; 36' - 1\" is the highest proposed (Building 3)\n    14→*   **Impervious Cover:** 59% proposed (55,502 sf) vs 60% allowable\n    15→*   **Building Coverage:** 34% proposed (32,296 sf) vs 50% allowable\n    16→*   **Gross Floor Area:** 83,986 sf\n    17→*   **Vehicle Parking:** 88 total spaces provided (10 surface, 78 garage)\n    18→*   **Bicycle Parking:** 5 required; 41 provided (39 long term, 2 short term)\n    19→*   **Accessibility Slopes:** Max parking slope 1:50; Max cross-slope 1:50; Max ramp slope 1:12\n    20→*   **Benchmarks (NAVD 88):** BM #1 = 678.52'; BM #2 = 681.08'\n    21→\n    22→**Content blocks on this sheet:**\n    23→\n    24→*   **Block 1: drawing — Main Site Plan**\n    25→    A comprehensive layout drawing of the property. Use VISION to examine the spatial layout of Buildings 1-8, the routing of internal driveways and concrete/decomposed granite walkways, the location of the biofiltration/detention pond in the northeast corner, and the placement of retaining walls around the site perimeter.\n    26→\n    27→*   **Block 16: table — Site Data Table**\n    28→    A summary table of overall site metrics. READ the block content for exact values verifying zoning compliance, including site area, existing vs. proposed impervious cover percentages, allowable vs. proposed building coverage, and gross floor area.\n    29→\n    30→*   **Block 14: table — Building Data Table**\n    31→    A breakdown of metrics per building. READ the block content for individual building types (4-, 5-, or 6-plexes), gross floor areas, building footprints, bedroom configurations, and total unit counts (39 total, maximum 3 stories).\n    32→\n    33→*   **Block 15: table — Building Height Table**\n    34→    A summary of building heights for compliance checking. READ the block content for the average MSL, physical building heights (ranging from 33'-4.75\" to 36'-1\"), and verification that all buildings fall under the 40' allowable height limit.\n    35→\n    36→*   **Block 17: table — Site Area Calculation (MF-2)**\n    37→    A calculation of required area based on unit types. READ the block content to verify that the 94,192 sf provided site area satisfies the 93,600 sf required for the 39 2+ bedroom units.\n    38→\n    39→*   **Block 8: notes — Parking Data**\n    40→    A tabular summary of parking requirements. READ the block content for the breakdown of vehicle parking (surface vs. garage) and the exact counts for short-term and long-term bicycle parking spaces.\n    41→\n    42→*   **Block 10: notes — Site Plan Release Notes**\n    43→    A list of administrative conditions for the site plan. READ the block content for compliance requirements regarding standard building codes, signage, utility providers, demolition, and right-of-way excavation permits.\n    44→\n    45→*   **Block 4: notes — Accessibility Notes**\n    46→    Design constraints for ADA compliance. READ the block content for specific, mandated slope tolerances for accessible parking spaces, cross-slopes, and ramps (e.g., max ramp slope of 1:12).\n    47→\n    48→*   **Block 2: drawing — Lighting Note & Figure 34**\n    49→    Requirements for exterior lighting. READ for the requirement that all exterior lighting must be full cut-off and fully shielded per Subchapter E 2.5. Use VISION to review the four acceptable fixture profiles illustrated in Figure 34.\n    50→\n    51→*   **Block 6: notes — Fence Note**\n    52→    Tree protection requirements. READ the block content for instructions mandating hand-digging of post holes within Critical Root Zones (CRZ) and the required application of 3-inch hardwood mulch.\n    53→\n    54→*   **Block 9: notes — Trash Collection Notes**\n    55→    Rules for waste management. READ the block content for curbside unattended container restrictions and necessary enforcement signage requirements.\n    56→\n    57→*   **Blocks 3, 5, 7, 11, 12, 13: various — Administrative & Boilerplate Data**\n    58→    Standard site plan identifiers and administrative data. READ for the legal description (Block 3), the specific benchmark elevations (Block 5), and general utility liability notes (Block 7). Use VISION to locate the graphic scale showing 1\" = 20' (Block 11), the Texas 811 call-before-you-dig logo (Block 12), and the engineer's seal dated 2/27/26 (Block 13).\n    59→\n    60→---\n    61→\n    62→All other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n    63→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"158c3787-95dd-4091-81cc-891db6165072","uuid":"b1d114b2-0d32-423f-81ea-ee6963f259aa","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/vercel/sandbox/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-09/guide.md","content":"# Sheet 9 — Site Plan\n\nDetailed site plan layout with associated building and parking data.\n\n## Reading Guide\n\nThis sheet contains the primary Site Plan for the Valley View Townhomes project (Sheet 9 of 39). It illustrates the overall site layout, including the arrangement of eight multi-family residential buildings, internal driveways, parking, a detention pond, pedestrian walkways, and retaining walls, while providing comprehensive tabular data to verify compliance with zoning, area, coverage, height, and parking requirements.\n\n**Key values:**\n*   **Site Area:** 94,192 sf (2.162 acres)\n*   **Zoning:** MF-2/Multi-Family Low Density\n*   **Total Units:** 39 units (16 Two Bedroom, 23 Three Bedroom) across 8 buildings\n*   **Maximum Building Height:** 40' allowed; 36' - 1\" is the highest proposed (Building 3)\n*   **Impervious Cover:** 59% proposed (55,502 sf) vs 60% allowable\n*   **Building Coverage:** 34% proposed (32,296 sf) vs 50% allowable\n*   **Gross Floor Area:** 83,986 sf\n*   **Vehicle Parking:** 88 total spaces provided (10 surface, 78 garage)\n*   **Bicycle Parking:** 5 required; 41 provided (39 long term, 2 short term)\n*   **Accessibility Slopes:** Max parking slope 1:50; Max cross-slope 1:50; Max ramp slope 1:12\n*   **Benchmarks (NAVD 88):** BM #1 = 678.52'; BM #2 = 681.08'\n\n**Content blocks on this sheet:**\n\n*   **Block 1: drawing — Main Site Plan**\n    A comprehensive layout drawing of the property. Use VISION to examine the spatial layout of Buildings 1-8, the routing of internal driveways and concrete/decomposed granite walkways, the location of the biofiltration/detention pond in the northeast corner, and the placement of retaining walls around the site perimeter.\n\n*   **Block 16: table — Site Data Table**\n    A summary table of overall site metrics. READ the block content for exact values verifying zoning compliance, including site area, existing vs. proposed impervious cover percentages, allowable vs. proposed building coverage, and gross floor area.\n\n*   **Block 14: table — Building Data Table**\n    A breakdown of metrics per building. READ the block content for individual building types (4-, 5-, or 6-plexes), gross floor areas, building footprints, bedroom configurations, and total unit counts (39 total, maximum 3 stories).\n\n*   **Block 15: table — Building Height Table**\n    A summary of building heights for compliance checking. READ the block content for the average MSL, physical building heights (ranging from 33'-4.75\" to 36'-1\"), and verification that all buildings fall under the 40' allowable height limit.\n\n*   **Block 17: table — Site Area Calculation (MF-2)**\n    A calculation of required area based on unit types. READ the block content to verify that the 94,192 sf provided site area satisfies the 93,600 sf required for the 39 2+ bedroom units.\n\n*   **Block 8: notes — Parking Data**\n    A tabular summary of parking requirements. READ the block content for the breakdown of vehicle parking (surface vs. garage) and the exact counts for short-term and long-term bicycle parking spaces.\n\n*   **Block 10: notes — Site Plan Release Notes**\n    A list of administrative conditions for the site plan. READ the block content for compliance requirements regarding standard building codes, signage, utility providers, demolition, and right-of-way excavation permits.\n\n*   **Block 4: notes — Accessibility Notes**\n    Design constraints for ADA compliance. READ the block content for specific, mandated slope tolerances for accessible parking spaces, cross-slopes, and ramps (e.g., max ramp slope of 1:12).\n\n*   **Block 2: drawing — Lighting Note & Figure 34**\n    Requirements for exterior lighting. READ for the requirement that all exterior lighting must be full cut-off and fully shielded per Subchapter E 2.5. Use VISION to review the four acceptable fixture profiles illustrated in Figure 34.\n\n*   **Block 6: notes — Fence Note**\n    Tree protection requirements. READ the block content for instructions mandating hand-digging of post holes within Critical Root Zones (CRZ) and the required application of 3-inch hardwood mulch.\n\n*   **Block 9: notes — Trash Collection Notes**\n    Rules for waste management. READ the block content for curbside unattended container restrictions and necessary enforcement signage requirements.\n\n*   **Blocks 3, 5, 7, 11, 12, 13: various — Administrative & Boilerplate Data**\n    Standard site plan identifiers and administrative data. READ for the legal description (Block 3), the specific benchmark elevations (Block 5), and general utility liability notes (Block 7). Use VISION to locate the graphic scale showing 1\" = 20' (Block 11), the Texas 811 call-before-you-dig logo (Block 12), and the engineer's seal dated 2/27/26 (Block 13).\n\n---\n\nAll other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n","numLines":63,"startLine":1,"totalLines":63}}}
{"level":30,"time":1776973760523,"pid":123,"hostname":"844f2260-bff","step":"review-runs","item":"16.md","index":2,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MzhcwrUqcFCPPNQR6gL9BW","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Sheet 31 — Landscape Plan\n     2→\n     3→Landscape design plan featuring planting details and irrigation notes.\n     4→\n     5→## Reading Guide\n     6→\n     7→This sheet presents the Landscape Plan for the Valley View Townhomes project, detailing the layout of plantings, open spaces, hardscape features, and site contours. It serves as the primary reference for landscape grading, planting mitigation requirements, and automatic irrigation system specifications.\n     8→\n     9→**Key values:**\n    10→*   **Drawing Scale:** 1\" = 20'-0\"\n    11→*   **Topsoil Placement Depth:** Finished elevation for parking lot islands and similar areas must be at least 6 inches below the finished parking lot/curb elevation.\n    12→*   **Irrigation Spray Limits:** No spray irrigation is permitted on areas less than 10 feet wide (e.g., medians, buffer strips).\n    13→*   **Irrigation Setbacks:** Above-ground irrigation emission devices must be set back at least 6 inches from impervious surfaces.\n    14→*   **Rain Shut-off Threshold:** Automatic rain shut-off devices must trigger after more than 1/2 inch (0.5\") of rainfall.\n    15→*   **Tree Mitigation Size:** Street yard and parking lot trees exceeding 1.5 caliper inches count towards mitigation.\n    16→*   **Site Elevations:** Topographic contour lines indicate site elevations ranging generally from approximately 660 to 690 feet.\n    17→\n    18→**Content blocks on this sheet:**\n    19→\n    20→*   **Block 2: drawing — Main Landscape and Site Plan**\n    21→    A comprehensive site plan illustrating building footprints, parking layouts, sidewalks, utility lines (Water, Storm Drain, Overhead Electric), topographical contours, and the distribution of landscape elements.\n    22→    *Use VISION to examine* the spatial layout of the site, locate specific landscape zones (using H-series key notes), trace contour grading, and identify the placement of mitigation trees.\n    23→\n    24→*   **Block 5: notes — Key Notes & Legend**\n    25→    Defines the hatch patterns and symbols used in the main drawing, including paving (H.1), street yards (H.2, H.3), parking lot landscaping (H.4), common open space (H.5), wooden privacy fences (H.6), and sod (H.7). It also defines abbreviations for tree types (SY, PL, P, M).\n    26→    *READ the block content for* exact definitions of hatch patterns, symbols, and mitigation tree sizing requirements (>1.5 cal. inch) to accurately interpret the main drawing.\n    27→\n    28→*   **Block 3: notes — Irrigation Notes**\n    29→    Technical specifications ensuring the automatic irrigation system complies with TCEQ Chapter 344. It covers hardware requirements (master valves, rain shut-offs), spatial constraints, and deliverables required from the installer (as-built plans, water budgets).\n    30→    *READ the block content for* specific compliance metrics, installation constraints, and administrative requirements for final plumbing inspection.\n    31→\n    32→*   **Block 4: notes — General Landscape Notes**\n    33→    Specific grading and soil requirements for landscaped areas adjacent to paving, detailing the necessary finished elevation offsets to accommodate topsoil placement. Also provides guidance on drought variance procedures.\n    34→    *READ the block content for* exact grading dimensions (6 inches below finished elevation) and supplemental irrigation requirements.\n    35→\n    36→*   **Block 1: diagram — Scale and Orientation**\n    37→    Provides the graphical scale and North arrow for the main drawing.\n    38→    *READ the block content for* the exact scale (1\" = 20'-0\") and *Use VISION to* orient the site layout.\n    39→\n    40→*   **Blocks 6, 7, 8, 9: various — Boilerplate & Administrative**\n    41→    Contains the title block information, including the project name (Valley View Townhomes), location (3759 Valley View Road, Austin, TX), property owner (WM 41 Austin RE, LLC), and the licensed landscape architect's professional seal (dated 02/13/2026).\n    42→    *READ the block content for* general project context, property address, and professional certification details.\n    43→\n    44→---\n    45→\n    46→- `block-3.md` — notes: Irrigation notes detailing requirements for automatic irrigation systems to comply with TCEQ Chapter\n    47→\n    48→All other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n    49→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"158c3787-95dd-4091-81cc-891db6165072","uuid":"83937955-bf3b-4d7d-a549-3bfd4155d306","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/vercel/sandbox/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-31/guide.md","content":"# Sheet 31 — Landscape Plan\n\nLandscape design plan featuring planting details and irrigation notes.\n\n## Reading Guide\n\nThis sheet presents the Landscape Plan for the Valley View Townhomes project, detailing the layout of plantings, open spaces, hardscape features, and site contours. It serves as the primary reference for landscape grading, planting mitigation requirements, and automatic irrigation system specifications.\n\n**Key values:**\n*   **Drawing Scale:** 1\" = 20'-0\"\n*   **Topsoil Placement Depth:** Finished elevation for parking lot islands and similar areas must be at least 6 inches below the finished parking lot/curb elevation.\n*   **Irrigation Spray Limits:** No spray irrigation is permitted on areas less than 10 feet wide (e.g., medians, buffer strips).\n*   **Irrigation Setbacks:** Above-ground irrigation emission devices must be set back at least 6 inches from impervious surfaces.\n*   **Rain Shut-off Threshold:** Automatic rain shut-off devices must trigger after more than 1/2 inch (0.5\") of rainfall.\n*   **Tree Mitigation Size:** Street yard and parking lot trees exceeding 1.5 caliper inches count towards mitigation.\n*   **Site Elevations:** Topographic contour lines indicate site elevations ranging generally from approximately 660 to 690 feet.\n\n**Content blocks on this sheet:**\n\n*   **Block 2: drawing — Main Landscape and Site Plan**\n    A comprehensive site plan illustrating building footprints, parking layouts, sidewalks, utility lines (Water, Storm Drain, Overhead Electric), topographical contours, and the distribution of landscape elements.\n    *Use VISION to examine* the spatial layout of the site, locate specific landscape zones (using H-series key notes), trace contour grading, and identify the placement of mitigation trees.\n\n*   **Block 5: notes — Key Notes & Legend**\n    Defines the hatch patterns and symbols used in the main drawing, including paving (H.1), street yards (H.2, H.3), parking lot landscaping (H.4), common open space (H.5), wooden privacy fences (H.6), and sod (H.7). It also defines abbreviations for tree types (SY, PL, P, M).\n    *READ the block content for* exact definitions of hatch patterns, symbols, and mitigation tree sizing requirements (>1.5 cal. inch) to accurately interpret the main drawing.\n\n*   **Block 3: notes — Irrigation Notes**\n    Technical specifications ensuring the automatic irrigation system complies with TCEQ Chapter 344. It covers hardware requirements (master valves, rain shut-offs), spatial constraints, and deliverables required from the installer (as-built plans, water budgets).\n    *READ the block content for* specific compliance metrics, installation constraints, and administrative requirements for final plumbing inspection.\n\n*   **Block 4: notes — General Landscape Notes**\n    Specific grading and soil requirements for landscaped areas adjacent to paving, detailing the necessary finished elevation offsets to accommodate topsoil placement. Also provides guidance on drought variance procedures.\n    *READ the block content for* exact grading dimensions (6 inches below finished elevation) and supplemental irrigation requirements.\n\n*   **Block 1: diagram — Scale and Orientation**\n    Provides the graphical scale and North arrow for the main drawing.\n    *READ the block content for* the exact scale (1\" = 20'-0\") and *Use VISION to* orient the site layout.\n\n*   **Blocks 6, 7, 8, 9: various — Boilerplate & Administrative**\n    Contains the title block information, including the project name (Valley View Townhomes), location (3759 Valley View Road, Austin, TX), property owner (WM 41 Austin RE, LLC), and the licensed landscape architect's professional seal (dated 02/13/2026).\n    *READ the block content for* general project context, property address, and professional certification details.\n\n---\n\n- `block-3.md` — notes: Irrigation notes detailing requirements for automatic irrigation systems to comply with TCEQ Chapter\n\nAll other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n","numLines":49,"startLine":1,"totalLines":49}}}
{"level":30,"time":1776973760525,"pid":123,"hostname":"844f2260-bff","step":"review-runs","item":"16.md","index":2,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014SMybMCPsxkoLZ8Zdaz57b","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Sheet 1 — Cover\n     2→\n     3→Cover sheet containing project details, location map, and sheet index.\n     4→\n     5→## Reading Guide\n     6→\n     7→This is the cover sheet for the Valley View Townhomes site plan (SP-2025-0126C). It serves as the primary reference document for the project, containing the sheet index, site development data, fire department requirements, a location map, and required municipal compliance notes.\n     8→\n     9→**Key values:**\n    10→*   Project Area: 2.16 Acres\n    11→*   Limits of Construction: 2.26 Acres\n    12→*   Total Residential Units: 39 units\n    13→*   Total Plan Sheets: 39 sheets\n    14→*   Fire Flow Demand (@ 20 psi): 3000 GPM (Reduced to 1500 GPM with sprinkler system)\n    15→*   Building Fire Area: 13,344 s.f.\n    16→*   Occupancy Classification: R3\n    17→*   Construction Classification: Type V-B\n    18→*   Sprinkler System Type: NFPA 13D\n    19→*   Private Hydrants: 1\n    20→*   Mapsco / City of Austin Grid: #614S / #G19\n    21→\n    22→**Content blocks on this sheet:**\n    23→\n    24→*   **Block 15:** text_block — Project title, address (3759 Valley View Road), and permit number (SP-2025-0126C). READ for core project identification.\n    25→*   **Block 4:** table — Site Development Data. READ for project team contact information, legal description, and exact acreage values. \n    26→*   **Block 6:** table — Sheet List Table. READ to understand the structure of the 39-page drawing set and locate specific disciplines (grading, drainage, landscaping, etc.).\n    27→*   **Block 7:** table — Austin Fire Department requirements. READ for specific fire design codes, fire flow demands (in GPM), and building classification data.\n    28→*   **Blocks 1 & 30:** drawing & text_block — Project Location Map and associated scale/coordinate data. VISION for the spatial layout of the site relative to major cross streets (Manchaca, Clawson Rd, 290); READ Block 30 for Mapsco #614S and Grid #G19.\n    29→*   **Blocks 8 & 31:** text_block — Environmental status notes. READ to confirm the site is in the West Bouldin Creek Watershed, is outside the 100-year floodplain, and is not in the Edwards Aquifer zone.\n    30→*   **Blocks 16, 17, 25, 26, 27:** various — Project-specific requirements and waivers. READ for specific stipulations including private hydrant maintenance (Block 16), private biofiltration pond maintenance (Block 17), parkland dedication fees for 39 units (Block 25), a specific DCM waiver (Block 26), and Traffic Control Plan requirements (Block 27).\n    31→*   **Block 5:** table — Revisions/Corrections. READ to confirm no revisions have been logged yet.\n    32→*   **Blocks 2, 3, 9-14, 18-24, 28-29, 32, 33:** various — Boilerplate, Administrative Notes, and Seals. READ selectively if reviewing general contractor responsibilities, standard city ordinances (lead-free water, recycling, USTs), engineer certifications, liability disclaimers, or standard erosion control notes. Includes empty approval stamps and review tables.\n    33→\n    34→---\n    35→\n    36→All other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n    37→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"158c3787-95dd-4091-81cc-891db6165072","uuid":"5c745ef6-d0f4-46c4-9e23-b64746e3b3f9","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/vercel/sandbox/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-01/guide.md","content":"# Sheet 1 — Cover\n\nCover sheet containing project details, location map, and sheet index.\n\n## Reading Guide\n\nThis is the cover sheet for the Valley View Townhomes site plan (SP-2025-0126C). It serves as the primary reference document for the project, containing the sheet index, site development data, fire department requirements, a location map, and required municipal compliance notes.\n\n**Key values:**\n*   Project Area: 2.16 Acres\n*   Limits of Construction: 2.26 Acres\n*   Total Residential Units: 39 units\n*   Total Plan Sheets: 39 sheets\n*   Fire Flow Demand (@ 20 psi): 3000 GPM (Reduced to 1500 GPM with sprinkler system)\n*   Building Fire Area: 13,344 s.f.\n*   Occupancy Classification: R3\n*   Construction Classification: Type V-B\n*   Sprinkler System Type: NFPA 13D\n*   Private Hydrants: 1\n*   Mapsco / City of Austin Grid: #614S / #G19\n\n**Content blocks on this sheet:**\n\n*   **Block 15:** text_block — Project title, address (3759 Valley View Road), and permit number (SP-2025-0126C). READ for core project identification.\n*   **Block 4:** table — Site Development Data. READ for project team contact information, legal description, and exact acreage values. \n*   **Block 6:** table — Sheet List Table. READ to understand the structure of the 39-page drawing set and locate specific disciplines (grading, drainage, landscaping, etc.).\n*   **Block 7:** table — Austin Fire Department requirements. READ for specific fire design codes, fire flow demands (in GPM), and building classification data.\n*   **Blocks 1 & 30:** drawing & text_block — Project Location Map and associated scale/coordinate data. VISION for the spatial layout of the site relative to major cross streets (Manchaca, Clawson Rd, 290); READ Block 30 for Mapsco #614S and Grid #G19.\n*   **Blocks 8 & 31:** text_block — Environmental status notes. READ to confirm the site is in the West Bouldin Creek Watershed, is outside the 100-year floodplain, and is not in the Edwards Aquifer zone.\n*   **Blocks 16, 17, 25, 26, 27:** various — Project-specific requirements and waivers. READ for specific stipulations including private hydrant maintenance (Block 16), private biofiltration pond maintenance (Block 17), parkland dedication fees for 39 units (Block 25), a specific DCM waiver (Block 26), and Traffic Control Plan requirements (Block 27).\n*   **Block 5:** table — Revisions/Corrections. READ to confirm no revisions have been logged yet.\n*   **Blocks 2, 3, 9-14, 18-24, 28-29, 32, 33:** various — Boilerplate, Administrative Notes, and Seals. READ selectively if reviewing general contractor responsibilities, standard city ordinances (lead-free water, recycling, USTs), engineer certifications, liability disclaimers, or standard erosion control notes. Includes empty approval stamps and review tables.\n\n---\n\nAll other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n","numLines":37,"startLine":1,"totalLines":37}}}
{"level":30,"time":1776973760608,"pid":123,"hostname":"844f2260-bff","step":"review-runs","item":"15.md","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01QrUUMsrcqemLyWcYJqFTUP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01HSVZAH9CeYzyFQx7rEdi6Z","name":"mcp__conductor_tools__vision","input":{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":9,"prompt":"Examine the site plan drawing carefully. Look for and describe:\n\n1. Any labeled setback lines on the property boundaries (such as \"Building Setback Line,\" \"Front Setback,\" \"Rear Setback,\" \"Side Setback,\" \"Compatibility Buffer,\" or similar labels)\n2. Dimensions or measurements associated with any setback lines visible on the drawing\n3. Any buffer zones or compatibility buffer areas shown with hatching, shading, or labels\n4. The property lines and their proximity to buildings or structures\n5. Any reference callouts or notes pointing to setback requirements\n6. Location of all 8 buildings relative to property boundaries\n\nProvide specific details about what is and is not shown for setback compliance documentation."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":13,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6615,"cache_read_input_tokens":51189,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":6615,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"33f519bd-bced-4a7a-aae5-831dbf134acc","uuid":"fe59bcf7-4288-4382-a7bc-9ce3344b275b"}
{"level":30,"time":1776973760762,"pid":123,"hostname":"844f2260-bff","step":"review-runs","item":"15.md","index":9,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01RR9vVoUu4kTDgzNx7XNnru","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good information. From the blocks I can see that:\n\nSheet 1 (Cover sheet):\n- AFD Fire Pipeline Ordinance: \"No\" - so hazardous pipeline is NOT applicable\n- Site plan notes reference \"West Bouldin Creek Watershed\"\n- No elevation certificate mentioned\n- All standard cover sheet info\n\nSheet 9 (Site Plan):\n- Shows the main site plan with buildings, driveways, parking, detention pond, etc.\n- Has a scale of 1\" = 20'\n- Building heights are all under 40 ft (max is 36'-1\" for Building 3)\n- Shows zoning as MF-2\n- Shows parking, parking data, accessibility notes\n- I can see Block 2 mentions \"showing layout of buildings... utility lines, easements, existing trees, retaining walls, and surrounding properties\"\n- But I don't see specific mention of setback lines being drawn and labeled\n\nI need to check:\n1. Whether zoning setback lines are shown\n2. Whether compatibility buffer/setback lines are shown (since SF-3 adjacent property triggers Article 10)\n3. Whether a separate compatibility exhibit is provided\n4. Whether cross-sections are provided showing distances and heights\n\nLet me check the landscape plan (Sheet 31) to see if compatibility buffer information is there.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3716,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3117,"cache_read_input_tokens":49558,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3117,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d203a61d-b956-4bf7-a62f-71a0e7d71a2a","uuid":"60fda4a1-df31-4028-b1f2-7089b4b562b6"}
