{"level":30,"time":1776973762680,"pid":123,"hostname":"844f2260-bff","step":"review-runs","item":"32.md","index":4,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017TpxNpEzhf8y3svW6KvLkM","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# General Information and Applicable Codes\n     2→\n     3→*This section identifies the project location, legal description, and establishes that the current Land Development Code applies to the project.*\n     4→\n     5→![City of Austin Development Services Department Logo]\n     6→# Project Review Form (PRF)\n     7→## Statement of Applicable Codes\n     8→*This completed form must accompany all applications for site plan or subdivisions*\n     9→\n    10→DevelopmentATX.com | Phone: 311 (or 512-974-2000 outside Austin)\n    11→For submittal and fee information, see austintexas.gov/digitaldevelopment\n    12→\n    13→**For Office Use Only — See Vested Rights Determination (if applicable) for additional information**\n    14→File # Assigned: ___________________ Date Filed: _______________ Original Application Vesting Date: _______________\n    15→Signature: _______________________________ Date: _______________\n    16→Director’s Determination of Vested Rights (select one): [ ] Not Applicable [ ] Approved [ ] Denied\n    17→\n    18→Proposed Project Name: Valley View Townhomes\n    19→Address/Location: 3759 Valley View Road, Austin TX 78704\n    20→Legal Description: LOT 1 MECEY SUBD, V.72, P.6\n    21→\n    22→[X] A. **Current Land Development Code.** Application is subject to generally applicable land use and development regulations established in the current Land Development Code (Title 25/30), including any applicable zoning overlays, conditions and administrative rules.\n    23→*** NOTE: If \"A\" is checked above, proceed to the signature block at the bottom.\n    24→\n    25→[ ] B. **Special Council-Approved Ordinance or Development Agreement.** Application is subject to regulations included in a Council-approved ordinance or development agreement, such as a Planned Unit Development (PUD), Planned Development Agreement (PDA), regulating plan, or other ordinance specific to the property or areas covered by the ordinance. Applicable regulations are as specified in the ordinance or development agreement.\n    26→\n    27→[ ] C. **Vested Rights Claimed.** Application is subject to a version of the Land Development Code, or other applicable development regulations, in effect prior to the date of the application based on a claim of vested rights under state law. This includes rights asserted under Chapter 245 of the Texas Local Government Code or a Council-approved settlement agreement resolving litigation.\n    28→***NOTE: If \"C\" is checked, complete the \"Information Required for Vested Rights Review\" below, and attach a Vested Rights Petition that provides additional information and more fully describes the basis for the claim.\n    29→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4e7b1c1f-9804-4a61-b82e-41dbab740236","uuid":"1381fb8d-9062-4435-89cf-635144e7de93","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/vercel/sandbox/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/supplementary-docs/project-review-form/01-general-information-and-applicable-codes.md","content":"# General Information and Applicable Codes\n\n*This section identifies the project location, legal description, and establishes that the current Land Development Code applies to the project.*\n\n![City of Austin Development Services Department Logo]\n# Project Review Form (PRF)\n## Statement of Applicable Codes\n*This completed form must accompany all applications for site plan or subdivisions*\n\nDevelopmentATX.com | Phone: 311 (or 512-974-2000 outside Austin)\nFor submittal and fee information, see austintexas.gov/digitaldevelopment\n\n**For Office Use Only — See Vested Rights Determination (if applicable) for additional information**\nFile # Assigned: ___________________ Date Filed: _______________ Original Application Vesting Date: _______________\nSignature: _______________________________ Date: _______________\nDirector’s Determination of Vested Rights (select one): [ ] Not Applicable [ ] Approved [ ] Denied\n\nProposed Project Name: Valley View Townhomes\nAddress/Location: 3759 Valley View Road, Austin TX 78704\nLegal Description: LOT 1 MECEY SUBD, V.72, P.6\n\n[X] A. **Current Land Development Code.** Application is subject to generally applicable land use and development regulations established in the current Land Development Code (Title 25/30), including any applicable zoning overlays, conditions and administrative rules.\n*** NOTE: If \"A\" is checked above, proceed to the signature block at the bottom.\n\n[ ] B. **Special Council-Approved Ordinance or Development Agreement.** Application is subject to regulations included in a Council-approved ordinance or development agreement, such as a Planned Unit Development (PUD), Planned Development Agreement (PDA), regulating plan, or other ordinance specific to the property or areas covered by the ordinance. Applicable regulations are as specified in the ordinance or development agreement.\n\n[ ] C. **Vested Rights Claimed.** Application is subject to a version of the Land Development Code, or other applicable development regulations, in effect prior to the date of the application based on a claim of vested rights under state law. This includes rights asserted under Chapter 245 of the Texas Local Government Code or a Council-approved settlement agreement resolving litigation.\n***NOTE: If \"C\" is checked, complete the \"Information Required for Vested Rights Review\" below, and attach a Vested Rights Petition that provides additional information and more fully describes the basis for the claim.\n","numLines":29,"startLine":1,"totalLines":29}}}
{"level":30,"time":1776973762682,"pid":123,"hostname":"844f2260-bff","step":"review-runs","item":"32.md","index":4,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WhZE1TfEdWTHVNXwcE4u1V","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Sheet 1 — Content Blocks\n     2→\n     3→## Block 1: drawing — This block shows a map of the project location, highlighting the surrounding streets and intersection. A pointer indicates the specific project location.\n     4→\n     5→[Map showing the project location and surrounding streets.]\n     6→\n     7→N\n     8→\n     9→PROJECT\n    10→LOCATION\n    11→\n    12→## Block 5: table — This block contains data related to the Austin Fire Department's requirements for the project. It includes information such as fire design codes, fire flow demand, occupancy classification, construction classification, building fire area, automatic fire sprinkler system type, reduced fire flow demand, applies to project status, AFD fire hydrant flow test dates and locations, city of Austin pipeline ordinance compliance, high-rise status, international wildland-urban interface code compliance, and alternative method of compliance AMOC.\n    13→\n    14→Austin Fire Department\n    15→\n    16→| Fire Design Codes | 2021 International Fire Code Edition\n    17→with City of Austin Local Amendments |\n    18→|---|---|\n    19→| Fire Flow Demand @ 20 psi\n    20→(gpm) | 3000 GPM |\n    21→| Occupancy Classification | R3 |\n    22→| Construction Classification | Type V-B |\n    23→| Building Fire Area (s.f.) | 13,344 |\n    24→| Automatic Fire Sprinkler System\n    25→Type (If applicable) | NFPA 13D |\n    26→| Reduced Fire Flow Demand @ 20\n    27→psi for having a sprinkler system\n    28→(gpm) | 1500 GPM |\n    29→| AFD Fire Hydrant Flow Test Date | 3/21/2025 |\n    30→| AFD Fire Hydrant Flow Test\n    31→Location | 3700 Valley View Rd. |\n    32→| City of Austin Pipeline Ordinance\n    33→Applies to Project | No |\n    34→| High-Rise | No |\n    35→| International Wildland-Urban\n    36→Interface Code | N/A |\n    37→| Alternative Method of\n    38→Compliance AMOC (If applicable) | N/A |\n    39→\n    40→## Block 6: table — This block contains the site development data for the Valley View Townhomes project. It includes contact information for the owner, engineer, architect, and landscape architect, as well as the legal description, subdivision file number, zoning case number, and limits of construction.\n    41→\n    42→Site Development Data Valley View Townhomes\n    43→Owner: WM 41 Austin RE, LLC.\n    44→Contact Person: Richard D. Agnew\n    45→500 West 5th Street, Ste. 1010\n    46→Austin, Texas 78701\n    47→Phone: 512-565-6159\n    48→Email: Richard.Agnew@slpops.com\n    49→\n    50→Engineer: Bleyl Engineering\n    51→Contact Person: Jason Rodgers\n    52→7701 San Felipe, Suite 200\n    53→Austin, Texas 78729\n    54→Phone: (512) 454-2400\n    55→Email: jrodgers@bleylengineering.com\n    56→\n    57→Architect: Danze & Davis Architects, Inc.\n    58→Contact Person: Harrison Davis\n    59→4701 Spicewood Springs Rd, Ste 200\n    60→Austin, Texas 78759\n    61→Phone: (512) 343-0714\n    62→\n    63→Landscape Architect: Blu Fish Collaborative, Inc.\n    64→Contact Person: Mike Fishbaugh\n    65→3607 S. Lamar Blvd., Suite 104\n    66→Austin, Texas 78704\n    67→Phone: (512) 338-4115\n    68→\n    69→Legal Description: Lot 1 Mecey Subdivision, Volume 73, Page 76, Plat Records of Travis County,\n    70→Texas\n    71→2.16 Acres\n    72→Subdivision File No. C8S-75-160\n    73→Zoning Case No. C14-2011-0093\n    74→Limits of Construction: 2.26 Acres\n    75→\n    76→## Block 8: text_block — This block is the title and primary identification information for the site plan. It states the project name, address, jurisdiction, SP number, and submittal date.\n    77→\n    78→Site Plan\n    79→Valley View Townhomes\n    80→3759 Valley View Road\n    81→Austin, Texas 78704\n    82→Jurisdiction: Austin Full Purpose\n    83→\n    84→SP-2025-0126C\n    85→Submittal Date: May 20, 2025\n    86→\n    87→## Block 9: text_block — This block is a disclaimer from Bleyl Engineering stating that they are not responsible for the accuracy of the survey or design errors resulting from survey inaccuracies.\n    88→\n    89→Bleyl Engineering and its associates will not be held responsible for the accuracy of the survey or for design errors or\n    90→omissions resulting from survey inaccuracies.\n    91→\n    92→## Block 10: text_block — This block is a note stating that all detention basins, water quality ponds, and appurtenances must be maintained by the record owner in accordance with the Drainage and Environmental Criteria Manual.\n    93→\n    94→All detention basins, water quality ponds and appurtenances which receive stormwater runoff from commercial or\n    95→multi-family development shall be maintained by the record owner in accordance with the maintenance standards in the\n    96→Drainage and Environmental Criteria Manual.\n    97→\n    98→## Block 11: text_block — This block is a note stating that compliance with the Commercial and Multi-Family Recycling Ordinance is mandatory.\n    99→\n   100→Compliance with the Commercial and Multi-Family Recycling Ordinance is mandatory for multi-family complexes,\n   101→businesses and office buildings.\n   102→\n   103→## Block 12: text_block — This block is a note indicating where the Integrated Pest Management Plan can be found in the Official Public Records of Travis County, Texas.\n   104→\n   105→For Integrated Pest Management Plan, see agreement filed in document No.____________, Official Public Records,\n   106→Travis County, Texas.\n   107→\n   108→## Block 13: text_block — This block is a note stating that the project is located within the West Bouldin Creek Watershed and that no portion of the tract is within the 100-year flood plain.\n   109→\n   110→This project is located within the West Bouldin Creek Watershed (Urban). All storm flows from this site will be directed\n   111→to the West Bouldin Creek Watershed. No portion of this tract is within the boundaries of the 100 year flood plain of\n   112→any waterway that is within the limits of study of the Federal Flood Insurance Administration FIRM panel\n   113→#48453C0585H, dated September 26, 2008 for Travis County.\n   114→\n   115→## Block 14: text_block — This block is a note stating that the project is not located within the Edwards Aquifer Recharge Zone or the Edwards Aquifer Contributing Zone.\n   116→\n   117→Edwards Aquifer Note This project is not located within the Edwards Aquifer Recharge Zone or the Edwards Aquifer\n   118→Contributing Zone.\n   119→\n   120→## Block 15: text_block — This block contains the scale, mapsco number, and city of Austin grid number for the project location map.\n   121→\n   122→Project Location Map\n   123→Scale: 1\" = 400'\n   124→Mapsco #614S\n   125→City of Austin Grid #G19\n   126→\n   127→## Block 16: text_block — This block contains a table for recording the dates that various City departments reviewed the plans.\n   128→\n   129→Reviewed By:\n   130→\n   131→Development Services Department Date\n   132→SP-2025-0126C\n   133→Development Permit No.\n   134→\n   135→City of Austin Fire Department Date\n   136→\n   137→Austin Water Date\n   138→\n   139→## Block 17: text_block — This block is a note indicating that the contractor is responsible for filing all necessary forms with the Environmental Protection Agency for projects involving 5 acres or more of disturbed area.\n   140→\n   141→Contractor is responsible for filing all necessary forms with the Environmental Protection Agency for all projects\n   142→involving 5 acres or more of disturbed area or part of a larger development which will eventually disturb 5 acres or more.\n   143→Note The contractor and the owner both must file a Notice of Intent.\n   144→\n   145→## Block 18: text_block — This block is a note requiring all potable water system components installed after January 4, 2014, to be \"lead free\" according to the US Safe Drinking Water Act. It lists examples of exempt and non-exempt components.\n   146→\n   147→All potable water system components installed after January 4, 2014, shall be essentially \"lead free\" according to the\n   148→US Safe Drinking Water Act. Examples are valves (corporation stop, curb stop, and pressure reducing), nipples,\n   149→bushings, pipe, fittings and backflow preventers. Fire hydrants, tapping saddles and 2 inch and larger gate valves are\n   150→the only components exempt from this requirement. Components that are not clearly identified by the manufacturer as\n   151→meeting this requirement either by markings on the component or on the packaging shall not be installed.\n   152→\n   153→## Block 19: text_block — This block is a note regarding the project's private hydrants and the owner's responsibility to comply with the Austin Fire Code. It states that private hydrants must be serviced, maintained, and flowed annually.\n   154→\n   155→City of Austin - Water and Wastewater Utility - Special Services Division (512) 972-1060\n   156→This project has private hydrants located within the property. The property owner is required to comply with Austin\n   157→Fire Code. Failure to comply may result in civil and/or criminal remedies available to the City. The performance of\n   158→this obligation shall always rest with the owner or record. Fire hydrants on private property are required to serviced,\n   159→maintained and flowed annually, using a contractor registered with the City to provide this service. This project\n   160→includes __1__ private hydrants.\n   161→\n   162→## Block 20: text_block — This block states that a civil engineer registered in Texas must certify the plan as complete, accurate, and in compliance with the Land Development Code, unless waived by the director.\n   163→\n   164→A civil engineer registered in Texas must certify a plan or plat as complete, accurate, and in compliance with Chapter\n   165→25-8 Subchapter A of the Land Development Code. The director may waive this requirement after making a\n   166→determination that the plan or plat includes only minor alterations or improvement that do not require the services of an\n   167→engineer.\n   168→\n   169→## Block 21: text_block — This block is a note regarding the placement of silt fences and additional erosion/sedimentation controls as required by the City's Environmental and Conservation Services Department. It also specifies that only approved construction entrances should be used.\n   170→\n   171→All temporary spoils and equipment storage areas shall have silt fence placed along the perimeter of the downslope\n   172→side. Additional erosion/sedimentation controls may be required at the direction of the City's Environmental and\n   173→Conservation Services Department Officer/Inspector. The contractor shall work closely with all City Personnel to insure\n   174→adequacy of placement and maintenance of all erosion/sedimentation control devices. Only those construction\n   175→entrances shown on the approved site plan shall be used for ingress and egress to and from site. In the event that\n   176→additional entrance locations are required to facilitate placement of materials, the contractor shall construct a stabilized\n   177→construction entrance in accordance with City of Austin Standard Details in order to comply with all provisions of the\n   178→City's Land Development Code and Environmental Protection Ordinances.\n   179→\n   180→## Block 22: text_block — This block is a note stating that approval by the City of Austin indicates compliance with applicable City regulations only and that approval by other governmental entities may be required.\n   181→\n   182→Approval of these plans by the City of Austin indicates compliance with applicable City regulations only. Approval by\n   183→other governmental entities may be required prior to the start of construction. The applicant is responsible for\n   184→determining what additional approvals may be necessary.\n   185→\n   186→## Block 23: text_block — This block is a note stating that the project received approval from the Watershed Protection Department for a waiver to a specific section of the COA Drainage Criteria Manual.\n   187→\n   188→DCM Waiver Note: On 01/21/2026 this project received approval from the Watershed Protection Department of a\n   189→waiver to Section 1.2.4.E.1.e.i of the COA Drainage Criteria Manual.\n   190→\n   191→## Block 24: text_block — This block contains a stamp for the City of Austin to officially approve the site plan. It includes fields for the file number, application date, approval date, whether it was approved administratively or by commission, the expiration date, case manager, and zoning.\n   192→\n   193→SITE PLAN APPROVAL SHEET ____1____ of ____39____\n   194→FILE NUMBER ____SP-2025-0126C____ APPLICATION DATE ____05/20/2025____\n   195→APPROVED ON _________________ \n   196→□ADMINISTRATIVELY \n   197→□BY COMMISSION\n   198→UNDER SECTION 112 OF CHAPTER 25-5 OF THE CITY OF AUSTIN CODE.\n   199→EXPIRATION DATE (25-5-81,LDC) ___________________ CASE MANAGER ___Jim Gobel_______\n   200→____________________________________________________________________________________________\n   201→Austin Development Services\n   202→RELEASED FOR GENERAL COMPLIANCE _________________ ZONING ____MF-2____\n   203→____________________________________________________________________________________________\n   204→Approval Stamps:\n   205→\n   206→## Block 25: text_block — This block contains a certification statement signed by the engineer, stating that the engineering work complies with the Texas Engineering Practice Act and the City of Austin's Land Development Code.\n   207→\n   208→I Jason K. Rodgers do hereby certify that the engineering work being submitted herein complies with all provisions of\n   209→the Texas Engineering Practice Act, including Section 131.152(e). I hereby acknowledge that any misrepresentation\n   210→regarding this certification constitutes a violation of the Act, and may result in criminal, civil and/or administrative\n   211→penalties against me, as authorized by the Act. The plan or plat is complete, accurate and in compliance with Chapter\n   212→25-8 Subchapter A of the Land Development Code.\n   213→I certify that these engineering documents are complete, accurate and adequate for the intended purposes,\n   214→including construction, but are not authorized for construction prior to formal City approval.\n   215→\n   216→[Signature of Jason K. Rodgers]\n   217→Jason K. Rodgers\n   218→2/27/26\n   219→\n   220→## Block 26: text_block — This block contains notes regarding the requirement for a temporary traffic control plan (TCP) to be reviewed and approved prior to construction.\n   221→\n   222→Traffic Control Plan Note:\n   223→This note is being placed on the plan set in the absence of a temporary traffic control plan (TCP) with the full\n   224→understanding that an engineered TCP shall be reviewed and approved by the Right of Way Management\n   225→Division. Furthermore, a TCP shall be submitted to TCPReview@austintexas.gov for review a minimum of 6\n   226→weeks prior to the start of construction. The applicant/project representative further recognizes that a TCP review\n   227→fee is required for the initial review and all re- reviews, as prescribed by the most current version of the City's fee\n   228→ordinance.\n   229→\n   230→The following must be taken into consideration:\n   231→· Refer to the “Mobility Guidelines” for developing traffic control strategies\n   232→http://www.austintexas.gov/page/mobility-guidelines.\n   233→· TCPs shall not be approved without an approved site plan, site plan exemption, or general permit.\n   234→· A traffic control plan is not a permit.\n   235→\n   236→## Block 27: text_block — This block is a note stating that the site plan is subject to Subchapter E of the Land Development Code (Commercial Design Standards) and that compliance is required during building code review.\n   237→\n   238→This site plan is subject to Subchapter E of the Land Development Code (Commercial Design Standards). Compliance\n   239→with Building Design Standards, Article 3 of Subchapter E, is required, and is to be reviewed for compliance during\n   240→building code review.\n   241→\n   242→## Block 28: text_block — This block states that a fee in-lieu of parkland dedication must be paid prior to the issuance of the Certificate of Occupancy.\n   243→\n   244→A fee in-lieu of parkland dedication must be paid for 39 residential units prior to the issuance of the Certificate of\n   245→Occupancy. No Certificate of Occupancy may be issued for this development until receipt of payment. Contact the\n   246→Parks and Recreation Department prior to requesting inspections.\n   247→\n   248→## Block 29: text_block — This block is a disclaimer stating that the City's review of the application does not verify the data, information, and calculations supplied by the applicant. The engineer of record is solely responsible for the submittal's completeness, accuracy, and adequacy.\n   249→\n   250→Release of this application does not constitute a verification of all data, information and calculations supplied by the\n   251→applicant. The engineer of record is solely responsible for the completeness, accuracy and adequacy of his/her\n   252→submittal, whether or not the application is reviewed for Code compliance by City engineers.\n   253→\n   254→## Block 30: text_block — This block is a note stating that development of structures requiring a building permit must comply with the City of Austin Street Impact Fee Ordinances and must be paid upon completion of the building permit plan review.\n   255→\n   256→Development of structures that require a building permit within this Site Plan, or revisions thereof, are required to\n   257→comply with the City of Austin Street Impact Fee Ordinances, as applicable, and must be paid upon completion of the\n   258→building permit plan review for each building. Reference: LDC 25-6-662\n   259→\n   260→## Block 31: text_block — This block is a note regarding procedures to follow if an underground storage tank (UST) is found during construction.\n   261→\n   262→If at any time during construction of this project as underground storage tank (UST) is found, construction in that area\n   263→must stop until a City of Austin UST Construction Permit is applied for and approved. Any UST removal work must be\n   264→conducted by a UST Contractor that is registered with the Texas Commission on Environmental Quality (TCEQ).\n   265→Contact UST@austintexas.gov if you have any questions.[COA Title 6]\n   266→\n   267→## Block 32: text_block — This block is a note stating that the engineer who prepared the plans is responsible for their adequacy and that the City of Austin relies on their work.\n   268→\n   269→All responsibility for the adequacy of these plans remains with the Engineer who prepared them. In reviewing these\n   270→plans, the City of Austin must rely upon the adequacy of the work of the Design Engineer.\n   271→\n   272→## Block 33: text_block — This block is a note stating that the proposed stacked biofiltration/detention pond will be privately maintained.\n   273→\n   274→The proposed stacked biofiltration/detention pond will\n   275→be privately maintained.\n   276→\n   277→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4e7b1c1f-9804-4a61-b82e-41dbab740236","uuid":"89867db3-4ade-4aba-aa5e-222f7778a484","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/vercel/sandbox/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-01/blocks.md","content":"# Sheet 1 — Content Blocks\n\n## Block 1: drawing — This block shows a map of the project location, highlighting the surrounding streets and intersection. A pointer indicates the specific project location.\n\n[Map showing the project location and surrounding streets.]\n\nN\n\nPROJECT\nLOCATION\n\n## Block 5: table — This block contains data related to the Austin Fire Department's requirements for the project. It includes information such as fire design codes, fire flow demand, occupancy classification, construction classification, building fire area, automatic fire sprinkler system type, reduced fire flow demand, applies to project status, AFD fire hydrant flow test dates and locations, city of Austin pipeline ordinance compliance, high-rise status, international wildland-urban interface code compliance, and alternative method of compliance AMOC.\n\nAustin Fire Department\n\n| Fire Design Codes | 2021 International Fire Code Edition\nwith City of Austin Local Amendments |\n|---|---|\n| Fire Flow Demand @ 20 psi\n(gpm) | 3000 GPM |\n| Occupancy Classification | R3 |\n| Construction Classification | Type V-B |\n| Building Fire Area (s.f.) | 13,344 |\n| Automatic Fire Sprinkler System\nType (If applicable) | NFPA 13D |\n| Reduced Fire Flow Demand @ 20\npsi for having a sprinkler system\n(gpm) | 1500 GPM |\n| AFD Fire Hydrant Flow Test Date | 3/21/2025 |\n| AFD Fire Hydrant Flow Test\nLocation | 3700 Valley View Rd. |\n| City of Austin Pipeline Ordinance\nApplies to Project | No |\n| High-Rise | No |\n| International Wildland-Urban\nInterface Code | N/A |\n| Alternative Method of\nCompliance AMOC (If applicable) | N/A |\n\n## Block 6: table — This block contains the site development data for the Valley View Townhomes project. It includes contact information for the owner, engineer, architect, and landscape architect, as well as the legal description, subdivision file number, zoning case number, and limits of construction.\n\nSite Development Data Valley View Townhomes\nOwner: WM 41 Austin RE, LLC.\nContact Person: Richard D. Agnew\n500 West 5th Street, Ste. 1010\nAustin, Texas 78701\nPhone: 512-565-6159\nEmail: Richard.Agnew@slpops.com\n\nEngineer: Bleyl Engineering\nContact Person: Jason Rodgers\n7701 San Felipe, Suite 200\nAustin, Texas 78729\nPhone: (512) 454-2400\nEmail: jrodgers@bleylengineering.com\n\nArchitect: Danze & Davis Architects, Inc.\nContact Person: Harrison Davis\n4701 Spicewood Springs Rd, Ste 200\nAustin, Texas 78759\nPhone: (512) 343-0714\n\nLandscape Architect: Blu Fish Collaborative, Inc.\nContact Person: Mike Fishbaugh\n3607 S. Lamar Blvd., Suite 104\nAustin, Texas 78704\nPhone: (512) 338-4115\n\nLegal Description: Lot 1 Mecey Subdivision, Volume 73, Page 76, Plat Records of Travis County,\nTexas\n2.16 Acres\nSubdivision File No. C8S-75-160\nZoning Case No. C14-2011-0093\nLimits of Construction: 2.26 Acres\n\n## Block 8: text_block — This block is the title and primary identification information for the site plan. It states the project name, address, jurisdiction, SP number, and submittal date.\n\nSite Plan\nValley View Townhomes\n3759 Valley View Road\nAustin, Texas 78704\nJurisdiction: Austin Full Purpose\n\nSP-2025-0126C\nSubmittal Date: May 20, 2025\n\n## Block 9: text_block — This block is a disclaimer from Bleyl Engineering stating that they are not responsible for the accuracy of the survey or design errors resulting from survey inaccuracies.\n\nBleyl Engineering and its associates will not be held responsible for the accuracy of the survey or for design errors or\nomissions resulting from survey inaccuracies.\n\n## Block 10: text_block — This block is a note stating that all detention basins, water quality ponds, and appurtenances must be maintained by the record owner in accordance with the Drainage and Environmental Criteria Manual.\n\nAll detention basins, water quality ponds and appurtenances which receive stormwater runoff from commercial or\nmulti-family development shall be maintained by the record owner in accordance with the maintenance standards in the\nDrainage and Environmental Criteria Manual.\n\n## Block 11: text_block — This block is a note stating that compliance with the Commercial and Multi-Family Recycling Ordinance is mandatory.\n\nCompliance with the Commercial and Multi-Family Recycling Ordinance is mandatory for multi-family complexes,\nbusinesses and office buildings.\n\n## Block 12: text_block — This block is a note indicating where the Integrated Pest Management Plan can be found in the Official Public Records of Travis County, Texas.\n\nFor Integrated Pest Management Plan, see agreement filed in document No.____________, Official Public Records,\nTravis County, Texas.\n\n## Block 13: text_block — This block is a note stating that the project is located within the West Bouldin Creek Watershed and that no portion of the tract is within the 100-year flood plain.\n\nThis project is located within the West Bouldin Creek Watershed (Urban). All storm flows from this site will be directed\nto the West Bouldin Creek Watershed. No portion of this tract is within the boundaries of the 100 year flood plain of\nany waterway that is within the limits of study of the Federal Flood Insurance Administration FIRM panel\n#48453C0585H, dated September 26, 2008 for Travis County.\n\n## Block 14: text_block — This block is a note stating that the project is not located within the Edwards Aquifer Recharge Zone or the Edwards Aquifer Contributing Zone.\n\nEdwards Aquifer Note This project is not located within the Edwards Aquifer Recharge Zone or the Edwards Aquifer\nContributing Zone.\n\n## Block 15: text_block — This block contains the scale, mapsco number, and city of Austin grid number for the project location map.\n\nProject Location Map\nScale: 1\" = 400'\nMapsco #614S\nCity of Austin Grid #G19\n\n## Block 16: text_block — This block contains a table for recording the dates that various City departments reviewed the plans.\n\nReviewed By:\n\nDevelopment Services Department Date\nSP-2025-0126C\nDevelopment Permit No.\n\nCity of Austin Fire Department Date\n\nAustin Water Date\n\n## Block 17: text_block — This block is a note indicating that the contractor is responsible for filing all necessary forms with the Environmental Protection Agency for projects involving 5 acres or more of disturbed area.\n\nContractor is responsible for filing all necessary forms with the Environmental Protection Agency for all projects\ninvolving 5 acres or more of disturbed area or part of a larger development which will eventually disturb 5 acres or more.\nNote The contractor and the owner both must file a Notice of Intent.\n\n## Block 18: text_block — This block is a note requiring all potable water system components installed after January 4, 2014, to be \"lead free\" according to the US Safe Drinking Water Act. It lists examples of exempt and non-exempt components.\n\nAll potable water system components installed after January 4, 2014, shall be essentially \"lead free\" according to the\nUS Safe Drinking Water Act. Examples are valves (corporation stop, curb stop, and pressure reducing), nipples,\nbushings, pipe, fittings and backflow preventers. Fire hydrants, tapping saddles and 2 inch and larger gate valves are\nthe only components exempt from this requirement. Components that are not clearly identified by the manufacturer as\nmeeting this requirement either by markings on the component or on the packaging shall not be installed.\n\n## Block 19: text_block — This block is a note regarding the project's private hydrants and the owner's responsibility to comply with the Austin Fire Code. It states that private hydrants must be serviced, maintained, and flowed annually.\n\nCity of Austin - Water and Wastewater Utility - Special Services Division (512) 972-1060\nThis project has private hydrants located within the property. The property owner is required to comply with Austin\nFire Code. Failure to comply may result in civil and/or criminal remedies available to the City. The performance of\nthis obligation shall always rest with the owner or record. Fire hydrants on private property are required to serviced,\nmaintained and flowed annually, using a contractor registered with the City to provide this service. This project\nincludes __1__ private hydrants.\n\n## Block 20: text_block — This block states that a civil engineer registered in Texas must certify the plan as complete, accurate, and in compliance with the Land Development Code, unless waived by the director.\n\nA civil engineer registered in Texas must certify a plan or plat as complete, accurate, and in compliance with Chapter\n25-8 Subchapter A of the Land Development Code. The director may waive this requirement after making a\ndetermination that the plan or plat includes only minor alterations or improvement that do not require the services of an\nengineer.\n\n## Block 21: text_block — This block is a note regarding the placement of silt fences and additional erosion/sedimentation controls as required by the City's Environmental and Conservation Services Department. It also specifies that only approved construction entrances should be used.\n\nAll temporary spoils and equipment storage areas shall have silt fence placed along the perimeter of the downslope\nside. Additional erosion/sedimentation controls may be required at the direction of the City's Environmental and\nConservation Services Department Officer/Inspector. The contractor shall work closely with all City Personnel to insure\nadequacy of placement and maintenance of all erosion/sedimentation control devices. Only those construction\nentrances shown on the approved site plan shall be used for ingress and egress to and from site. In the event that\nadditional entrance locations are required to facilitate placement of materials, the contractor shall construct a stabilized\nconstruction entrance in accordance with City of Austin Standard Details in order to comply with all provisions of the\nCity's Land Development Code and Environmental Protection Ordinances.\n\n## Block 22: text_block — This block is a note stating that approval by the City of Austin indicates compliance with applicable City regulations only and that approval by other governmental entities may be required.\n\nApproval of these plans by the City of Austin indicates compliance with applicable City regulations only. Approval by\nother governmental entities may be required prior to the start of construction. The applicant is responsible for\ndetermining what additional approvals may be necessary.\n\n## Block 23: text_block — This block is a note stating that the project received approval from the Watershed Protection Department for a waiver to a specific section of the COA Drainage Criteria Manual.\n\nDCM Waiver Note: On 01/21/2026 this project received approval from the Watershed Protection Department of a\nwaiver to Section 1.2.4.E.1.e.i of the COA Drainage Criteria Manual.\n\n## Block 24: text_block — This block contains a stamp for the City of Austin to officially approve the site plan. It includes fields for the file number, application date, approval date, whether it was approved administratively or by commission, the expiration date, case manager, and zoning.\n\nSITE PLAN APPROVAL SHEET ____1____ of ____39____\nFILE NUMBER ____SP-2025-0126C____ APPLICATION DATE ____05/20/2025____\nAPPROVED ON _________________ \n□ADMINISTRATIVELY \n□BY COMMISSION\nUNDER SECTION 112 OF CHAPTER 25-5 OF THE CITY OF AUSTIN CODE.\nEXPIRATION DATE (25-5-81,LDC) ___________________ CASE MANAGER ___Jim Gobel_______\n____________________________________________________________________________________________\nAustin Development Services\nRELEASED FOR GENERAL COMPLIANCE _________________ ZONING ____MF-2____\n____________________________________________________________________________________________\nApproval Stamps:\n\n## Block 25: text_block — This block contains a certification statement signed by the engineer, stating that the engineering work complies with the Texas Engineering Practice Act and the City of Austin's Land Development Code.\n\nI Jason K. Rodgers do hereby certify that the engineering work being submitted herein complies with all provisions of\nthe Texas Engineering Practice Act, including Section 131.152(e). I hereby acknowledge that any misrepresentation\nregarding this certification constitutes a violation of the Act, and may result in criminal, civil and/or administrative\npenalties against me, as authorized by the Act. The plan or plat is complete, accurate and in compliance with Chapter\n25-8 Subchapter A of the Land Development Code.\nI certify that these engineering documents are complete, accurate and adequate for the intended purposes,\nincluding construction, but are not authorized for construction prior to formal City approval.\n\n[Signature of Jason K. Rodgers]\nJason K. Rodgers\n2/27/26\n\n## Block 26: text_block — This block contains notes regarding the requirement for a temporary traffic control plan (TCP) to be reviewed and approved prior to construction.\n\nTraffic Control Plan Note:\nThis note is being placed on the plan set in the absence of a temporary traffic control plan (TCP) with the full\nunderstanding that an engineered TCP shall be reviewed and approved by the Right of Way Management\nDivision. Furthermore, a TCP shall be submitted to TCPReview@austintexas.gov for review a minimum of 6\nweeks prior to the start of construction. The applicant/project representative further recognizes that a TCP review\nfee is required for the initial review and all re- reviews, as prescribed by the most current version of the City's fee\nordinance.\n\nThe following must be taken into consideration:\n· Refer to the “Mobility Guidelines” for developing traffic control strategies\nhttp://www.austintexas.gov/page/mobility-guidelines.\n· TCPs shall not be approved without an approved site plan, site plan exemption, or general permit.\n· A traffic control plan is not a permit.\n\n## Block 27: text_block — This block is a note stating that the site plan is subject to Subchapter E of the Land Development Code (Commercial Design Standards) and that compliance is required during building code review.\n\nThis site plan is subject to Subchapter E of the Land Development Code (Commercial Design Standards). Compliance\nwith Building Design Standards, Article 3 of Subchapter E, is required, and is to be reviewed for compliance during\nbuilding code review.\n\n## Block 28: text_block — This block states that a fee in-lieu of parkland dedication must be paid prior to the issuance of the Certificate of Occupancy.\n\nA fee in-lieu of parkland dedication must be paid for 39 residential units prior to the issuance of the Certificate of\nOccupancy. No Certificate of Occupancy may be issued for this development until receipt of payment. Contact the\nParks and Recreation Department prior to requesting inspections.\n\n## Block 29: text_block — This block is a disclaimer stating that the City's review of the application does not verify the data, information, and calculations supplied by the applicant. The engineer of record is solely responsible for the submittal's completeness, accuracy, and adequacy.\n\nRelease of this application does not constitute a verification of all data, information and calculations supplied by the\napplicant. The engineer of record is solely responsible for the completeness, accuracy and adequacy of his/her\nsubmittal, whether or not the application is reviewed for Code compliance by City engineers.\n\n## Block 30: text_block — This block is a note stating that development of structures requiring a building permit must comply with the City of Austin Street Impact Fee Ordinances and must be paid upon completion of the building permit plan review.\n\nDevelopment of structures that require a building permit within this Site Plan, or revisions thereof, are required to\ncomply with the City of Austin Street Impact Fee Ordinances, as applicable, and must be paid upon completion of the\nbuilding permit plan review for each building. Reference: LDC 25-6-662\n\n## Block 31: text_block — This block is a note regarding procedures to follow if an underground storage tank (UST) is found during construction.\n\nIf at any time during construction of this project as underground storage tank (UST) is found, construction in that area\nmust stop until a City of Austin UST Construction Permit is applied for and approved. Any UST removal work must be\nconducted by a UST Contractor that is registered with the Texas Commission on Environmental Quality (TCEQ).\nContact UST@austintexas.gov if you have any questions.[COA Title 6]\n\n## Block 32: text_block — This block is a note stating that the engineer who prepared the plans is responsible for their adequacy and that the City of Austin relies on their work.\n\nAll responsibility for the adequacy of these plans remains with the Engineer who prepared them. In reviewing these\nplans, the City of Austin must rely upon the adequacy of the work of the Design Engineer.\n\n## Block 33: text_block — This block is a note stating that the proposed stacked biofiltration/detention pond will be privately maintained.\n\nThe proposed stacked biofiltration/detention pond will\nbe privately maintained.\n\n","numLines":277,"startLine":1,"totalLines":277}}}
