{"level":30,"time":1776973762779,"pid":123,"hostname":"844f2260-bff","step":"review-runs","item":"15.md","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01QrUUMsrcqemLyWcYJqFTUP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01AG3F34HcbSP6T8Bzn6Gq8N","name":"mcp__conductor_tools__vision","input":{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":21,"prompt":"Examine the electrical design plan carefully. Look for:\n\n1. Location and exact placement of all transformer pad(s) on the site\n2. Any dimensions or measurements showing clearances from the transformer pad to buildings, structures, parking areas, or other features\n3. Clearance annotations (such as \"10 ft,\" \"12 ft,\" \"5 ft,\" etc.) near transformer locations\n4. Any notes referencing Austin Energy Design Criteria, transformer clearance standards, or specific clearance distances\n5. Building construction materials (wood, masonry, etc.) that would affect transformer clearance requirements\n6. The exact distance from each transformer pad to the nearest building\n\nProvide specific details about transformer pad locations and whether clearances are labeled or dimensioned on the plans."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":13,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6615,"cache_read_input_tokens":51189,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":6615,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"33f519bd-bced-4a7a-aae5-831dbf134acc","uuid":"ea628473-e258-4306-a80a-cf795e240147"}
{"level":30,"time":1776973762807,"pid":123,"hostname":"844f2260-bff","step":"review-runs","item":"15.md","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":9,"prompt":"Examine the site plan drawing carefully. Look for and describe:\n\n1. Any labeled setback lines on the property boundaries (such as \"Building Setback Line,\" \"Front Setback,\" \"Rear Setback,\" \"Side Setback,\" \"Compatibility Buffer,\" or similar labels)\n2. Dimensions or measurements associated with any setback lines visible on the drawing\n3. Any buffer zones or compatibility buffer areas shown with hatching, shading, or labels\n4. The property lines and their proximity to buildings or structures\n5. Any reference callouts or notes pointing to setback requirements\n6. Location of all 8 buildings relative to property boundaries\n\nProvide specific details about what is and is not shown for setback compliance documentation.","msg":"Calling vision tool: 1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777 (9)"}
