{"level":30,"time":1776973768573,"pid":123,"hostname":"844f2260-bff","step":"review-runs","item":"32.md","index":1,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013FqEEhB61LdJsV84KUuNjF","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Property Attributes\n     2→\n     3→*Outlines jurisdictional boundaries, housing program participation, watershed details, and street/neighborhood plans for the site.*\n     4→\n     5→Section 6: Property Attributes\n     6→Land Development Jurisdiction: [x] Full-Purpose [ ] Limited-Purpose\n     7→Does your project include affordable housing units or fee-in-lieu of affordable units? Select all type(s) of affordable housing program(s) and funding being pursued:\n     8→[ ] Permanent Supportive Housing (PSH)\n     9→[ ] S.M.A.R.T. Housing\n    10→[ ] Density Bonus\n    11→[ ] Density Bonus (DB) 90. Is the Certification Letter attached? [ ] Yes [x] No\n    12→[ ] Government Funding (County/State/Federal). Exp. Date(s):\n    13→If residential, are there other Tax Credits or State/Federal funding? [ ] Yes [x] No\n    14→Is your project a capital improvement project? If so, who is the department sponsor? \n    15→Is your project a school project? [ ] Yes [x] No\n    16→School District: AISD Provide the name of the school district this project is located within.\n    17→Does the proposal include demolition or relocation of any buildings over 45 years old? [ ] Yes [x] No\n    18→If demolition is proposed, how many residential units will be demolished? \n    19→Number of these residential units currently occupied: \n    20→\n    21→City of Austin | Consolidated Site Plan Completeness Check Application 10/21/24 | Page 3 of 8\n    22→\n    23→Number of Newly Proposed Residential Units (if applicable): 39\n    24→Is your project in City of Austin Edwards Aquifer Recharge Zone? [ ] Yes [x] No\n    25→[x] Smart Growth Zone -OR- [ ] Drinking Water Protection Zone\n    26→Watershed: West Bouldin Creek Watershed Class: Urban Watersheds\n    27→Is your project subject to all current Watershed Protection regulations? [x] Yes [ ] No\n    28→Is your project on a Hill Country Roadway? [ ] Yes [x] No\n    29→Specify Hill Country Roadway: \n    30→Principal Street Type: [ ] Core Transit Corridor [x] Urban Roadway [ ] Internal Circulation Route [ ] Suburban Roadway [ ] Hill Country Roadway [ ] Highway\n    31→In a Neighborhood Plan? [ ] Yes [x] No\n    32→If Yes, name of Neighborhood Plan: South Lamar\n    33→Select which regulating plan the property is in, if applicable:\n    34→[ ] Transit-Oriented Development (TOD) District. Name: \n    35→[ ] North Burnet/Gateway (NBG)\n    36→[ ] East Riverside Corridor (ERC)\n    37→[ ] Planned Unit Development (PUD). Ordinance #: \n    38→[ ] Planned Development Agreement (PDA). Ordinance #: \n    39→Select which historic district the property is in, if applicable:\n    40→[ ] Local historic district (HD zoning)\n    41→[ ] National Register historic district\n    42→[ ] Landmarked property (H zoning)\n    43→Is the project located within the University Neighborhood Overlay (UNO) boundaries, and subject to the streetscape standards of UNO? [ ] Yes [x] No\n    44→Is the project located within the boundaries of downtown Austin, with the boundaries of MLK Blvd. to the north, the Colorado River to the south, Lamar Blvd. to the west, and I35 to the east, and subject to required streetscape standards? [ ] Yes [x] No\n    45→Will the project need to participate in the Downtown Density Bonus Program (DDBP), seeking to increase maximum building height, and/or Floor to Area Ratio (FAR) beyond base entitlements? [ ] Yes [x] No\n    46→Is the project opting to participate in the Great Streets Program? [ ] Yes [x] No\n    47→Will a License Agreement Application be submitted for this project? [ ] Yes [x] No\n    48→Electric Utility Provider: Austin Energy\n    49→Water Provider: Austin Water\n    50→Wastewater Disposal Provider: Austin Water\n    51→\n   