{"level":30,"time":1776973771550,"pid":123,"hostname":"844f2260-bff","step":"review-runs","item":"32.md","index":7,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_012PXeFV6RL6zCuyTu2cyqTx","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Great! Now I have good detail from the cover sheet. Let me extract key information:\n\n**From the Site Development Data (Block 6):**\n- Zoning: MF-2 (confirmed)\n- Zoning Case No.: C14-2011-0093 (matches facts.md: Ordinance 20120112-092)\n- Limits of Construction: 2.26 Acres\n- Site Area: 2.16 Acres\n\n**Key Notes from Cover Sheet:**\n- No neighborhood plan statement visible (South Lamar NPA is suspended per facts.md, so may not be required)\n- No mention of DDBP participation\n- No mention of Article 10/compatibility standards being triggered\n- No mention of UNO, ETOD, TOD, WO, VMU, CBD, DMU\n- Nonconforming Signs area applies per facts.md line 55 — but I need to check if the site plan has a sign compliance note\n- The site plan notes subject to Subchapter E (Commercial Design Standards) per Block 27 — wait, this is odd. The site is MF-2 (multi-family), not commercial. Let me check this more carefully.\n\nActually looking at Block 27:\n\"This site plan is subject to Subchapter E of the Land Development Code (Commercial Design Standards). Compliance with Building Design Standards, Article 3 of Subchapter E, is required, and is to be reviewed for compliance during building code review.\"\n\nThis seems like boilerplate that might apply to all developments. I need to verify what design standards actually apply.\n\n**Related to ZLU-32 Checklist items:**\n\n1. ZLU-32.44 (Sign compliance note) — APPLICABLE to all sites per checklist. I need to check if the site plan includes \"a note stating that all signs must comply with the requirements of LDC Chapter 25-10.\" Looking at the blocks above, I don't see such a note explicitly. Let me check if there's more detail.\n\n\n2. ZLU-32.47 (Nonconforming Signs area compliance) — APPLICABLE per facts.md. The site is in a Nonconforming Signs Ordinance area, so the site plan must address compliance with LDC § 25-10-152.\n3. ZLU-32.31 (Townhouse lots) — APPLICABLE. The proposed use is \"39 multi-family townhome units\" per facts. The checklist item requires that each townhouse unit be located on a separate townhouse lot per LDC § 25-2-775. I need to check the site plan sheets to verify this.\n4. ZLU-32.35 (Mult\n\n-family transit proximity) — APPLICABLE since the development involves multifamily units. LDC § 25-1-703(B)(4) mandates proximity to public transit within a half-mile walking distance, so I need to verify the site plan and facts confirm this requirement is met.\n5. ZLU-32.20 (Neighborhood plan statement) — The South Lamar NPA is SUSPENDED per facts, making this likely NOT APPLICABLE.\n6. ZLU-32.46 (Scenic Roadway sign) — Only relevant if Valley View Road qualifies as a scenic roadway. Facts.md doesn't identify it as such, but I should confirm this designation.\n\nNow I'll examine the site plan more closely, particularly Sheet 9, to assess the townhouse lot layout and other site-specific requirements.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":12,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7834,"cache_read_input_tokens":46296,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":7834,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c1ccbdc1-20f6-4e62-a4c2-17685db82f6f","uuid":"f38f008f-c6ed-42dc-9816-d7ec5e198800"}
