| Total | |\n\nSP2 – Current Status: Pending\n* U1: Please ensure that each building height is calculated correctly. The height of each building is calculated from the average of the highest and lowest grades adjacent to the building to the top of the coping. Therefore, the building height could be different for each building.\n* U0: Show the following building information (show proposed and allowed) for each building and the total for all buildings in a Building Data Table:\n  o gross floor area for each building (in sq. ft.)\n  o building coverage for each building (in sq. ft.)\n  o building height for each building (in feet and stories)\n  o foundation type and finished floor elevation for each building\n\nSP3 – Current Status: Cleared\n* U1: Multifamily use confirmed. Please let the Case Manager know if you would like to change the project name. Comment cleared. \n* U0: Please confirm that you are proposing Townhouse use. FYI – Townhouses will need to plat a townhouse subdivision as not more than one townhouse is permitted on a townhouse lot. A townhouse lot must include a private yard with a wall or solid fence along a side lot line. \nReference: 25-2-775\n\nSUBCHAPTER E: DESIGN STANDARDS\nSP4 - Current Status: Cleared\nU1: Comment cleared. \nU0: Include the following note with Figure 34 on the site plan page: \"All exterior lighting will be full cut-off and fully shielded in compliance with Subchapter E 2.5 and will be reviewed during building plan review. Any change or substitution of lamp/light fixtures shall be submitted to the Director for approval in accordance with Section 2.5.2.E.\" \n\nADMINISTRATIVE \nSP5 - Current Status: Cleared\nU1: Comment cleared. \nU0: Confirm that all amenities such as walls, fences, sidewalks, swimming pools, and all other land improvements are shown on each site plan sheet.\n\nSP6 - Current Status: Cleared\nU1: Comment cleared. \nU0: Please remove all City of Pflugerville Notes and show the following City of Austin site plan release notes on the site plan:\na. All improvements shall be made in accordance with the released site plan. Any additional improvements will require site plan amendment and approval of the Development Services Department.\nb. Approval of this Site Plan does not include Building and Fire Code approval nor building permit approval. \nc. All signs must comply with requirements of the Land Development Code (Chapter 25-10).\nd. Additional electric easements may be required at a later date. \ne. Water and wastewater service will be provided by the City of Austin (or identify the service provider if other than the City of Austin). \nf. All existing structures shown to be removed will require a demolition permit from the City of Austin Development Services Department.\ng. No certificate of occupancy may be issued for the proposed residential condominium project until the owner or owners of the property have complied with Chapter 81 and 82 of the Property Code of the State of Texas or any other statutes enacted by the State concerning condominiums.\nh. For driveway construction: The owner is responsible for all costs for relocation of, or damage to utilities. \ni. For construction within the right-of-way, a ROW excavation permit is required.\n","numLines":55,"startLine":1,"totalLines":55}}}
{"level":30,"time":1776973785414,"pid":123,"hostname":"844f2260-bff","step":"review-runs","item":"32.md","index":7,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01VddzZi9wWFUGCQFyKHJH8V","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Excellent. I now have key information from Sheet 9 blocks. Most importantly:\n\n**Block 5 (Release Notes) - CRITICAL for ZLU-32.44:**\nLine 33: \"All signs must comply with requirements of the Land Development Code (Chapter 25-10).\"\n\nThis directly addresses ZLU-32.44! The site plan DOES include a note stating signs must comply with LDC Chapter 25-10. So this item appears to PASS.\n\n**For ZLU-32.31 (Townhouse lots):**\nLooking at the Building Data Table (Block 15), I see the buildings are described as:\n- 4 Plex\n- 6 Plex\n- 5 Plex\n- etc.\n\nThis terminology suggests multi-unit buildings (\"4 Plex\" = 4 units). The checklist item ZLU-32.31 requires that for townhouse use, \"each townhouse unit [must be] located on a separate townhouse lot.\"\n\nThe fact that they're described as \"plexes\" and the site plan shows them as buildings on a single subdivision lot (Lot 1, Mecey Subdivision) suggests they may NOT be on separate townhouse lots. This could be a FAIL for ZLU-32.31.\n\nHowever, I need to verify this more carefully. The term \"townhome\" in the project name and \"multifamily residential\" in the use description could mean:\n1. Townhouses designed as separate units on separate lots (compliant with ZLU-32.31)\n2. Townhome-style multifamily apartments in a complex (which would not require separate lots if they're condominiums or apartments)\n\nLooking at Block 5 line 37: \"No certificate of occupancy may be issued for the proposed residential condominium project until the owner or owners of the property have complied with Chapter 81 and 82 of the Property Code...\"\n\nThis note explicitly mentions \"residential condominium project,\" which suggests the units may be set up as condominiums rather than townhouse lots.\n\n\nThe boilerplate language about condominiums doesn't necessarily clarify the actual structure. Since the project is zoned MF-2 (Multi-Family) with \"Multi-Family Residential\" as the use, ZLU-32.31 might not apply at all—it only triggers when \"townhouse use is proposed.\" If the units are legally configured as multi-family apartments or condominiums rather than separate townhouse lots, then the townhouse requirement wouldn't be relevant. I need to check the plat sheet to determine whether there's an actual subdivision showing separate townhouse lots or if it's a single multi-family development.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":13,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4733,"cache_read_input_tokens":57065,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4733,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c1ccbdc1-20f6-4e62-a4c2-17685db82f6f","uuid":"cd14c174-1386-4ca6-a12b-92172ddaab6a"}
