{"level":30,"time":1776973791918,"pid":123,"hostname":"844f2260-bff","step":"review-runs","item":"15.md","index":9,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01MNj79XY5YLuYyU4KrQ3tjE","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"CRITICAL FINDING! The Consolidated Site Plan Application Section 10 shows:\n\n\"Subject to Compatibility Standards? [ ] Yes [x] No\"\n\nThis is a major red flag. The applicant is claiming that the site is NOT subject to compatibility standards. However, based on the facts.md, there IS an adjacent SF-3 parcel that should trigger compatibility standards (either under the old Subchapter F or the new Article 10).\n\nLet me verify my understanding:\n- Site is zoned MF-2\n- SF-3 parcel (0406100210) is immediately adjacent\n- Under Article 10 (effective after July 15, 2024), compatibility applies when:\n  - Site is zoned MF-4 or less restrictive (MF-2 qualifies ✓)\n  - Site is within 75 feet of a triggering property\n  - Triggering property = 1-3 dwelling units + zoned SF-5 or more restrictive (SF-3 qualifies ✓)\n\nThe facts.md mentions this SF-3 parcel and states \"Compatibility Standards: LDC Subchapter F triggered by adjacent SF-3 parcel\". So the old Subchapter F should have applied, and now the NEW Article 10 should apply.\n\nThe fact that the applicant checked \"No\" for \"Subject to Compatibility Standards\" is a major deficiency. This is either:\n1. An error/oversight by the applicant\n2. A misunderstanding of how Article 10 applies\n\nI need to verify:\n1. Is the SF-3 parcel really within 75 feet of the site boundary?\n2. Does the SF-3 parcel have 1-3 dwelling units?\n\nThe facts.md calls it \"SF-3 parcel (0406100210)\" suggesting it's a separate parcel immediately adjacent, but doesn't specify the unit count. However, SF-3 is a single-family zone, so logically it should have 1-3 dwelling units (typically 1-2 per parcel).\n\n\nThe application is missing critical compatibility documentation. The plans should include a compatibility exhibit identifying the triggering property, required buffers (25 ft or 15 ft along the shared line), height restrictions per § 25-2-1061, and cross-sections demonstrating compliance. Since these elements don't appear in the sheet guides or blocks reviewed, I need to flag deficiencies under ZLU-15.7 (incorrect compatibility determination), ZLU-15.26 (missing compatibility exhibit), and related standards.\n\nBefore finalizing these findings, I should verify whether Article 10 actually applies by confirming the SF-3 property is within 75 feet and qualifies as a triggering property. Let me examine the site plan blocks more closely for any setback or property line information that might clarify this.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":13,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2350,"cache_read_input_tokens":62079,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2350,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d203a61d-b956-4bf7-a62f-71a0e7d71a2a","uuid":"ffbb1784-fdaf-45a7-8ba9-451d9f0230f7"}
