y line with a \"setback\" callout.\n\n**3. Buffer Zones or Compatibility Buffer Areas**\n*   There are **no buffer zones or compatibility buffer areas** shown with hatching, shading, or specific labels on this plan. \n*   The site features a \"Common Open Space\" (labeled \"4,709.62 sf\") and a \"Detention Pond\" (with a \"Pond Perimeter Fence\"), but neither is labeled as a compliance or compatibility buffer.\n\n**4 & 6. Property Lines, Proximity to Buildings, and Location of the 8 Buildings**\nThe property is bounded by a thick dashed line indicating the property limits. The 8 buildings are arranged systematically within these lines:\n*   **Northern Boundary:** **Bldg. 1**, **Bldg. 3**, and **Bldg. 5** run parallel to the northern property line. They are positioned south of a \"5' P.U.E.\", a proposed \"4' Wide Decomposed Granite Walkway,\" and a proposed \"Concrete Retaining Wall\" that borders the northern boundary.\n*   **Eastern Boundary:** **Bldg. 5** and **Bldg. 6** are situated near the eastern property line. They are positioned west of a labeled \"25' Drainage Easement\" and an \"Existing Retaining Wall to be Replaced\". An \"Existing Apartment Building\" is noted on the adjacent property to the east.\n*   **Southern Boundary:** **Bldg. 7** and **Bldg. 8** are located in the southern portion of the site but are separated from the southern property line by an internal drive aisle labeled \"Construct Type II Driveway\" and surface parking spaces.\n*   **Western Boundary:** **Bldg. 1** and **Bldg. 8** are adjacent to the western property line/street frontage. They are separated from the street right-of-way by a driveway, parking, and a labeled \"Sidewalk Easement\".\n*   **Interior Buildings:** **Bldg. 2** and **Bldg. 4** are centrally located within the site's interior, completely surrounded by internal driveways, surface parking, and the other perimeter buildings.\n\n**5. Reference Callouts or Notes Pointing to Setback Requirements**\n*   There are **no notes, tables, or reference callouts** on this page regarding setback requirements.\n*   The **\"Site Data Table\"** lists \"Zoning: MF-2/Multi-Family Low Density\" and details Impervious Cover and Building Coverage percentages, but entirely omits setback dimensions.\n*   The **\"Site Plan Release Notes,\"** **\"Building Data Table,\"** and other informational blocks (Accessibility, Lighting, Trash, Parking) contain standard compliance notes but do not mention setbacks.\n\n**Summary of Setback Compliance Documentation**\nOn this specific sheet (Sheet 9 of 39), **there is zero explicit documentation for setback compliance**. No setback lines are drawn, no setback dimensions are provided, and no tables list the required versus provided setbacks for the MF-2 zoning. To validate setback compliance, other sheets within the 39-page drawing set (such as a dedicated zoning site plan, cover sheet with expanded zoning data, or architectural site plan) would need to be reviewed.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1455,"outputTokens":962,"totalTokens":5270,"reasoningTokens":2853},"warnings":[],"providerMetadata":{"google":{"promptFeedback":null,"groundingMetadata":null,"urlContextMetadata":null,"safetyRatings":null,"serviceTier":null},"gateway":{"routing":{"originalModelId":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","resolvedProvider":"vertex","resolvedProviderApiModelId":"gemini-3.1-pro-preview","fallbacksAvailable":["google"],"planningReasoning":"System credentials planned for: vertex, google. Total execution order: vertex(system) → google(system)","canonicalSlug":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","finalProvider":"vertex","modelAttemptCount":1,"modelAttempts":[{"modelId":"vertex:gemini-3.1-pro-preview","canonicalSlug":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","success":true,"providerAttemptCount":1,"providerAttempts":[{"provider":"vertex","internalModelId":"vertex:gemini-3.1-pro-preview","providerApiModelId":"gemini-3.1-pro-preview","c