{"level":30,"time":1776973805507,"pid":123,"hostname":"844f2260-bff","step":"review-runs","item":"16.md","index":8,"runIndex":"run-3","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":9,"prompt":"Review Sheet 9 (Site Plan) and identify: (1) Are there any notations showing adjacent land uses (what uses are on adjacent properties to the north, south, east, west)? (2) Are there any labels or callouts indicating adjacent zoning districts? (3) Are there any building footprints or structures shown from adjacent properties? (4) Are there any notes about adjacent properties? (5) What is clearly shown on the perimeter of this site plan regarding adjacent areas? Be specific about what you can and cannot see.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a visual analysis of Sheet 9 (Site Plan), here is the detailed information regarding adjacent properties and areas:\n\n**(1) Are there any notations showing adjacent land uses?**\nYes, land uses are indicated primarily through subdivision names and descriptive labels of existing structures rather than formal land use classification codes. \n*   **East:** The adjacent property is labeled with residential condo uses: \"Lot 2, Chateaux Ridge Condominiums\" and \"Lot 1, Chateaux Ridge Condominiums\". It also has labels pointing to dashed footprints that read \"Existing Apartment Building\".\n*   **South:** The adjacent property has a label referencing \"William James Condos, Jr.\", indicating a residential condo use.\n*   **West:** The property bounds a roadway Right-of-Way (ROW) containing street infrastructure. \n\n**(2) Are there any labels or callouts indicating adjacent zoning districts?**\nYes, zoning labels are visible for some, but not all, adjacent areas:\n*   **East:** There are two distinct labels reading \"Zoning: MF-2-CO\" corresponding to the adjacent Chateaux Ridge Condominiums lots.\n*   **North:** Near the top boundary line (slightly right of center), there is faint text that reads \"Zoning: MF-2-CO\".\n*   **South & West:** There are no visible zoning district labels for the properties to the south or across the street to the west.\n\n**(3) Are there any building footprints or structures shown from adjacent properties?**\nYes, specifically to the East:\n*   **East:** There are two partial building footprints shown using dashed lines. Both are explicitly labeled \"Existing Apartment Building\". There are also structures labeled \"Existing Stone Retaining Wall\" and \"Existing Rock Rubble\" shown on this adjacent eastern property.\n*   **North, South, West:** There are no adjacent building footprints visible in these directions. The west shows public roadway infrastructure (pavement, manholes, curb/gutter) rather than adjacent buildings.\n\n**(4) Are there any notes about adjacent properties?**\nYes, there are several notes and callouts regarding adjacent properties:\n*   **Property/Deed References:** \n    *   East: \"Vol. 73, Pg. 76 P.R.T.C.Tx.\"\n    *   South: \"Vol. 69, Pg. 14 F.R.T.C.Tx.\"\n*   **Easements:** Adjacent property easements are noted, such as a \"25' Drainage Easement\" and \"30' Water/Wastewater Easement\" to the East, and a \"5' Elec. Easement\" (Vol. 69, Pg. 14) and \"5' Elec. & Tele. Easement\" (Vol. 5068, Pg. 883) to the South.\n*   **Construction/Tie-in Notes:** There are callouts indicating where proposed site walls will interact with existing adjacent structures. For example, pointing to the south property line: \"Begin Concrete Retaining Wall at Existing Concrete Retaining Wall\" and \"Tie to Existing Concrete Retaining Wall\". Along the eastern boundary, there are notes stating \"Existing Retaining Wall to be Replaced\".\n\n**(5) What is clearly shown on the perimeter of this site plan regarding adjacent areas?**\n*   **What is clearly visible:** \n    *   To the **West**, the physical connection to the public right-of-way is detailed, including the \"Edge of Pavement\", proposed \"Construct 5' Concrete Sidewalk\", \"Construct Type III Driveway\", \"Wastewater Service Connection\", and an \"Existing Water Manhole\". \n    *   To the **East**, the plan clearly delineates dashed building footprints (\"Existing Apartment Building\"), existing physical features (\"Existing Rock Rubble\", \"Existing Stone Retaining Wall\"), specific easements, lot names (\"Chateaux Ridge Condominiums\"), and zoning (\"Zoning: MF-2-CO\").\n    *   To the **South**, the property boundary lines, subdivision name (\"William James Condos, Jr.\"), deed recording information, electrical easements, and retaining wall tie-in locations are clearly shown.\n    *   To the **North**, \"Existing Water Line\" infrastructure, a manhole, and zoning/deed reference text are visible just outside the property line.\n*   **What is NOT visible:** \n    *   There are no building footprints shown for adjacent properties to the North, South, or West. \n    *   There are no zoning labels provided for the properties to the South or West. \n    *   There is no broader context map or detailed topographic survey shown extending deep into the adjacent lots (the drawing cuts off shortly past the property boundaries).","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1419,"outputTokens":1004,"totalTokens":4986,"reasoningTokens":2563},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 2702484]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just because you do not find evidence for a requirement on this page does not mean it will not be present on another page.\n\nReport back precisely on what you see, using exact quotes for any text you transcribe from forms, tables, or labels.\n\nThe final review agent will not be able to look at this document directly, so you must be their eyes. Ensure you describe everything relevant in full detail with perfect accuracy.\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Review Sheet 9 (Site Plan) and identify: (1) Are there any notations showing adjacent land uses (what uses are on adjacent properties to the north, south, east, west)? (2) Are there any labels or callouts indicating adjacent zoning districts? (3) Are there any building footprints or structures shown from adjacent properties? (4) Are there any notes about adjacent properties? (5) What is clearly shown on the perimeter of this site plan regarding adjacent areas? Be specific about what you can and cannot see."}]}],"headers":{"user-agent":"ai/5.0.152"}}},"response":{"id":"aitxt-vgVz46QGJDlaL5LJBb6VrmnH","timestamp":{},"modelId":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","headers":{"access-control-allow-headers":"Content-Type, Authorization, ai-gateway-auth-method, ai-gateway-protocol-version, ai-model-id, ai-language-model-id, ai-language-model-specification-version, ai-image-model-specification-version, ai-embedding-model-specification-version, ai-language-model-streaming, ai-reporting-tags, ai-reporting-user, http-referer, x-title, anthropic-beta","access-control-allow-methods":"GET, POST, PUT, PATCH, DELETE, OPTIONS","access-control-allow-origin":"*","cache-control":"public, max-age=0, must-revalidate","content-encoding":"br","content-type":"application/json","da