{"level":30,"time":1776973805847,"pid":123,"hostname":"844f2260-bff","step":"review-runs","item":"32.md","index":7,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014uDEZnu6bKd7RYy2JYCscE","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# PARD / Planning & Design Review\n     2→\n     3→*Details the pending parkland dedication fee amount required prior to the issuance of the certificate of occupancy.*\n     4→\n     5→PARD / Planning & Design Review – Suzannah DesRoches suzannah.desroches@austintexas.gov\n     6→\n     7→FYI: If the number of dwelling units changes before payment is made, before the site plan is approved or after it is approved, it is the applicant's responsibility to notify PARD and the case manager in order to have the cost estimate revised. The note on the coversheet must also reflect the correct number of dwelling units paid for and be consistent with all other site plan sheets.\n     8→\n     9→PR1 – Current Status: Pending\n    10→* U1: Thank you for confirming the unit count of 39 multifamily units. The parkland dedication fee owed is $177,244.24. The fee must be paid prior to the issuance of certificate of occupancy (§25-1-609 (B)) for this development in the URBAN geographic area. [This comment will be cleared prior to SP approval]. Please contact this reviewer with any questions about fee amounts, the time of payment, or if there are any changes to the final [unit/hotel/motel key] count. Please confirm receipt of fee amount.\n    11→\n    12→PR2 – Current Status: Cleared\n    13→* U1: Thank you for providing cover sheet note referencing payment for 39 units.\n    14→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c1ccbdc1-20f6-4e62-a4c2-17685db82f6f","uuid":"dba597c2-9397-4a2d-b21a-e92a8945cd91","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/vercel/sandbox/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/supplementary-docs/master-comment-report/08-pard-planning-design-review.md","content":"# PARD / Planning & Design Review\n\n*Details the pending parkland dedication fee amount required prior to the issuance of the certificate of occupancy.*\n\nPARD / Planning & Design Review – Suzannah DesRoches suzannah.desroches@austintexas.gov\n\nFYI: If the number of dwelling units changes before payment is made, before the site plan is approved or after it is approved, it is the applicant's responsibility to notify PARD and the case manager in order to have the cost estimate revised. The note on the coversheet must also reflect the correct number of dwelling units paid for and be consistent with all other site plan sheets.\n\nPR1 – Current Status: Pending\n* U1: Thank you for confirming the unit count of 39 multifamily units. The parkland dedication fee owed is $177,244.24. The fee must be paid prior to the issuance of certificate of occupancy (§25-1-609 (B)) for this development in the URBAN geographic area. [This comment will be cleared prior to SP approval]. Please contact this reviewer with any questions about fee amounts, the time of payment, or if there are any changes to the final [unit/hotel/motel key] count. Please confirm receipt of fee amount.\n\nPR2 – Current Status: Cleared\n* U1: Thank you for providing cover sheet note referencing payment for 39 units.\n","numLines":14,"startLine":1,"totalLines":14}}}
