{"level":30,"time":1776973815098,"pid":123,"hostname":"844f2260-bff","step":"review-runs","item":"32.md","index":1,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01LsUjjdix2ZSVK62HjDEjQS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Excellent! I found critical information:\n\n**Block 5 (Sheet 9), Note c states:**\n\"All signs must comply with requirements of the Land Development Code (Chapter 25-10).\"\n\n**Sheet 3, Block 12, Note 3 states:**\n\"All signs must comply with the requirements of the Land Development Code.(Chapter 25-10)\"\n\nSo the site plan DOES include the general sign compliance note required by ZLU-32.44. Good.\n\nHowever, I notice that:\n1. There is NO mention of Article 10 Compatibility Standards on the site plan\n2. There is NO mention of Nonconforming Signs Ordinance area requirements (ZLU-32.47) - just general Chapter 25-10 compliance\n3. The height allowed on Sheet 9 is 40 feet for all buildings, which aligns with base MF-2 zoning, not with the Article 10 40-foot limit within 50 feet of SF-3 (which would also be 40 feet)\n\nNow let me systematically go through the checklist items:\n\n**Step 1: Identify which items apply**\n\nFrom my analysis:\n1. **NOT APPLICABLE (N/A):** DDBP, DMU, TOD, UNO, WO, ETOD, PUD, MUD, ERC, CS-MU-V, Community Recreation, Townhouse, ADU/civic, Condominium, Group D expansion, Vesting rights, etc.\n\n2. **APPLICABLE - ARTICLE 10 COMPATIBILITY STANDARDS:**\n   - Site is MF-2 (less restrictive than MF-4, so Article 10 applies)\n   - Adjacent to SF-3 (triggering property within 75 ft)\n   - Therefore: ZLU-32.21, ZLU-32.22, ZLU-32.24, ZLU-32.26, ZLU-32.28, ZLU-32.29\n   \n3. **APPLICABLE - OTHER:**\n   - ZLU-32.20: Neighborhood plan statement (South Lamar is suspended) → N/A\n   - ZLU-32.23: GO/LR/CS/CS-1 exterior lighting (site is MF-2) → N/A\n   - ZLU-32.35: Multifamily transit proximity requirements under § 25-1-703 apply here\n   - ZLU-32.36: Tenant notification requirements for demolition or displacement\n   - ZLU-32.38-39: Redevelopment exception provisions may be relevant\n   - ZLU-32.40: Trip generation limits\n   - ZLU-32.43: Accommodation letter needed\n   - ZLU-32.44: General sign compliance note → PASS (documented on Sheet 9 and Sheet 3)\n   - ZLU-32.46: Scenic Roadway signage requirements\n   - ZLU-32.47: Nonconforming Signs Ordinance area compliance\n\n**Critical Items Requiring Verification:**\n\n1. **ZLU-32.21 & ZLU-32.22:** Article 10 compatibility standards appear absent from the site plan submittal. The application indicates \"No\" for compatibility standards, with no supporting notes on the cover sheet or plan sheets. This represents a potential compliance gap that needs clarification.\n\n2. **ZLU-32.35:** Must verify whether the site falls within ½ mile of available public transit service.\n\n3. **ZLU-32.36:** Need to determine if any demolition is planned and whether tenant notification obligations would be triggered.\n\n4. **ZLU-32.47:** The site sits within a Nonconforming Signs area, but the notation only references Chapter 25-10 compliance. Should verify whether this adequately addresses the specific nonconforming signs requirements for this area.\n\n5. **ZLU-32.31:** The proposal describes \"39 multi-family townhome units\" - must clarify whether this constitutes \"townhouse use\" under § 25-2-775, which would require each unit to occupy a separate lot, or if it's simply townhome-style construction.\n\n6. **ZLU-32.24, 32.26, 32.28:** These depend on what on-site amenities are actually proposed.\n\nNeed to examine the site plan more closely for amenity details and check transit accessibility to the site.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":13,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5257,"cache_read_input_tokens":61101,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":5257,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":6,"service