{"level":30,"time":1776973822018,"pid":123,"hostname":"844f2260-bff","step":"review-runs","item":"15.md","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":21,"prompt":"Examine the electrical design plan carefully. Look for:\n\n1. Location and exact placement of all transformer pad(s) on the site\n2. Any dimensions or measurements showing clearances from the transformer pad to buildings, structures, parking areas, or other features\n3. Clearance annotations (such as \"10 ft,\" \"12 ft,\" \"5 ft,\" etc.) near transformer locations\n4. Any notes referencing Austin Energy Design Criteria, transformer clearance standards, or specific clearance distances\n5. Building construction materials (wood, masonry, etc.) that would affect transformer clearance requirements\n6. The exact distance from each transformer pad to the nearest building\n\nProvide specific details about transformer pad locations and whether clearances are labeled or dimensioned on the plans.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a careful visual analysis of the provided \"Preliminary Electrical Design Plan\" for Valley View Townhomes, here are the findings regarding your specific requirements:\n\n**1. Location and exact placement of all transformer pad(s) on the site:**\nThere are five locations specifically labeled \"**Electrical Transformer Pad**\" on this plan sheet. They are indicated by dashed rectangular boxes connected to the blue electrical line routing. Their locations are:\n*   **Pad 1:** Located on the western side of the site, just west of Bldg. 1 (near Unit 101).\n*   **Pad 2:** Located on the western side of the site, south of Pad 1, just west of Bldg. 2 (near Unit 201).\n*   **Pad 3:** Located in the southwest corner of the site, west of Bldg. 8 (near Unit 801).\n*   **Pad 4:** Located in the central portion of the site, situated between Bldg. 2 (east of Unit 204) and Bldg. 4/Bldg. 5 (west of Units 404/504).\n*   **Pad 5:** Located in the south-central portion of the site, situated between Bldg. 7 (north of Unit 704) and Bldg. 6 (south of Unit 601).\n\n**2. Dimensions or measurements showing clearances:**\nThere are **no** dimension lines or measurements indicating clearances from any of the transformer pads to buildings, structures, parking areas, or other features.\n\n**3. Clearance annotations:**\nThere are **no** text annotations specifying clearance distances (such as \"10 ft,\" \"12 ft,\" \"5 ft,\" etc.) near any of the transformer locations. The only text pointing to these boxes is \"Electrical Transformer Pad\".\n\n**4. Notes referencing Austin Energy Design Criteria or clearance standards:**\nThere are **no** notes on this document referencing Austin Energy Design Criteria, transformer clearance standards, or specific clearance distances. The \"Utility Notes\" section (items 1-4) primarily addresses horizontal/vertical verification of utilities and specifications for private domestic water and wastewater branches (referencing Detail 520-AW-01B and 520-AW-01C).\n\n**5. Building construction materials:**\nThere are **no** labels or annotations indicating the construction materials (e.g., wood, masonry, non-combustible) of the buildings. Buildings are only labeled by building number (e.g., \"Bldg. 1\"), unit numbers, square footage, and FFE (Finished Floor Elevation).\n\n**6. Exact distance from each transformer pad to the nearest building:**\nBecause there are no dimension lines provided between the transformer pads and the adjacent buildings, the exact distances are **not provided** on this specific plan sheet.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1462,"outputTokens":602,"totalTokens":4268,"reasoningTokens":2204},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 2092056]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are ana