the site, situated between Bldg. 7 (north of Unit 704) and Bldg. 6 (south of Unit 601).\n\n**2. Dimensions or measurements showing clearances:**\nThere are **no** dimension lines or measurements indicating clearances from any of the transformer pads to buildings, structures, parking areas, or other features.\n\n**3. Clearance annotations:**\nThere are **no** text annotations specifying clearance distances (such as \"10 ft,\" \"12 ft,\" \"5 ft,\" etc.) near any of the transformer locations. The only text pointing to these boxes is \"Electrical Transformer Pad\".\n\n**4. Notes referencing Austin Energy Design Criteria or clearance standards:**\nThere are **no** notes on this document referencing Austin Energy Design Criteria, transformer clearance standards, or specific clearance distances. The \"Utility Notes\" section (items 1-4) primarily addresses horizontal/vertical verification of utilities and specifications for private domestic water and wastewater branches (referencing Detail 520-AW-01B and 520-AW-01C).\n\n**5. Building construction materials:**\nThere are **no** labels or annotations indicating the construction materials (e.g., wood, masonry, non-combustible) of the buildings. Buildings are only labeled by building number (e.g., \"Bldg. 1\"), unit numbers, square footage, and FFE (Finished Floor Elevation).\n\n**6. Exact distance from each transformer pad to the nearest building:**\nBecause there are no dimension lines provided between the transformer pads and the adjacent buildings, the exact distances are **not provided** on this specific plan sheet."}]}
{"level":30,"time":1776973823539,"pid":123,"hostname":"844f2260-bff","step":"review-runs","item":"32.md","index":1,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01YLefdQj2GaqhLQaL6usCer","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good. The landscape plan shows that the site includes landscaped common open spaces (H.5 per the key notes). This means there are common open spaces/amenities on the site. These would be \"amenities available exclusively to residents or occupants\" under ZLU-32.24.\n\nNow I need to:\n1. Check the distance of these amenities from the SF-3 triggering property\n2. Check for transit proximity (ZLU-32.35)\n3. Determine if demolition is proposed and if tenant notification is required (ZLU-32.36)\n4. Check the redevelopment exception status (ZLU-32.38-39)\n\nFrom the engineer's summary letter and facts, I know:\n- Demolition is NOT mentioned for this project (facts say \"existing assisted living / nursing care facility; demolished June 2022\") - the site is NOW vacant. So NO active demolition with tenant displacement for THIS project.\n- Redevelopment exception: Need to check if claimed. The site is in Urban watershed with 65% existing IC and 59-60% proposed, so it's reducing IC. May not need redevelopment exception.\n\nNow let me look at the master comment report to see what the city reviewers have noted about compliance issues.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":13,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1872,"cache_read_input_tokens":69943,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1872,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"38ff40a3-baa1-4588-8a44-429884d301ed","uuid":"034896af-1d81-452a-b165-d0e3d7337c5a"}
