{"level":30,"time":1776973830671,"pid":123,"hostname":"844f2260-bff","step":"review-runs","item":"15.md","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01PtCPDYKq8EhAfr7ioZJWup","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_013RLXyXuvFNuFqo6Us7JqfT","name":"mcp__conductor_tools__vision","input":{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":4,"prompt":"Examine the existing conditions survey carefully. Look for and describe:\n\n1. Any recorded setback lines or building restriction lines shown on the plat or survey\n2. All easements labeled on the survey (including widths and directions) - particularly focus on easements mentioned in the facts.md like the greenbelt easement, drainage easement, and any setback lines\n3. The location of the \"5' Public Utility Easement\" and \"25' Drainage Easement\" if shown\n4. Any notes or dimensions indicating restricted building or setback areas\n5. Whether the property lines are clearly dimensioned and labeled\n6. The orientation and layout relative to Valley View Road\n\nProvide specific information about what easements and restrictions are and are not visible on this survey."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":12,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1156,"cache_read_input_tokens":60273,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1156,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"33f519bd-bced-4a7a-aae5-831dbf134acc","uuid":"64b264fc-2887-44dd-99ac-5ab5c1875ec4"}
{"level":30,"time":1776973831423,"pid":123,"hostname":"844f2260-bff","step":"review-runs","item":"32.md","index":7,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_018reGoV2PMoufwVAs1YfQhK","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Perfect! I found critical information in SP3:\n\n\"SP3 – Current Status: Cleared\n* U1: Multifamily use confirmed. Please let the Case Manager know if you would like to change the project name. Comment cleared. \n* U0: Please confirm that you are proposing Townhouse use. FYI – Townhouses will need to plat a townhouse subdivision as not more than one townhouse is permitted on a townhouse lot. A townhouse lot must include a private yard with a wall or solid fence along a side lot line. \nReference: 25-2-775\"\n\nThis is interesting! The city reviewer asked whether they're proposing \"Townhouse use.\" The response was:\n- The comment is now \"Cleared\"\n- The statement is \"Multifamily use confirmed\"\n\nSo the clarification is that the project is NOT proposing \"Townhouse use\" (which would require separate townhouse lots per § 25-2-775) — it's proposing \"Multifamily use.\" The \"townhome\" terminology is for marketing/branding (project name is \"Valley View Townhomes\"), but the legal use is \"Multi-Family Residential.\"\n\nTherefore, **ZLU-32.31 (Townhouse lots) is NOT APPLICABLE** because the use is Multifamily, not Townhouse.\n\nNow, let me analyze the other applicable items:\n\n1. **ZLU-32.20** (Neighborhood plan statement) — South Lamar NPA is SUSPENDED, so NOT APPLICABLE per applicability condition.\n\n2. **ZLU-32.35** (Multifamily transit proximity) — APPLICABLE. The project is multifamily residential. Per LDC § 25-1-703(B)(4), the project must be within one-half mile walking distance of a public transit route. No comment in the site plan review addresses this requirement. The site plan has not documented that the site is within 1/2 mile of transit, nor has a waiver been provided. \n\nI need to determine if this is a FAIL or NOT-VERIFIABLE. The checklist deficiency states the project is not within one-half mile walking distance of a public transit route per LDC § 25-1-703(B)(4) and no approved waiver from the director has been provided. This appears to be an applicability requirement rather than a design standard, meaning the project either meets the condition or it doesn't—there's no middle ground for verification.\n\nThe applicant should provide documentation showing the site is within 1/2 mile of transit or that a waiver has been approved. I haven't found any such documentation in my review. Looking at the master comment report, there are no comments from the Case Manager or reviewers about transit proximity, which is telling. If the site failed to meet this requirement, it would likely have been flagged. The absence of comments suggests either the site complies with the transit proximity requirement or the requirement was missed during review.\n\nThe project is located at 3759 Valley View Road in South Austin, near Congress Avenue, an area served by MetroRapid and other transit lines. I need to verify this more definitively by checking the project location map on Sheet 1, Block 1 to identify nearby transit routes and confirm whether the site actually falls within the required distance.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":13,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3000,"cache_read_input_tokens":72043,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3000,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c1ccbdc1-20f6-4e62-a4c2-17685db82f6f","uuid":"9e93ee42-15a5-4d9e-a3fa-96874b64d0b3"}
