{"level":30,"time":1776973831741,"pid":123,"hostname":"844f2260-bff","step":"review-runs","item":"15.md","index":9,"runIndex":"run-3","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":9,"prompt":"Examine the main site plan drawing and identify: (1) Are any setback lines drawn and labeled (e.g., zoning setback lines, compatibility buffer lines, property lines, building setback lines)? (2) Are there any notations indicating the distance from buildings to property lines or adjacent properties? (3) Can you identify or estimate the location of the adjacent SF-3 property relative to the site? (4) Are there any notation boxes, legends, or references to compatibility standards, Article 10, or Subchapter F? Please describe what setback or property boundary information is visible on the drawing.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a visual analysis of the provided site plan document, here are the findings corresponding to your questions:\n\n**(1) Are any setback lines drawn and labeled (e.g., zoning setback lines, compatibility buffer lines, property lines, building setback lines)?**\n*   **Property Lines:** The property boundary is drawn using a heavy line weight with a dash-dot pattern, and property corners are marked with small circles indicating survey pins. \n*   **Setback/Compatibility Lines:** I do not see any dashed lines explicitly labeled as \"Building Setback,\" \"Zoning Setback,\" \"Compatibility Setback,\" or \"Compatibility Buffer\" on the main drawing. \n*   **Easement Lines:** There are several labeled dashed lines indicating easements rather than setbacks, such as \"5' P.U.E.\", \"10' P.U.E.\", \"25' Drainage Easement\", and \"Sidewalk Easement\".\n\n**(2) Are there any notations indicating the distance from buildings to property lines or adjacent properties?**\nThere are a few dimension lines that appear to indicate distances from buildings to property boundaries, though they are not explicitly labeled with the word \"setback\":\n*   Near the bottom-left corner of **Bldg. 8**, there is a dimension line labeled **\"28.8'\"** extending from the corner of the building down to the southern property boundary line.\n*   To the right of **Bldg. 6**, there is a dimension line labeled **\"25'\"** extending from the right face of the building to a dashed line near the eastern property boundary.\n*   To the left of **Bldg. 1**, there is a dimension line labeled **\"26.1'\"** extending from the building's top-left corner area toward the curved western property line/right-of-way.\n*   *Note:* There are no explicit dimension lines drawn from the southern edges of Bldg. 7 or Bldg. 6 directly to the southern property boundary.\n\n**(3) Can you identify or estimate the location of the adjacent SF-3 property relative to the site?**\nYes, the adjacent SF-3 property is located immediately to the **south** (along the bottom edge of the drawing). Just outside the bottom central property line, there is faint text identifying the adjacent parcel that reads:\n*   \"William James Estate, Jr.\"\n*   \"Vol. 69, Pg. 14\"\n*   \"F.R.T.C.Tx.\"\n*   **\"Zoning: SF-3\"**\n\n**(4) Are there any notation boxes, legends, or references to compatibility standards, Article 10, or Subchapter F?**\n*   **Compatibility / Article 10 / Subchapter F:** I do not see any notation boxes, legends, or text explicitly referencing \"compatibility standards,\" \"Article 10,\" or \"Subchapter F\".\n*   **Subchapter E:** There is a reference to a different subchapter regarding lighting. In the lower-left quadrant, there is a **\"Lighting Note\"** box that states exactly:\n    > \"All exterior lighting will be full cut-off and fully shielded in compliance with Subchapter E 2.5. All site lighting to be located on the building will be in compliance with Subchapter E 2.5, and will be reviewed during building plan review. Any change or substitution of luminaire/light fixtures shall be submitted to the Director for approval in accordance wit