{"level":30,"time":1776973834579,"pid":123,"hostname":"844f2260-bff","step":"review-runs","item":"32.md","index":1,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BDhRhuCS1CzqJRdrTvcmxZ","type":"tool_result","content":"workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/supplementary-docs/master-comment-report/03-transportation-public-works-tpw-tds-review.md:138:Reference: LDC 25-2-1067(c); TCM, 9.3.0.2"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"38ff40a3-baa1-4588-8a44-429884d301ed","uuid":"78daeb64-9eaf-43cb-8e0f-8c6bef45d446","tool_use_result":{"mode":"content","numFiles":0,"filenames":[],"content":"workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/supplementary-docs/master-comment-report/03-transportation-public-works-tpw-tds-review.md:138:Reference: LDC 25-2-1067(c); TCM, 9.3.0.2","numLines":1}}
{"level":30,"time":1776973834900,"pid":123,"hostname":"844f2260-bff","step":"review-runs","item":"16.md","index":2,"runIndex":"run-1","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":9,"prompt":"Examine the site plan drawing (Block 2) and answer these specific questions:\n\n1. Are adjacent land uses labeled on the site plan for properties on all four sides (north, south, east, west)?\n2. Are adjacent zoning designations shown on the site plan?\n3. Are existing building footprints shown on the site plan for adjacent properties within 50 feet of the site?\n4. Are the proposed building dimensions shown on the plan (width, depth, height)?\n5. Is parking layout clearly shown and labeled? How many surface parking spaces vs garage spaces?\n6. Are there any screening details or notes about screening between the subject site and adjacent properties?\n7. Are perimeter boundary lines clearly shown for all buildings?\n8. Is there any notation about connections to adjacent properties or shared access points?\n\nPlease provide specific observations about what is depicted on the actual site plan drawing.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a detailed visual analysis of the provided site plan document, here are the answers to your specific questions:\n\n**1. Are adjacent land uses labeled on the site plan for properties on all four sides (north, south, east, west)?**\nNo, adjacent land uses are not explicitly labeled with a use type on all four sides.\n*   **East:** Yes. There are clear labels indicating the land use, specifically reading \"Existing Apartment Building\" and \"Clarion Ridge Condominiums\".\n*   **North:** Partially. The zoning is labeled (\"Zoning: MF-4-CO\"), but there is no explicit text stating the general land use (e.g., \"Residential\" or \"Apartments\").\n*   **South:** The area immediately south of the property line is a public right-of-way/street. Across the street, there are faint property lines and text mentioning \"Valley View\" and \"Creek Pointe\", but no specific land use type is labeled.\n*   **West:** There are no explicit land use labels for the property immediately adjacent to the western boundary.\n\n**2. Are adjacent zoning designations shown on the site plan?**\nYes, adjacent zoning designations are shown for some, but not all, surrounding properties.\n*   **North:** The plan explicitly notes **\"Zoning: MF-4-CO\"** just outside the northern property line.\n*   **East:** The plan explicitly notes **\"Zoning: MF-2-CO\"** under the \"Clarion Ridge Condominiums\" label outside the eastern property line.\n*   **South/West:** Zoning designations are not visibly labeled for adjacent properties on the south or west sides within the provided drawing area.\n\n**3. Are existing building footprints shown on the site plan for adjacent properties within 50 feet of the site?**\nYes. On the **eastern** side of the property, there are light gray, dashed outlines depicting building footprints. Several of these footprints are labeled with a leader line pointing to text that reads **\"Existing Apartment Building\"**. These footprints are located immediately adjacent to the property line, clearly within 50 feet of the subject site. No existing footprints are shown on the north, south, or west sides.\n\n**4. Are the proposed building dimensions shown on the plan (width, depth, height)?**\nYes, all three dimensions are provided, though in different locations:\n*   **Width and Depth (Footprint):** These are shown directly on the plan view using dimension lines and text on the building footprints. For example, \"Bldg 1\" shows footprint dimensions of **\"19.3'\"** and **\"78.2'\"**. \"Bldg 2\" shows **\"21.3'\"** and **\"97.8'\"**.\n*   **Height:** Building heights are not listed directly on the building footprints in the plan view. However, they are detailed in the **\"Building Height Table\"** located in the bottom right quadrant of the sheet. This table provides specific height dimensions for every building. For example, Building 1 shows a \"Building Height (FT)\" of **\"35' - 10.75\"\"**, and Building 2 shows **\"33' - 4.75\"\"**.\n\n**5. Is parking layout clearly shown and labeled? How many surface parking spaces vs garage spaces?**\nYes, the parking layout is clearly drawn, showing individual striped surface spaces, hatched ADA aisles, and driveway aprons leading into building garages.\nThe exact counts are explicitly stated in the **\"Parking Data\"** table located on the right side of the sheet, just below the building height table. It reads exactly as follows:\n*   **\"Parking Spaces Provided: 70 Surface/ 78 Garage\"**\n\n**6. Are there any screening details or notes about screening between the subject site and adjacent properties?**\nWhile there is no large text block specifically titled \"Screening,\" the plan does denote physical barriers acting as screening along the perimeters:\n*   **East Boundary:** The plan points to a solid line on the property boundary labeled **\"Wood Fence\"**. It also notes an **\"Existing Retaining Wall to be Replaced\"**.\n*   **North Boundary:** The plan notes a **\"Pond Perimeter Fence\"** and a **\"Concrete Retaining Wall\"**.\n*   Additionally, under the **\"Lighting Note\"** (bottom left), it states: *\"All exterior lighting will be full cut-off and fully shielded in compliance with Subchapter E 2.5. All site lighting to be located on the building will be in compliance with Subchapter E 2.5, and will be reviewed during building plan review.\"* This indicates measures taken to prevent light spillover to adjacent properties.\n\n**7. Are perimeter boundary lines clearly shown for all buildings?**\nYes. Every proposed building (Bldg. 1 through Bldg. 8) has a distinct, solid, dark black outline clearly defining the perimeter footprint of the structure on the site plan.\n\n**8. Is there any notation about connections to adjacent properties or shared access points?**\nNo. There are no notations, drive aisles, or pedestrian pathways indicating shared access or connections to the private adjacent properties to the north, east, or west. All depicted access points (labeled **\"Construct Type II Driveway\"**) connect exclusively to the public street/right-of-way located at the bottom (south) and lower-left (west) of the site plan.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1497,"outputTokens":1152,"totalTokens":5105,"reasoningTokens":2456},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 2702484]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just because you do not find evidence for a requirement on this page does not mean it will not be present on another page.\n\nReport back precisely on what you see, using exact quotes for any text you transcribe from forms, tables, or labels.\n\nThe final review agent will not be able to look at this document directly, so you must be their eyes. Ensure you describe everything relevant in full detail with perfect accuracy.\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Examine the site plan drawing (Block 2) and answer these specific questions:\n\n1. Are adjacent land uses labeled on the site plan for properties on all four sides (north, south, east, west)?\n2. Are adjacent zoning designations shown on the site plan?\n3. Are existing building footprints shown on the site plan for adjacent properties within 50 feet of the site?\n4. Are the proposed building dimensions shown on the plan (width, depth, height)?\n5. Is parking layout clearly shown and labeled? How many surface parking spaces vs garage spaces?\n6. Are there any screening details or notes about screening between the subject site and adjacent properties?\n7. Are perimeter boundary lines clearly shown for all buildings?\n8. Is there any notation about connections to adjacent properties or shared access points?\n\nPlease provide specific observations about what is depicted on the actual site plan drawing."}]}],"headers":{"user-agent":"ai/5.0.152"}}},"response":{"id":"aitxt-HPnZEsFimNgOM8n29Cp85vw8","timestamp":{},"modelId":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","headers":{"access-control-allow-headers":"Content-Type, Authorization, ai-gateway-auth-method, ai-gateway-protocol-version, ai-model-id, ai-language-model-id, ai-language-model-specification-version, ai-image-model-specification-version, ai-embedding-model-specification-version, ai-language-model-streaming, ai-reporting-tags, ai-reporting-user, http-referer, x-title, anthropic-beta","access-control-allow-methods":"GET, POST, PUT, PATCH, DELETE, OPTIONS","access-control-allow-origin":"*","cache-control":"public, max-age=0, must-revalidate","content-encoding":"br","content-type":"application/json","date":"Thu, 23 Apr 2026 19:50:34 GMT","server":"Vercel","strict-transport-security":"max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains; preload","transfer-encoding":"chunked","vary":"rsc, next-router-state-tree, next-router-prefetch, next-router-segment-prefetch","x-matched-path":"/v1/ai/language-model","x-vercel-cache":"MISS","x-vercel-id":"iad1::iad1::pr4ww-1776973775607-dace77d38f69"},"body":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a detailed visual anal