king Spaces Provided: 70 Surface/ 78 Garage\"**\n\n**6. Are there any screening details or notes about screening between the subject site and adjacent properties?**\nWhile there is no large text block specifically titled \"Screening,\" the plan does denote physical barriers acting as screening along the perimeters:\n*   **East Boundary:** The plan points to a solid line on the property boundary labeled **\"Wood Fence\"**. It also notes an **\"Existing Retaining Wall to be Replaced\"**.\n*   **North Boundary:** The plan notes a **\"Pond Perimeter Fence\"** and a **\"Concrete Retaining Wall\"**.\n*   Additionally, under the **\"Lighting Note\"** (bottom left), it states: *\"All exterior lighting will be full cut-off and fully shielded in compliance with Subchapter E 2.5. All site lighting to be located on the building will be in compliance with Subchapter E 2.5, and will be reviewed during building plan review.\"* This indicates measures taken to prevent light spillover to adjacent properties.\n\n**7. Are perimeter boundary lines clearly shown for all buildings?**\nYes. Every proposed building (Bldg. 1 through Bldg. 8) has a distinct, solid, dark black outline clearly defining the perimeter footprint of the structure on the site plan.\n\n**8. Is there any notation about connections to adjacent properties or shared access points?**\nNo. There are no notations, drive aisles, or pedestrian pathways indicating shared access or connections to the private adjacent properties to the north, east, or west. All depicted access points (labeled **\"Construct Type II Driveway\"**) connect exclusively to the public street/right-of-way located at the bottom (south) and lower-left (west) of the site plan.","providerOptions":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}]}]},"providerMetadata":{"google":{"promptFeedback":null,"groundingMetadata":null,"urlContextMetadata":null,"safetyRatings":null,"serviceTier":null},"gateway":{"routing":{"originalModelId":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","resolve