{"level":30,"time":1776973845603,"pid":123,"hostname":"844f2260-bff","step":"review-runs","item":"15.md","index":6,"runIndex":"run-2","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":9,"prompt":"Examine the main site plan drawing and identify: (1) Are setback lines drawn and labeled on the site plan? (2) Are any compatibility buffer lines or \"no-build\" zones shown? (3) Are property lines marked and are they graphically distinct? (4) Are easements shown on the site plan? (5) What is the relationship between buildings and the adjacent properties to the south/east (especially the SF-3 property at 0406100210)?","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a precise visual analysis of the provided site plan document, here are the findings regarding your specific questions:\n\n**(1) Are setback lines drawn and labeled on the site plan?**\nThere are dashed lines running parallel to the interior of the property boundaries, and there are numerous specific dimension lines indicating the exact distance from the buildings to the property lines (e.g., \"25.0'\", \"21.3'\", \"44.2'\", \"46.9'\"). However, there are no text labels explicitly reading \"Setback Line\", \"Building Line\", or \"B.L.\" clearly legible on these specific perimeter lines. \n\n**(2) Are any compatibility buffer lines or \"no-build\" zones shown?**\nNo. There are no lines, hatched areas, or zones explicitly labeled as a \"Compatibility Buffer\" or \"No-Build Zone\" anywhere on the visible site plan.\n\n**(3) Are property lines marked and are they graphically distinct?**\nYes. The property boundary is marked using a graphically distinct, heavy solid line that forms the perimeter of the site. It is clearly annotated with bearing and distance measurements (e.g., the southern boundary is labeled **\"N62° 36' 57\\\"W 414.24'\"** and the top right boundary is labeled **\"N27° 02' 28\\\"E 199.96'\"**).\n\n**(4) Are easements shown on the site plan?**\nYes, numerous easements are drawn with dashed lines and explicitly labeled across the site. Exactly transcribed examples include:\n*   **\"5' P.U.E.\"** (located along the top/northern boundary edge)\n*   **\"10' P.U.E.\"** (located along the bottom/southern boundary edge)\n*   **\"25' Drainage Easement Vol. 73, Pg. 76 P.R.T.C.Tx\"** (top right corner area)\n*   **\"15' Easement Vol. 73, Pg. 76 P.R.T.C.Tx\"** (eastern boundary, center)\n*   **\"25' Drainage Easement Doc. 2013021137 O.P.R.T.C.Tx.\"** (eastern boundary, upper middle)\n*   **\"5' Elec. & Tele. Easement Vol. 5468, Pg. 883 D.R.T.C.Tx.\"** (bottom right corner)\n*   **\"Sidewalk Easement Doc#\"** (multiple instances along the western/left boundary)\n*   **\"Wastewater Easement Doc#\"** (top left corner)\n\n**(5) What is the relationship between buildings and the adjacent properties to the south/east (especially the SF-3 property at 0406100210)?**\n*   **Southern Relationship (SF-3 Property):** The adjacent properties to the south (below the boundary line labeled N62° 36' 57\"W) are explicitly labeled **\"Zoning: SF-3\"** in at least two visible locations. *(Note: The specific parcel number \"0406100210\" is not legibly visible in the faint text).* The buildings closest to this southern SF-3 boundary are **Bldg. 8**, **Bldg. 7**, and **Bldg. 6**. \n    *   There is a dimension line indicating that **Bldg. 8** is set back **\"46.9'\"** from the southern property line. \n    *   **Bldg. 6** (specifically Unit 604) has a dimension line showing it is **\"21.3'\"** from the southern property line.\n    *   The space between these buildings and the southern property line contains a drive aisle/parking area, a **\"Concrete Retaining Wall\"**, and a **\"Wood Fence\"** near the southeastern corner.\n*   **Eastern Relationship:** The adjacent properties to the east are labeled **\"Existing Apartment Building\"** and **\"Zoning: MF-2-CO\"**. The buildings closest to this eastern boundary are **Bldg. 4**, **Bldg. 5**, and **Bldg. 6**.\n    *   Dimension lines indicate distances from these buildings to the eastern property line, specifically: **\"27.3'\"** (from Bldg. 4), **\"21.3'\"** (from Bldg. 5), **\"44.2'\"** (from Bldg. 6, Unit 601), and **\"25'\"** (from Bldg. 6, Unit 602).\n    *   Physical separations noted along this eastern boundary include an **\"Existing Retaining Wall to be Replaced\"**, a **\"Concrete Retaining Wall\"**, and a **\"Wood Fence\"**.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1414,"outputTokens":1068,"totalTokens":5709,"reasoningTokens":3227},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 2702484]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just because you do not find evidence for a requirement on this page does not mean it will not be present on another page.\n\nReport back precisely on what you see, using exact quotes for any text you transcribe from forms, tables, or labels.\n\nThe final review agent will not be able to look at this document directly, so you must be their eyes. Ensure you describe everything relevant in full detail with perfect accuracy.\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Examine the main 