um and minimum depth of channel\n  - Manning's \"n\" values\nReference: DCM Section 6; DCM Table 6-2\n\nDE 11 – Current Status: Pending\n* U1: Comment remains.\n* U0: No public storm drain system should be allowed to go through an inlet box. However, a stub out from one or two lots in a commercial subdivision can be tied into an existing inlet if it does not impede the function of the inlet and if the laterals and overflow provisions contain the capacity to convey the additional flows. Please demonstrate compliance.\nReference: DCM 5.2.0(H)\n\nDE 12 – Current Status: Pending\n* U1: Comment pending. We still need an analysis of the existing channel on the site. If you are planning to discharge to it, we will need to ensure it has capacity. Please note that your outfall is within an electrical easement. You will need to provide approval from the easements’ owner to do this. Please note the intent of this code is also to cause no adverse impact to your neighbors.\n* U0: If the development is located within 550 feet of an existing storm system, the developer shall provide all the necessary infrastructure required to connect to that system. If there is no existing storm sewer, the outlet design shall provide for a change in the discharge pattern from concentrated flow back to sheet flow.\nReference: DCM 1.2.3(C)\n\nDE 13 – Current Status: Pending\n* U1: Provide additional bottom of wall, or toe of bank elevations to verify the pond does not exceed 6’. For instance, the red X below appears to have a 6 ft difference.\n\n[Figure: Cross-section detail of a detention pond structure showing a wall with TW 677.50, FG 672.00, and a 6\" PVC discharge pipe at 1.00% slope onto a 3' x 4' concrete splash pad]\n\n* U0: Any hydraulic structure designed to impound storm water that has a height greater than 6 feet at any point along the perimeter of the SWM pond is a dam. The height of the hydraulic structure (dam) is measured from the top of the structure to the downstream intersection of the structure and the natural or excavated ground, whichever is lower. Provide additional top of wall, bottom of wall, or toe of bank elevations to verify the pond does not exceed 6’.\nReference: DCM 8.3.3(B)\n\nDE 14 – Current Status: Pending\n* U1: Comment pending more verification.\n* U0: Dams must be designed to pass the minimum design flood hydrograph which is the greater of:\n  a) 75% of the PMF; or\n  b) The percentage of the PMF as defined in Texas Administrative Code Chapter 299 Dams and Reservoirs (Figure: 30 TAC § 299.15(a)(1)(A)).\nReference: DCM 8.3.3(B)(3)\n\nDE 15 – Current Status: Pending\n* U1: Comment pending more verification.\n* U0: Adequate design of the dam is evidenced by certification using the statement provided in DCM 8.3.3.B.3 by an engineer licensed in the State of Texas. The certification statement may be divided into the four disciplines of hydrology, hydraulics, structural and geotechnical and independently certified. Please add the following Dam Safety Certification Statement to the cover sheet: “I [name of professional engineer] Texas license number [number] certify that the design of the dam in this set of plans can safely pass the minimum design flood hydrograph as required by the City of Austin and the State of Texas based on the hydrologic, hydraulic, structural and geotechnical analysis using standard accepted engineering practices.”\nReference: DCM 8.3.3(B)\n\nDE 16 – Current Status: Pending\n* U1: Comment pending more verification.\n* U0: SWM ponds that are considered dams as defined in the Drainage Criteria Manual may not be designed or constructed with any trees or other woody vegetation on the dam structure or within 20-feet of the upstream or downstream toe of the dam. This 20-foot clear zone must be called out on the site plan and for City maintained facilities must be part of the drainage easement dedicated for the dam facility. The toe of the dam is the junction of the constructed dam structure with the natural ground. Please Demonstrate compliance.\nReference: DCM 8.3.3(B)(5)\n\nDE 17 – Current Status: Cleared\n* U1: Comment cleared.\n* U0: Provide details of the detention pond outlet structure. Please show the elevations for the 2-, 10-, 25-, and 100-year storm events in the detention outlet structure detail.","numLines":100,"startLine":1,"totalLines":127}}}
{"level":30,"time":1776973850626,"pid":123,"hostname":"844f2260-bff","step":"review-runs","item":"32.md","index":7,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01H49LpM4px8dD1gbukHMerQ","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Land Use, Waivers, and Arborist Review\n     2→\n     3→*Details compatibility standards, requested waivers or variances, and tree counts within and adjacent to the limits of construction.*\n     4→\n     5→Section 10: Land Use Site Plan Data - as applicable\n     6→Subject to Compatibility Standards? [ ] Yes [x] No\n     7→In Combining District/Overlay Zone? (NCCD, CVC, WO, AO, etc.): [ ] Yes [x] No\n     8→If Yes, please specify: \n     9→Requires a Green Building Program Rating? [ ] Yes [x] No (If Yes, attach Letter of Intent)\n    10→\n    11→Section 11: Waiver / Variance / Etc. - as applicable\n    12→[ ] Compatibility Standards Waiver – Code Section(s): \n    13→[ ] Board of Adjustments Variance – Case Number(s): \n    14→[ ] Driveway Spacing – Code Section(s): \n    15→[ ] Hill Country – Code Section(s): \n    16→[ ] Waterfront Overlay District – Code Section(s): \n    17→[ ] Environmental – Code Section(s): \n    18→[ ] Shared Parking Analysis [ ] Off-Site or Remote Parking\n    19→[ ] Detention Pond Waiver [ ] Alternative Landscape Compliance\n    20→\n    21→Section 12: City Arborist Review\n    22→Has there been an onsite consultation with a City Arborist? [ ] Yes [ ] No\n    23→(If yes, please include all consultation correspondence and supporting documentation.)\n    24→Consultation – Tree Permit Number: \n    25→Will you be requesting a tree variance? [ ] Yes [x] No\n    26→For commercial site-plan applications, count trees within and adjacent to the limits of construction:\n    27→• Number of trees with a diameter of 8 in. or greater located within the Limits of Construction (LOC):\n    28→40\n    29→• Number of trees with a diameter of 8 in. or greater located immediately adjacent to the LOC:\n    30→7\n    31→• Total number of trees with a diameter of 8 in. or greater:\n    32→47\n    33→\n    34→City of Austin | Consolidated Site Plan Completeness Check Application 10/21/24 | Page 6 of 8\n    35→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c1ccbdc1-20f6-4e62-a4c2-17685db82f6f","uuid":"be35c3eb-b2bd-4833-bdcf-fe1b83e7dcd1","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/vercel/sandbox/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/supplementary-docs/consolidated-site-plan-application/05-land-use-waivers-and-arborist-review.md","content":"# Land Use, Waivers, and Arborist Review\n\n*Details compatibility standards, requested waivers or variances, and tree counts within and adjacent to the limits of construction.*\n\nSection 10: Land Use Site Plan Data - as applicable\nSubject to Compatibility Standards? [ ] Yes [x] No\nIn Combining District/Overlay Zone? (NCCD, CVC, WO, AO, etc.): [ ] Yes [x] No\nIf Yes, please specify: \nRequires a Green Building Program Rating? [ ] Yes [x] No (If Yes, attach Letter of Intent)\n\nSection 11: Waiver / Variance / Etc. - as applicable\n[ ] Compatibility Standards Waiver – Code Section(s): \n[ ] Board of Adjustments Variance – Case Number(s): \n[ ] Driveway Spacing – Code Section(s): \n[ ] Hill Country – Code Section(s): \n[ ] Waterfront Overlay District – Code Section(s): \n[ ] Environmental – Code Section(s): \n[ ] Shared Parking Analysis [ ] Off-Site or Remote Parking\n[ ] Detention Pond Waiver [ ] Alternative Landscape Compliance\n\nSection 12: City Arborist Review\nHas there been an onsite consultation with a City Arborist? [ ] Yes [ ] No\n(If yes, please include all consultation correspondence and supporting documentation.)\nConsultation – Tree Permit Number: \nWill you be requesting a tree variance? [ ] Yes [x] No\nFor commercial site-plan applications, count trees within and adjacent to the limits of construction:\n• Number of trees with a diameter of 8 in. or greater located within the Limits of Construction (LOC):\n40\n• Number of trees with a diameter of 8 in. or greater located immediately adjacent to the LOC:\n7\n• Total number of trees with a diameter of 8 in. or greater:\n47\n\nCity of Austin | Consolidated Site Plan Completeness Check Application 10/21/24 | Page 6 of 8\n","numLines":35,"startLine":1,"totalLines":35}}}
{"level":30,"time":1776973855175,"pid":123,"hostname":"844f2260-bff","step":"review-runs","item":"15.md","index":9,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01TyDCacW5tCR5rHEXRxPhSF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good. The form confirms that the current Land Development Code applies, which means the new Article 10 (effective July 15, 2024) would apply since the site plan was submitted May 20, 2025.\n\nNow I have enough information to start identifying the deficiencies. Let me compile what I've found:\n\n**KEY FACTS:**\n1. Site is zoned MF-2 (less restrictive than MF-4, so Article 10 could apply)\n2. Adjacent SF-3 parcel immediately to the south (shares property line)\n3. Buildings are 25-28.8 feet from the southern property line (well within 75-ft Article 10 trigger)\n4. Site plan submitted May 20, 2025 (after July 15, 2024 Article 10 effective date)\n5. Applicant claims site is NOT subject to compatibility standards (which is incorrect)\n6. No compatibility setback lines are shown on plans\n7. No separate compatibility exhibit provided\n8. No cross-sections showing distances and heights\n9. No references to Article 10 on the plans\n\n**CHECKLIST ITEMS TO EVALUATE:**\n\nLet me go through the checklist systematically:\n\n**ZLU-15.1 (Zoning District Setback Lines):** Need to check if basic MF-2 setback lines are shown and labeled. From vision analysis, I saw some distances (28.8', 25', 26.1') but the vision tool stated \"I do not see any dashed lines explicitly labeled as 'Building Setback,' 'Zoning Setback,'\" - so these appear to be present as dimensions but NOT clearly labeled as setback lines.\n\n**ZLU-15.2 (Zoning District Setback Distances Maintained):** Need to verify the MF-2 setback requirements against actual building positions. I need to know what the MF-2 minimum setbacks are.\n\n**ZLU-15.7 (Compatibility Standards Applicability Incorrectly Determined):** FAIL - The applicant incorrectly determined that compatibility standards don't apply. \n\nAll four triggering conditions are met: the site is zoned MF-2 (less restrictive than MF-4), an SF-3 parcel is adjacent, buildings fall within the 75-foot proximity threshold at 25-28.8 feet, and SF-3 is a qualifying zone under the regulation.\n\n**ZLU-15.10 (Compatibility Buffer Not Shown at Correct Width):** FAIL or NOT-VERIFIABLE - No compatibility buffer is shown on the plans.\n\n**ZLU-15.26 (Separate Compatibility Exhibit Not Provided):** FAIL or NOT-VERIFIABLE - No separate compatibility exhibit has been submitted.\n\n**ZLU-15.27 (Compatibility Cross-Sections Not Provided):** FAIL or NOT-VERIFIABLE - No cross-sections showing distances and heights are present.\n\nI should verify the SF-3 property actually qualifies—it needs 1-3 dwelling units. Since SF-3 is single-family zoning, it's limited to one dwelling unit per lot by definition, which satisfies the requirement. The adjacent SF-3 parcel is immediately south of the property line, confirming it's well within the 75-foot distance.\n\nArticle 10 applies here. To assess the MF-2 setback compliance, I'd need to reference LDC § 25-2-492, which establishes minimum setbacks for all base zoning districts, though the specific MF-2 values aren't detailed in the grouping document itself. What the vision analysis does show is that the buildings are positioned 25-28.8 feet from the property line.\n\nThe issue is that these distance measurements aren't identified as setback compliance lines on the plans—they're just dimensional notations. This means I can identify a deficiency under ZLU-15.1: the required zoning district setback lines lack clear labeling and identification. Now I'll organize my findings.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":11,"cache_creation_input_tokens":893,"cache_read_input_tokens":67572,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":893,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d203a61d-b956-4bf7-a62f-71a0e7d71a2a","uuid":"6ee0faf3-f589-4593-91bf-1933d94a4ec0"}
