{"level":30,"time":1776973860784,"pid":123,"hostname":"844f2260-bff","step":"review-runs","item":"15.md","index":9,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01TyDCacW5tCR5rHEXRxPhSF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_017AfakHnABqA36A5YYmnfeG","name":"mcp__conductor_tools__run_measure_distance","input":{"reasoning":"The site plan shows buildings positioned near the southern property boundary adjacent to the SF-3 zoned parcel. Under Article 10 (LDC § 25-2-1051), compatibility standards apply when a site is zoned MF-4 or less restrictive (MF-2 qualifies) AND located within 75 feet of a triggering property (1-3 dwelling units + SF-5 or more restrictive zoning). SF-3 is a qualifying triggering property zone. The vision analysis showed buildings at 25-28.8 feet from the property line. This measurement will confirm whether Article 10 is triggered and whether the site needs a compatibility buffer and height restrictions per § 25-2-1061 and § 25-2-1062.","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":9,"scaleInchesPerFoot":0.05,"objectPairs":[{"objectA":"southern property line shared with SF-3 parcel (William James Estate)","objectB":"nearest building corner (Building 8 southeast corner)"},{"objectA":"southern property line shared with SF-3 parcel","objectB":"nearest building corner (Building 6 southeast corner)"}],"applicable_checklist_items":[{"checklist_id":"ZLU-15.7","checklist_deficiency_text":"Compatibility standards (Article 10) applicability incorrectly determined: Article 10 applies when a site is zoned MF-4 or less restrictive AND is located within 75 feet of a triggering property; a triggering property is a site with 1–3 dwelling units zoned SF-5 or more restrictive (LA, RR, SF-1, SF-2, SF-3, SF-4A, SF-4B, or SF-5)"},{"checklist_id":"ZLU-15.10","checklist_deficiency_text":"Compatibility buffer not shown at the correct width along the shared triggering property line: the required buffer is 25 feet wide (standard) or 15 feet wide if the development site is less than 75 feet wide measured from the shared triggering property line"},{"checklist_id":"ZLU-15.27","checklist_deficiency_text":"Compatibility cross-sections not provided or incomplete: cross-sections must show the triggering property boundary, distance measurements from the triggering property boundary to proposed structures at the 50-ft and 75-ft thresholds, proposed building heights at each distance band, and elevation of the triggering property grade"}]},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":11,"cache_creation_input_tokens":893,"cache_read_input_tokens":67572,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":893,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d203a61d-b956-4bf7-a62f-71a0e7d71a2a","uuid":"7e5fcb84-e0bf-48df-a406-5a6c07bfb0e8"}
{"level":30,"time":1776973860804,"pid":123,"hostname":"844f2260-bff","step":"review-runs","item":"15.md","index":9,"runIndex":"run-3","tool":"run_measure_distance","command":"npx tsx /vercel/sandbox/workspace/bureau/jurisdictions/austin/workflows/review/scripts/measure-distance.ts --outputPath='/vercel/sandbox/workspace/output/measure-distance.json' --reasoning='The site plan shows buildings positioned near the southern property boundary adjacent to the SF-3 zoned parcel. Under Article 10 (LDC § 25-2-1051), compatibility standards apply when a site is zoned MF-4 or less restrictive (MF-2 qualifies) AND located within 75 feet of a triggering property (1-3 dwelling units + SF-5 or more restrictive zoning). SF-3 is a qualifying triggering property zone. The vision analysis showed buildings at 25-28.8 feet from the property line. This measurement will confirm whether Article 10 is triggered and whether the site needs a compatibility buffer and height restrictions per § 25-2-1061 and § 25-2-1062.' --applicable_checklist_items='[{\"checklist_id\":\"ZLU-15.7\",\"checklist_deficiency_text\":\"Compatibility standards (Article 10) applicability incorrectly determined: Article 10 applies when a site is zoned MF-4 or less restrictive AND is located within 75 feet of a triggering property; a triggering property is a site with 1–3 dwelling units zoned SF-5 or more restrictive (LA, RR, SF-1, SF-2, SF-3, SF-4A, SF-4B, or SF-5)\"},{\"checklist_id\":\"ZLU-15.10\",\"checklist_deficiency_text\":\"Compatibility buffer not shown at the correct width along the shared triggering property line: the required buffer is 25 feet wide (standard) or 15 feet wide if the development site is less than 75 feet wide measured from the shared triggering property line\"},{\"checklist_id\":\"ZLU-15.27\",\"checklist_deficiency_text\":\"Compatibility cross-sections not provided or incomplete: cross-sections must show the triggering property boundary, distance measurements from the triggering property boundary to proposed structures at the 50-ft and 75-ft thresholds, proposed building heights at each distance band, and elevation of the triggering property grade\"}]' --documentId='1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777' --sheetNum='9' --objectPairs='[{\"objectA\":\"southern property line shared with SF-3 parcel (William James Estate)\",\"objectB\":\"nearest building corner (Building 8 southeast corner)\"},{\"objectA\":\"southern property line shared with SF-3 parcel\",\"objectB\":\"nearest building corner (Building 6 southeast corner)\"}]' --scaleInchesPerFoot='0.05'","msg":"Executing typed script tool"}
{"level":30,"time":1776973948996,"pid":123,"hostname":"844f2260-bff","step":"review-runs","item":"32.md","index":7,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01UnHMAjnMj8a25RcysEBLhG","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"From the Waivers document, I see:\n- \"Subject to Compatibility Standards? [ ] Yes [x] No\" — This confirms Article 10 or other compatibility standards are NOT applicable.\n- No waivers/variances requested for compatibility standards or other items related to ZLU-32.\n\nThe drainage review shows various pending items, but nothing related to transit proximity (which would be LDC § 25-1-703, not drainage-related).\n\nI notice that NO reviewer in the Master Comment Report has specifically commented on the multifamily transit proximity requirement (ZLU-32.35). This is significant. If the site were NOT within 1/2 mile of transit and no waiver were approved, the site plan reviewers (especially the Case Manager) would flag this as a requirement not met.\n\nThe absence of any comment on this topic suggests either:\n1. The site IS within 1/2 mile of a transit route (so it complies), or\n2. The requirement was overlooked (which would be a deficiency)\n\nGiven that:\n- The site is in Council District 5, South Austin\n- It's on Valley View Road, a local street\n- The area has some transit service\n\nLet me do a final assessment. I need to determine if the site is likely within 1/2 mile of a capital Metro route. I can't definitively verify this from the documents available, but the fact that:\n1. No reviewer flagged it as a deficiency, and\n2. No waiver was requested\n\nSuggests the site likely DOES meet the proximity requirement. However, to be conservative, since the site plan doesn't explicitly document that it's within 1/2 mile of transit, I should flag this as NOT-VERIFIABLE unless there's documentation proving compliance.\n\nActually, let me reconsider. The standard review protocol would be:\n- If a requirement is not met, the reviewer flags it\n- If a requirement is met, no comment is necessary\n- Silence could mean either compliance (met) or oversight\n\n\n- Kate Castles, as the Site Plan Review officer handling this multifamily project, would be responsible for verifying multifamily-specific requirements like transit proximity, and her silence on this issue suggests the site likely complies. Still, without explicit documentation on the site plan sheets confirming the 1/2-mile proximity, I can't definitively mark this as PASS—it remains NOT-VERIFIABLE.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2518,"cache_creation_input_tokens":978,"cache_read_input_tokens":77334,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":978,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c1ccbdc1-20f6-4e62-a4c2-17685db82f6f","uuid":"6c227000-d7cb-4e38-abee-92bed9549f71"}
