/setback requirements, screening requirements, and noise limits per § 25-2-1063. Notes referencing the repealed § 25-2-1067 or old distance tiers are not compliant with current code."},{"deficiencyId":"ZLU-32.29","status":"fail","codeCitations":["LDC § 25-2-1052"],"applicableAreas":["cover sheet"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":1}],"documentReferences":[{"documentId":"2fa9891b-9ede-4030-9300-cce670e070e1","label":"Consolidated Site Plan Application"}],"comment":"Site plan does not document whether an Article 10 exception under § 25-2-1052 applies. The site does not qualify for any documented exemptions (site is not CBD/DMU, is not a structural alteration, and is multifamily residential, not a qualifying use type). Applicant must clarify whether an exception is claimed or confirm applicability of Article 10."},{"deficiencyId":"ZLU-32.35","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["LDC § 25-1-703(B)(4)"],"applicableAreas":["vicinity map or transit analysis"],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[{"documentId":"10f3f1b9-e25e-4118-bfe3-08ea287ce738","label":"Project Location Map"}],"comment":"Multifamily residential project with 39 units must be within one-half mile walking distance of a public transit route per § 25-1-703(B)(4). Site plan and supplementary documents do not include documentation of transit route proximity or evidence of an approved director waiver (which may be granted in high opportunity areas, when transit plans are available, for LIHTC projects, or for fair housing purposes)."},{"deficiencyId":"ZLU-32.47","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["LDC § 25-10-152"],"applicableAreas":["cover sheet and site plan"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":1},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Site is within a Nonconforming Signs Ordinance area per § 25-10-152. While the site plan includes a general note requiring compliance with Chapter 25-10, it does not specifically address or demonstrate compliance with the Nonconforming Signs Ordinance requirements. Specific nonconforming signs area compliance must be documented on the site plan."}]},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":12,"cache_creation_input_tokens":583,"cache_read_input_tokens":83134,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":583,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"38ff40a3-baa1-4588-8a44-429884d301ed","uuid":"faf128c1-e94f-4de4-bfd2-1c3441eee36d"}
