{"level":30,"time":1776973949002,"pid":123,"hostname":"844f2260-bff","step":"review-runs","item":"32.md","index":1,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_012ULaZLSF1eUuTv7Y7L96UA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good! I've submitted my findings. Let me summarize what was returned:\n\n**Findings Submitted (5 items):**\n\n1. **ZLU-32.21** - NOT-VERIFIABLE: Article 10 compatibility standards not demonstrated despite site being MF-2 adjacent to SF-3 triggering property\n\n2. **ZLU-32.22** - FAIL: Site plan does not include compatibility notes specifying applicable LDC sections per current Article 10\n\n3. **ZLU-32.29** - FAIL: Site plan does not document whether Article 10 exception under § 25-2-1052 applies\n\n4. **ZLU-32.35** - NOT-VERIFIABLE: No documentation of multifamily transit proximity compliance or waiver\n\n5. **ZLU-32.47** - NOT-VERIFIABLE: Site is in nonconforming signs area but specific compliance not documented; only general Chapter 25-10 note present\n\n**Items marked as PASS or N/A (not submitted):**\n- ZLU-32.44: PASS (sign compliance note present)\n- All other items: N/A (DDBP, DMU, TOD, UNO, WO, ETOD, PUD/MUD, ERC, neighborhood plan, townhouse, ADU, condominium, vesting rights, etc.)\n\nThis is a reasonable and well-supported set of findings for a grouping focused on overlay programs and special use requirements. The site is notably subject to Article 10 compatibility standards that are not being acknowledged or documented on the site plan, which is the most significant compliance issue identified.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":11,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4653,"cache_read_input_tokens":83717,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4653,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"38ff40a3-baa1-4588-8a44-429884d301ed","uuid":"a2d4b0a9-cb1e-45da-8790-87c3e8c585c3"}
{"level":30,"time":1776973949002,"pid":123,"hostname":"844f2260-bff","step":"review-runs","item":"32.md","index":1,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_012ULaZLSF1eUuTv7Y7L96UA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've completed my review of grouping ZLU-32 (Zoning Overlay Programs, Compatibility Standards, and Special Use Requirements) for the Valley View Townhomes site plan. \n\n## Summary\n\nOut of 47 checklist items in this grouping, I identified **5 items with deficiencies** (either fail or not-verifiable status). The remainder are either not applicable to this project or have passed.\n\n**Key Issues Identified:**\n\n1. **Article 10 Compatibility Standards Not Addressed** – The site is MF-2 zoned adjacent to an SF-3 triggering property, making it subject to current Article 10 (effective July 15, 2024). However, the site plan does not acknowledge this applicability, and the application form explicitly states \"No\" to compatibility standards. This is the most significant compliance gap.\n\n2. **Missing Compatibility Notes** – The site plan lacks required notes specifying which Article 10 sections apply, height limits (40 ft within 50 ft per § 25-2-1061), and other applicable standards.\n\n3. **No Exception Documentation** – If the applicant believes an exception under § 25-2-1052 applies, it is not documented. The site does not qualify for any of the available exceptions.\n\n4. **Transit Proximity Undocumented** – The 39-unit multifamily project must document compliance with the ½-mile transit proximity requirement or provide evidence of a director waiver. Neither is present.\n\n5. **Nonconforming Signs Area Compliance Incomplete** – While the site includes a general Chapter 25-10 signage note, specific compliance with the Nonconforming Signs Ordinance (§ 25-10-152) is not documented.\n\nThe site plan is otherwise well-documented for design standards, utility compliance, and other regulatory requirements. The primary deficiencies relate to overlay and compatibility standard compliance documentation."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":11,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4653,"cache_read_input_tokens":83717,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4653,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"38ff40a3-baa1-4588-8a44-429884d301ed","uuid":"8d1d3db0-bbce-43dc-9a08-cfe7855e3bd8"}
{"level":30,"time":1776973949002,"pid":123,"hostname":"844f2260-bff","step":"review-runs","item":"32.md","index":1,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":200268,"duration_api_ms":199811,"num_turns":26,"result":"I've completed my review of grouping ZLU-32 (Zoning Overlay Programs, Compatibility Standards, and Special Use Requirements) for the Valley View Townhomes site plan. \n\n## Summary\n\nOut of 47 checklist items in this grouping, I identified **5 items with deficiencies** (either fail or not-verifiable status). The remainder are either not applicable to this project or have passed.\n\n**Key Issues Identified:**\n\n1. **Article 10 Compatibility Standards Not Addressed** – The site is MF-2 zoned adjacent to an SF-3 triggering property, making it subject to current Article 10 (effective July 15, 2024). However, the site plan does not acknowledge this applicability, and the application form explicitly states \"No\" to compatibility standards. This is the most significant compliance gap.\n\n2. **Missing Compatibility Notes** – The site plan lacks required notes specifying which Article 10 sections apply, height limits (40 ft within 50 ft per § 25-2-1061), and other applicable standards.\n\n3. **No Exception Documentation** – If the applicant believes an exception under § 25-2-1052 applies, it is not documented. The site does not qualify for any of the available exceptions.\n\n4. **Transit Proximity Undocumented** – The 39-unit multifamily project must document compliance with the ½-mile transit proximity requirement or provide evidence of a director waiver. Neither is present.\n\n5. **Nonconforming Signs Area Compliance Incomplete** – While the site includes a general Chapter 25-10 signage note, specific compliance with the Nonconforming Signs Ordinance (§ 25-10-152) is not documented.\n\nThe site plan is otherwise well-documented for design standards, utility compliance, and other regulatory requirements. The primary deficiencies relate to overlay and compatibility standard compliance documentation.","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"38ff40a3-baa1-4588-8a44-429884d301ed","total_cost_usd":0.30171590000000004,"usage":{"input_tokens":8462,"cache_creation_input_tokens":88370,"cache_read_input_tokens":906064,"output_tokens":18437,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":88370},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":8462,"outputTokens":18437,"cacheReadInputTokens":906064,"cacheCreationInputTokens":88370,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.30171590000000004,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000}},"permission_denials":[],"structured_output":{"grouping":"32","findings":[{"deficiencyId":"ZLU-32.21","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["LDC § 25-2-1051"],"applicableAreas":["entire site plan"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":1},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[{"documentId":"2fa9891b-9ede-4030-9300-cce670e070e1","label":"Consolidated Site Plan Application"}],"comment":"Site is zoned MF-2 and located immediately adjacent to an SF-3 triggering property, making it subject to current Article 10 Compatibility Standards (LDC §§ 25-2-1051–25-2-1063, eff. July 15, 2024). Height limits of 40 feet within 50 feet of triggering property per § 25-2-1061 should apply. However, the site plan does not acknowledge or demonstrate compliance with Article 10; the application form states 'Subject to Compatibility Standards? No,' and no compatibility assessment appears on the cover sheet or site plan sheets."},{"deficiencyId":"ZLU-32.22","status":"fail","codeCitations":["LDC § 25-2-1063"],"applicableAreas":["cover sheet and site plan sheets"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":1},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[{"documentId":"2fa9891b-9ede-4030-9300-cce670e070e1","label":"Consolidated Site Plan Application"}],"comment":"Site plan does not include compatibility notes specifying which LDC sections apply per current Article 10. Notes must reference Ordinance 20240516-004 (eff. July 15, 2024) and identify applicable height limits, buffer/setback requirements, screening requirements, and noise limits per § 25-2-1063. Notes referencing the repealed § 25-2-1067 or old distance tiers are not compliant with current code."},{"deficiencyId":"ZLU-32.29","status":"fail","codeCitations":["LDC § 25-2-1052"],"applicableAreas":["cover sheet"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":1}],"documentReferences":[{"documentId":"2fa9891b-9ede-4030-9300-cce670e070e1","label":"Consolidated Site Plan Application"}],"comment":"Site plan does not document whether an Article 10 exception under § 25-2-1052 applies. The site does not qualify for any documented exemptions (site is not CBD/DMU, is not a structural alteration, and is multifamily residential, not a qualifying use type). Applicant must clarify whether an exception is claimed or confirm applicability of Article 10."},{"deficiencyId":"ZLU-32.35","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["LDC § 25-1-703(B)(4)"],"applicableAreas":["vicinity map or transit analysis"],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[{"documentId":"10f3f1b9-e25e-4118-bfe3-08ea287ce738","label":"Project Location Map"}],"comment":"Multifamily residential project with 39 units must be within one-half mile walking distance of a public transit route per § 25-1-703(B)(4). Site plan and supplementary documents do not include documentation of transit route proximity or evidence of an approved director waiver (which may be granted in high opportunity areas, when transit plans are available, for LIHTC projects, or for fair housing purposes)."},{"deficiencyId":"ZLU-32.47","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["LDC § 25-10-152"],"applicableAreas":["cover sheet and site plan"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":1},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Site is within a Nonconforming Signs Ordinance area per § 25-10-152. While the site plan includes a general note requiring compliance with Chapter 25-10, it does not specifically address or demonstrate compliance with the Nonconforming Signs Ordinance requirements. Specific nonconforming signs area compliance must be documented on the site plan."}]},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"bcad49c3-058a-4bb7-bc07-9d11542ea6ae"}
{"level":30,"time":1776973949003,"pid":123,"hostname":"844f2260-bff","step":"review-runs","item":"16.md","index":2,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01KELcUb1pNs9E8SmdU8wCWr","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Excellent. Now I have a clear picture of what's on the site plan. Let me evaluate the applicable checklist items:\n\n**ZLU-16.1 (Adjoining land uses noted on all four sides):**\nVision result: \"No, adjacent land uses are not explicitly labeled with a use type on all four sides.\"\n- East: Yes (Existing Apartment Building, Clarion Ridge Condominiums)\n- North: Only zoning noted (MF-4-CO), no land use type\n- South: Street and some faint text about \"Valley View\" and \"Creek Pointe\" but no specific land use type\n- West: No explicit land use labels\nSTATUS: **FAIL** - Not all four sides have adjacent land uses documented\n\n**ZLU-16.2 (Adjoining land uses for properties across adjacent streets/ROW):**\nVision result: South side has \"faint property lines and text mentioning 'Valley View' and 'Creek Pointe', but no specific land use type is labeled\"\nSTATUS: **NOT-VERIFIABLE** - The properties across the street are not clearly labeled with land use\n\n**ZLU-16.3 (Vacant adjoining properties not identified as \"vacant\"):**\nFrom vision tool, the properties shown have names (Apartment Building, Clarion Ridge Condominiums, Valley View). No vacant properties are mentioned. \nSTATUS: **NOT-VERIFIABLE** - Cannot confirm whether any adjacent properties are vacant, so cannot assess if they're labeled as such\n\n**ZLU-16.4 (Adjacent property zoning not shown):**\nVision result: \"Yes, adjacent zoning designations are shown for some, but not all, surrounding properties.\"\n- North: MF-4-CO labeled\n- East: MF-2-CO labeled\n- South/West: Not shown\nSTATUS: **FAIL** - Adjacent zoning not shown for all sides (South and West missing)\n\n**ZLU-16.5 (Adjacent zoning inaccurate/inconsistent with GIS):**\n\n\nChecking against the GIS data from facts.md, the adjacent parcels should show SF-3, GO, MF-3, MF-3-CO, and MF-2-CO. The site plan shows MF-4-CO to the north and MF-2-CO to the east. The MF-2-CO matches the GIS records, but MF-4-CO doesn't appear in the adjacent parcel list, suggesting a potential discrepancy or mislabeling on the site plan.\n\nSince the subject property is MF-2 and borders multiple zoning districts, the code requires all zoning boundary lines to be shown and labeled. The site plan only identifies zoning on the north and east sides, leaving the south and west boundaries unmarked. This appears to be a violation of the zoning boundary labeling requirement.\n\nFor ZLU-16.7, the site isn't within or adjacent to any PUD overlay, so this standard doesn't apply. Regarding ZLU-16.8, I need to verify whether zoning designations appear on the mylars themselves. The vision shows zoning on Sheet 9, but the standard may require this information to be included on the mylar sheets as well—I'll need to check the actual mylar documents to confirm compliance.\n\nFor ZLU-16.9, while building footprints are depicted with light gray dashed lines on the eastern boundary, they're absent from the north, south, and west sides despite neighboring properties existing on all sides (SF-3, GO, and MF-3 parcels). This appears to be a deficiency. Moving to ZLU-16.10, since buildings do exist on adjoining lots, a note explaining their absence would be required if they weren't shown—but given the incomplete depiction on three sides, this standard's applicability depends on whether the missing footprints constitute a violation.\n\nZLU-16.11 checks out: all three building dimensions are provided through the plan view and the Building Height Table. The perimeter boundaries for Buildings 1-8 are clearly marked with solid black outlines, satisfying ZLU-16.12.\n\nFor ZLU-16.13, I need to determine if property connections to adjacent lots must be identified based on whether the net site area meets the 3-acre threshold and other triggering conditions. The principal street appears to be Valley View Road to the south, with buildings and access points arranged around the site perimeter. Without a clear view of the exact positioning, I can't definitively determine if parking sits between buildings and the street, so condition (b) remains uncertain.\n\nSince MF-2 zoning is more restrictive than MF-4, Article 10 requirements don't apply to this site. All related items from ZLU-16.14 through ZLU-16.26 should be marked as N/A.\n\nThe applicable requirements are more limited: dumpster setbacks under General Note provisions, parking screening where residential uses are adjacent, waterfront overlay rules if applicable, service station standards if that use exists, lighting requirements for sites with adjacent residential properties, and mechanical equipment noise standards. Looking at ZLU-16.27 regarding refuse placement, the vision description doesn't specify where trash or dumpsters are located relative to single-family properties.\n\nFacts.md confirms adjacent SF-3 and other residential zoning, so I need to locate the refuse receptacle details in blocks.md to verify compliance.\n\nFor parking screening rules, the site's MF-2 zoning means ZLU-16.29 doesn't apply since that covers non-residential parking adjacent to residential districts. However, ZLU-16.30 is relevant—the site has 88 parking spaces in a residential zone adjacent to SF-3, GO, MF-3, and M-zoned properties, so screening requirements likely apply.\n\nI notice the vision tool shows 70 surface spaces while blocks.md lists 10 surface spaces with 78 garage spaces. The blocks.md data should be authoritative, giving 88 total spaces. Since this exceeds 10 spaces in a residential district adjoining other residential properties, ZLU-16.30 requires a wall, fence, or landscape screen of at least 6 feet.\n\nThe vision tool mentions a wood fence and existing retaining wall on the east boundary, but I need to confirm these meet the 6-foot minimum height requirement and are positioned correctly. The adjacent SF-3 zoning is more restrictive than SF-5, reinforcing the screening obligation.\n\nFor the waterfront overlay, facts.md shows no regulating plan and no waterfront designation, so ZLU-16.31-32 doesn't apply. Checking ZLU-16.33 regarding service station screening requirements next.\n\nThe site plan notes indicate all exterior lighting will be full cut-off and fully shielded per Subchapter E 2.5, addressing the hooding requirement. However, since the buildings reach three stories, I need to verify whether any lights on the third floor face the adjacent residential areas, as ZLU-16.35 restricts this.\n\nFor the mechanical equipment noise standard, the multi-family use means HVAC and other equipment will be present. I should locate the mechanical equipment schedule to confirm it meets the 70 dB(A) threshold. I also need to examine the site plan more closely for trash enclosure placement, equipment details, and parking lot screening specifications.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":10,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1755,"cache_read_input_tokens":57162,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1755,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"158c3787-95dd-4091-81cc-891db6165072","uuid":"fff99258-03d1-4d1c-bb85-736c3788704d"}
