{"level":30,"time":1776973949033,"pid":123,"hostname":"844f2260-bff","step":"review-runs","item":"15.md","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":4,"prompt":"Examine the existing conditions survey carefully. Look for and describe:\n\n1. Any recorded setback lines or building restriction lines shown on the plat or survey\n2. All easements labeled on the survey (including widths and directions) - particularly focus on easements mentioned in the facts.md like the greenbelt easement, drainage easement, and any setback lines\n3. The location of the \"5' Public Utility Easement\" and \"25' Drainage Easement\" if shown\n4. Any notes or dimensions indicating restricted building or setback areas\n5. Whether the property lines are clearly dimensioned and labeled\n6. The orientation and layout relative to Valley View Road\n\nProvide specific information about what easements and restrictions are and are not visible on this survey.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a detailed visual analysis of the provided document, titled **\"BOUNDARY, IMPROVEMENTS, TOPOGRAPHIC & TREE SURVEY\"** for **\"Valley View Townhomes\"** at **\"3759 Valley View Road\"**, here are the findings regarding your specific requirements:\n\n**1. Recorded setback lines or building restriction lines shown on the plat or survey**\nThere are no recorded building setback lines (often labeled as B.L. or B.S.L.) or building restriction lines drawn or labeled within the interior of the primary property boundary (identified as **\"LOT 1, MECEY SUBDIVISION\"**) on this specific survey page.\n\n**2. All easements labeled on the survey**\nThe following easements are explicitly labeled on the survey. (Note: Directions are described assuming a standard orientation where the North arrow, which points to the right side of the page, dictates direction):\n*   Along the Western property line (fronting Valley View Road): A dashed line is labeled **\"5' 