angular in shape, extending Eastward away from Valley View Road. The existing main structure (labeled **\"SLAB F.F.E.=686.8'\"**) is situated in the central/western portion of the lot, with a large paved area (labeled **\"ASPHALT\"** and **\"CONC\"**) separating the front of the structure from Valley View Road."}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"33f519bd-bced-4a7a-aae5-831dbf134acc","uuid":"aec50c2f-05c6-4f95-bc32-8f1836520e94","tool_use_result":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a detailed visual analysis of the provided document, titled **\"BOUNDARY, IMPROVEMENTS, TOPOGRAPHIC & TREE SURVEY\"** for **\"Valley View Townhomes\"** at **\"3759 Valley View Road\"**, here are the findings regarding your specific requirements:\n\n**1. Recorded setback lines or building restriction lines shown on the plat or survey**\nThere are no recorded building setback lines (often labeled as B.L. or B.S.L.) or building restriction lines drawn or labeled within the interior of the primary property boundary (identified as **\"LOT 1, MECEY SUBDIVISION\"**) on this specific survey page.\n\n**2. All easements labeled on the survey**\nThe following easements are explicitly labeled on the survey. (Note: Directions are described assuming a standard orientation where the North arrow, which points to the right side of the page, dictates direction):\n*   Along the Western property line (fronting Valley View Road): A dashed line is labeled **\"5' P.U.E. EASEMENT VOL. 44, PG. 78 P.R.T.C.TX\"**.\n*   Along the Southern property line: A dashed line is labeled **\"5' P.U.E. EASEMENT VOL. 44, PG. 78 P.R.T.C.TX\"**.\n*   Along the Eastern property line (rear of property): A dashed line inside the property is labeled with a leader line stating **\"5' ELEC EASEMENT DOC. NO. 2001019014 O.P.R.T.C.TX\"**.\n*   Near the Southeast corner: Another leader line points to the eastern easement line stating **\"5' ELEC EASEMENT DOC. NO. 2001019014 O.P.R.T.C.TX\"**.\n*   Adjacent to the Northern property li