{"level":30,"time":1776973949051,"pid":123,"hostname":"844f2260-bff","step":"review-runs","item":"16.md","index":8,"runIndex":"run-3","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":9,"prompt":"On Sheet 9 (Site Plan), I need to verify several compliance items: (1) Is there a note stating \"no buildings exist on adjoining lots within 50 feet\" for any direction, or is one needed? (2) Where are the surface parking spaces (you noted 10 surface spaces in the parking data) located relative to adjacent property lines? (3) Are there any screening features (fences, landscaping, walls) shown around parking areas, especially adjacent to residential-zoned properties? (4) Where is the trash/refuse collection area located and how far is it from adjacent property lines (especially residential zoning like MF-3, MF-2-CO)? (5) Are there any notes about property connections to adjacent lots or access points to neighboring parcels?","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a visual analysis of Sheet 9 of the site plan, here is the information regarding your compliance items:\n\n**1. Note regarding \"no buildings exist on adjoining lots within 50 feet\":**\nThere is no note stating \"no buildings exist on adjoining lots within 50 feet\" on this sheet. In fact, the plan explicitly labels existing structures on adjoining properties that appear to be very close to the property line. For example, there is an \"Existing Apartment Building\" labeled to the northeast and another \"Existing Apartment Building\" labeled on the adjacent eastern lot. Therefore, such a note would likely be inaccurate for this site. \n\n**2. Location of the 10 surface parking spaces:**\nThe 10 surface parking spaces are located along the perimeter of the site in two distinct groups:\n*   **Western Boundary:** There is a cluster of 4 perpendicular parking spaces (including one striped ADA accessible space) located on the west side of the site, immediately south of the northernmost \"Construct Type II Driveway\" entrance. These spaces abut the western property line.\n*   **Southern Boundary:** There is a row of 6 perpendicular parking spaces located along the southern drive aisle, directly south of Buildings 7 and 8. These spaces abut the southern property line.\n\n**3. Screening features (fences, landscaping, walls) around parking areas:**\n*   **Near the 4 western spaces:** There are no explicit labels for screening fences or walls directly adjacent to these spaces. The plan notes a \"Sidewalk Easement\" and a \"Tree Well\" nearby. \n*   **Near the 6 southern spaces:** There is a concrete retaining wall running along the southern boundary immediately behind these spaces. Labels in this area read \"Begin Concrete Retaining Wall\" and \"End Concrete Retaining Wall at Existing Concrete Retaining Wall / Tie to Existing Concrete Retaining Wall\".\n*   *Note on general site screening:* The plan labels a \"Wood Fence\" along portions of the eastern boundary and a \"Pond Perimeter Fence\" around the detention pond at the north. \n\n**4. Trash/refuse collection area location and distances:**\nThere is no designated central commercial dumpster pad or refuse collection enclosure visually delineated on this site plan. Because there is no central area shown, there are no distance measurements to adjacent property lines provided. \n\nInstead, the plan includes a **\"Trash Collection Notes\"** section at the bottom center, which suggests a curbside cart pickup system rather than a central dumpster. It reads exactly as follows:\n> \"Trash containers shall not be left at curbside unattended. Signs must be posted on the building or at a location that is publicly visible indicating that trash containers may not be left at curbside. The sign shall indicate the City of Austin's Code enforcement phone number for the public to report violations.\n> A restrictive covenant may be required for enforcement purposes. \n> *Reference: T.C.M. 9.4.2*\"\n\n**5. Notes about property connections or access points to neighboring parcels:**\nThere are no notes or drawn features indicating pedestrian or vehicular cross-access connections to adjacent neighboring parcels. \n*   Access to the site is provided solely via two driveways on the western boundary connecting to the public right-of-way (both labeled \"Construct Type II Driveway\").\n*   The northern, eastern, and southern boundaries feature retaining walls, existing fences, or drainage/detention infrastructure with no labeled egress/ingress points to the adjoining lots. (The only gates noted are internal: \"2 - 14' Pond Access Gates\" near the detention pond).","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1472,"outputTokens":752,"totalTokens":4990,"reasoningTokens":2766},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 2702484]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just because you do not find evidence for a requirement on this page does not mean it will not be present on another page.\n\nReport back precisely on what you see, using exact quotes for any text you transcribe from forms, tables, or labels.\