{"level":30,"time":1776973949066,"pid":123,"hostname":"844f2260-bff","step":"review-runs","item":"32.md","index":4,"runIndex":"run-2","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":9,"prompt":"Examine the site plan layout and identify: 1) Any on-site amenities (pools, courts, playgrounds, recreation areas) that are exclusively for residents, and their location relative to the site boundaries; 2) The location of the detention/biofiltration pond; 3) Building locations, especially those closest to the SF-3 adjacent parcel; 4) Any retaining walls or site features near the property line with the adjacent SF-3 parcel; 5) Any landscaping areas that appear to be rain gardens or bioretention features","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a careful examination of the provided site plan layout, here are the findings directly addressing your requests:\n\n**1. On-site amenities for residents and their locations:**\n*   **Common Open Space:** There is a centrally located area labeled \"**Common Open Space 4,960 sf**\" positioned between Building 2, Building 4, Building 7, and Building 8.\n*   **Recreation/Gathering:** There is a \"**BBQ Pit**\" and a \"**Picnic Table**\" located on the eastern side of the property, situated between Building 3, Building 5, and the eastern property boundary (adjacent to the \"Existing Apartment Building\").\n*   **Walking Paths:** A winding path labeled \"**4' Wide Decomposed Granite Walkway**\" loops through the northern half of the site, passing north of Buildings 1, 2, 3, and 4. \n*   *Note:* There are no pools, sports courts, or playgrounds explicitly labeled on this site plan. \n\n**2. Location of the detention/biofiltration pond:**\n*   The \"**Biofiltration/Detention Pond**\" is located in the far northeast corner of the site. It is bordered by a \"**Pond Perimeter Fence**\" and a \"**Concrete Retaining Wall**\" along its southern and eastern edges.\n\n**3. Building locations closest to the SF-3 adjacent parcel:**\n*   The parcel zoned SF-3 is located immediately to the south of the property line (indicated by the label \"**Zoning: SF-3**\" directly below the southern boundary).\n*   The buildings situated closest to this SF-3 parcel are **Building 7** (Units 701-705) and **Building 8** (Units 801-806), which are aligned parallel to and immediately adjacent to the southern property line.\n\n**4. Retaining walls or site features near the property line with the adjacent SF-3 parcel:**\n*   A \"**Concrete Retaining Wall**\" runs extensively along the southern property boundary line shared with the SF-3 parcel.\n*   Starting from the southwest corner, there is a callout to \"**Begin Concrete Retaining Wall**\". \n*   Moving eastward along that same boundary, there are two separate callout boxes pointing to the wall that read EXACTLY: \"**Begin Concrete Retaining Wall at Existing Concrete Retaining Wall**\" and \"**Tie to Existing Concrete Retaining Wall**\" (Note: the central label says \"**End Concrete Retaining Wall...**\" instead of \"Begin\").\n*   There are also several existing trees preserved along this southern boundary line.\n\n**5. Landscaping areas that appear to be rain gardens or bioretention features:**\n*   The primary stormwater/bioretention feature is the large, explicitly labeled \"**Biofiltration/Detention Pond**\" in the northeast corner. \n*   There are no other landscaping areas on the layout explicitly labeled as rain gardens, filter strips, or secondary bioretention features.\n\n***\n\n### Transcribed Document Tables\nPer your requirement to reproduce tables exactly as they appear, here are the transcriptions of the data tables found on the bottom left and bottom right of the plan:\n\n**Building Data Table**\n| Building # | Building Type | Gross Floor Area (sf) | Building Coverage (sf) | Bedroom Type | Units |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| 1 | 4 Plex | 8,550 | 3,290 | Two Bedroom | 16 |\n| 2 | 6 Plex | 13,004 | 4,997 | Three B