{"level":30,"time":1776974020295,"pid":123,"hostname":"844f2260-bff","step":"review-runs","item":"15.md","index":9,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_0128qVZZ2oguYDpzgpuUiKX6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"This is a critical finding. The measurements show:\n- Building 8 southeast corner is 31.2 feet from the southern property line\n- Building 6 southeast corner is 24.8 feet from the southern property line\n\nThe facts.md states there is an SF-3 parcel (0406100210) that is an immediate neighbor. The grouping file confirms that SF-3 is a qualifying \"triggering property\" zone under Article 10 (§ 25-2-1051 and § 25-2-1053).\n\nThe site is zoned MF-2, which is \"less restrictive\" than SF-5 or more restrictive. The adjacent parcel is SF-3. So Article 10 compatibility standards APPLY because:\n1. Site is MF-2 (less restrictive than MF-4) ✓\n2. Adjacent property is SF-3 within 75 feet ✓\n3. SF-3 is explicitly listed as a triggering property zone ✓\n\nWhat this means:\n- A 25-foot compatibility buffer is required along the shared property line (§ 25-2-1062(B))\n- Height restrictions apply: structures < 50 ft from triggering property = max 40 ft; 50-74 ft = max 60 ft (§ 25-2-1061)\n- Building 6 is at 24.8 feet - this is WITHIN the required buffer zone and encroaches into it\n- Building 8 is at 31.2 feet - this exceeds the 25-ft buffer but may be in the restricted zone per § 25-8-700\n\nKey deficiencies found:\n1. The site plan does not show ANY compatibility buffer line\n2. The site plan does not show ANY notation about Article 10 compatibility standards applying\n3. No compatibility exhibit is provided showing the SF-3 property and distance measurements\n\n\n4. No cross-sections demonstrating height compliance at the 50-foot and 75-foot thresholds from the triggering property\n5. Building 6's placement at 24.8 feet directly violates the 25-foot buffer requirement\n\nNow I need to check the standard MF-2 setback requirements and verify whether the required zoning district setback lines are shown on the site plan. I should also verify that the actual setback distances comply with MF-2 standards and examine any other applicable zoning requirements.\n\nFor the compatibility standards, Article 10 clearly applies here. The critical failures are: no height limits per § 25-2-1061 are displayed, no compatibility exhibit showing existing structures on the triggering property exists, and the 25-foot buffer along the southern property line isn't properly delineated. Additionally, the buffer line appears to be misaligned or incorrectly positioned relative to the property boundary.\n\nThe SF-3 parcel that triggers these requirements isn't identified on the plans. While the property line itself seems visible, there's no screening shown to meet buffer requirements. Several elements still need verification—whether improvements, covered structures, drainage features, on-site amenities, or parking encroach into the required screening zones, and whether exterior lighting meets hooding standards.\n\nMechanical equipment noise and screened elements can't be verified without knowing where mechanical/HVAC systems are located. The remaining compatibility standards don't apply to this site.\n\nA critical issue emerges from the application materials: the consolidated site plan form explicitly states \"Subject to Compatibility Standards? [NO]\"—but this is wrong. Article 10 is clearly triggered. The master comment report and site plan review comments never address compatibility standards, and the plan set contains no compatibility exhibit sheet or cross-sections. Building 6, positioned 24.8 feet away, falls directly within the required 25-foot buffer zone. The applicant has fundamentally failed to acknowledge that Article 10 applies and hasn't demonstrated the required compatibility buffer.\n\nThe missing documentation is extensive: no height compliance cross-sections, no identification of the triggering SF-3 parcel, no compatibility exhibit, and no confirmation that buildings maintain proper buffer distances. I should now examine the remaining setback requirements to see if there are additional violations.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":10,"cache_creation_input_tokens":47561,"cache_read_input_tokens":19314,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":47561,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d203a61d-b956-4bf7-a62f-71a0e7d71a2a","uuid":"220dc54f-cdd1-455f-84df-db789a769cd7"}
