e absence of a drawn dumpster). \n\nUnder the exact heading **Trash Collection Notes**, the following is stated character-by-character:\n\n> \"Trash containers shall not be left at curbside unattended. Signs must be posted on the building or at a location that is publicly visible indicating that trash containers may not be left at curbside. The sign shall indicate the City of Austin's Code enforcement phone number for the public to report violations.\"\n> \"A restrictive covenant may be required for enforcement purposes.\"\n> \"Reference: TCM, 9.4.2\"\n\n*Note for the reviewer: The absence of drawn central dumpsters and the specific wording of the \"Trash Collection Notes\" strongly indicate this development utilizes individual roll-away bins for each unit rather than a centralized commercial dumpster enclosure requiring screening or setbacks.*"}]}
{"level":30,"time":1776974020315,"pid":123,"hostname":"844f2260-bff","step":"review-runs","item":"15.md","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":2,"prompt":"Examine the plat carefully. Look for and describe:\n\n1. Any recorded setback lines or building restriction lines on the 1975 Mecey Subdivision plat\n2. All easements labeled on the plat with their widths and locations\n3. Any notes indicating building restrictions, setback requirements, or zoning setbacks\n4. The legal boundary dimensions and how the property is oriented\n5. Whether any historical setback lines or building restrictions are noted in the plat document\n6. Any references to easements from other subdivisions (Cortez Heights, Trico) that might apply\n\nProvide a complete list of all easements and restrictions shown on this recorded plat.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a careful visual analysis of the provided 1975 plat document for the \"MECEY SUBDIVISION\" (Travis County Plat Volume 73, Page 76), here are the findings corresponding to your specific requests:\n\n**1. Recorded setback lines or building restriction lines**\n*   **None are visible.** I have scanned the entirety of LOT 1 and LOT 2. While there are dashed lines indicating various easements (detailed below), there are no dashed lines labeled as \"Building Line\", \"B.L.\", \"Building Setback\", or \"Setback\".\n\n**2. All easements labeled on the plat with their widths and locations**\nThe plat explicitly labels several easements using dashed lines. They are transcribed exactly as follows:\n*   **\"15' P.U.E. (Exist.)\"** [Note: First digit is slightly blurry, could potentially be \"10'\"]: Located inside the northern boundary of both Lot 1 and Lot 2, running parallel to the property line shared with \"CORTEZ HEIGHTS\".\n*   **\"26' Drainage Easement (Existing)\"**: A wide, diagonally hatched easement running roughly north-south through the middle of LOT 2.\n*   **\"Exist 5' Elec. Ease.\"**: Located inside the southern boundary of LOT 1, running parallel to the property line shared with \"O.R. ROGERS\".\n*   **\"5' Elec. Eas.\"**: Located inside LOT 2. An arrow points to a dashed line running roughly north-south, near the eastern boundary shared with \"F.D. BADGER\".\n*   **\"10' Water Line Ease.\"** [Text slightly unclear, could be \"Water & W.W.\"]: Located in the southeast corner of LOT 2. An arrow points to a dashed line following the southern/eastern boundary curve near \"BEN H. ROBERTS\".\n\n**3. Any notes indicating building restrictions, setback requirements, or zoning setbacks**\n*   **None are present.** There is no \"Notes\" section on this plat that lists zoning categories, setback distances, or building restrictions.\n*   The dedication text (top right) states: \"...and I do hereby dedicate to the public all streets and easements as shown hereon.\" but makes no mention of building restrictions.\n*   The surveyor's certification (bottom right) states: \"This is to certify that Austin City Code Chapter 23, 27 of 1954 has been complied with.\" but does not explicitly list what those code requirements entail regarding setbacks.\n\n**4. The legal boundary dimensions and how the property is oriented**\n*   **Orientation**: The North arrow (located center-top, above the lot drawing) points diagonally to the top-left of the page. Given the bearings, the long edges of the lot run generally East-West, and the short edges run North-South.\n*   **Overall Boundary Dimensions**:\n    *   **North Boundary** (adjacent to Cortez Heights): Bearing **\"S 61° 14' E\"**, Distance **\"419.87'\"**.\n    *   **South Boundary** (adjacent to O.R. Rogers & Ben H. Roberts): Bearing **\"N 61° 42' W\"**, Distance **\"414.35'\"**.\n    *   **West Boundary** (adjacent to Valley View Road): Bearing **\"N 28° 18' E\"**, Distance **\"100.00'\"**.\n    *   **East Boundary** (adjacent to F.D. Badger & Clawson Road): This boundary is irregular, containing a straight segment and a curve at the southeast corner characterized by **\"CURVE DATA (1) $\\Delta$ = 31° 25', T = 20.84', R = 74.10', L.C. = 40.12', ARC = 40.63'\"**.\n*   The total property is subdivided vertically into **\"LOT 1\"** (West side, 364.35' wide along the south) and **\"LOT 2\"** (East side, 50.00' wide along the south). The dividing line is 100.00' long.\n\n**5. Historical setback lines or building restrictions noted in the plat document**\n*   **None are noted.** As stated in point 1, there are no historical building lines or setback restrictions drawn or mentioned anywhere on this specific document.\n\n**6. References to easements from other subdivisions that might apply**\n*   The dedication text states that the owner is subdividing **\"Lot A, Trico Subdivision, a subdivision out of the Isaac Decker League according to a map or plat of record in Book 69, Page 14...\"**\n*   Because this is a resubdivision of a prior lot (Trico), the repeated use of the word **\"(Exist.)\"** or **\"(Existing)\"** on the P.U.E., Drainage, and Electrical easements strongly suggests these easements were established by that prior Trico Subdivision plat or other historical deeds, and are simply being carried forward onto this new 1975 Mecey plat.\n*   The northern boundary is directly adjacent to **\"CORTEZ HEIGHTS - PLAT BK. 64 PG. 13\"**, and the existing P.U.E. runs exactly along this shared boundary.\n\n***\n\n### Complete List of All Easements and Restrictions Shown:\n*   **Building Restrictions/Setbacks**: NONE SHOWN\n*   **Easement 1**: \"15' P.U.E. (Exist.)\" [or possibly 10'] - Northern boundary\n*   **Easement 2**: \"26' Drainage Easement (Existing)\" - Diagonal through Lot 2\n*   **Easement 3**: \"Exist 5' Elec. Ease.\" - Southern boundary of Lot 1\n*   **Easement 4**: \"5' Elec. Eas.\" - Near eastern boundary of Lot 2\n*   **Easement 5**: \"10' Water Line Ease.\" [Text slightly unclear] - Southeast corner of Lot 2","providerMetadata":{"google":