 ft\")?**\n**No.** There are no labels specifying required clearance distances around the transformer pads.\n\n**4. What type of buildings or structures are adjacent to each transformer pad?**\nThe pads are located adjacent to multi-unit residential buildings labeled \"Bldg. 1\" through \"Bldg. 8\" and paved driving aisles/turnarounds. However, **the specific construction types (e.g., \"wood frame\" or \"masonry\") are not labeled** on this electrical plan. The buildings are only identified by their building number, square footage, Finished Floor Elevation (FFE), and unit numbers.\n\n**5. Are there notation/details specifying which clearance standard applies to each transformer?**\n**No.** There are no notations or detail blocks on this page that specify clearance standards for the transformers. The \"Utility Notes\" section in the bottom right corner only contains general instructions for the contractor to verify horizontal/vertical locations and details regarding private domestic water and wastewater branches; it does not mention electrical transformer clearances.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1436,"outputTokens":488,"totalTokens":3835,"reasoningTokens":1911},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 2092056]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it 