{"level":30,"time":1776974041785,"pid":123,"hostname":"844f2260-bff","step":"review-runs","item":"15.md","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014PmfZuz2eBqLysAF1WoSBF","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Site Plan Review\n     2→\n     3→*Requires updates to unit counts, site area calculations, building data tables, lighting notes, and administrative notes.*\n     4→\n     5→Site Plan Review – Kate Castles (512) 978-4555 - kate.castles@austintexas.gov\n     6→\n     7→LAND USE / ZONING \n     8→SP1 – Current Status: Pending\n     9→* U1: Thank you for providing the unit counts. According to 25-2-561, the minimum site area is 2400 sf for 2+ bedroom dwelling units, making the minimum site area for the site 93,600. Please update the Site Area Calculation (MF-2) table accordingly.\n    10→* U0: For Multi-Family Projects, please include the following table:\n    11→\n    12→| Unit type | Count |\n    13→| --- | --- |\n    14→| studio/eff | |\n    15→| 1 bedroom | |\n    16→| 2 bedroom | |\n    17→| 3 bedroom | |\n    18→| Total | |\n    19→\n    20→SP2 – Current Status: Pending\n    21→* U1: Please ensure that each building height is calculated correctly. The height of each building is calculated from the average of the highest and lowest grades adjacent to the building to the top of the coping. Therefore, the building height could be different for each building.\n    22→* U0: Show the following building information (show proposed and allowed) for each building and the total for all buildings in a Building Data Table:\n    23→  o gross floor area for each building (in sq. ft.)\n    24→  o building coverage for each building (in sq. ft.)\n    25→  o building height for each building (in feet and stories)\n    26→  o foundation type and finished floor elevation for each building\n    27→\n    28→SP3 – Current Status: Cleared\n    29→* U1: Multifamily use confirmed. Please let the Case Manager know if you would like to change the project name. Comment cleared. \n    30→* U0: Please confirm that you are proposing Townhouse use. FYI – Townhouses will need to plat a townhouse subdivision as not more than one townhouse is permitted on a townhouse lot. A townhouse lot must include a private yard with a wall or solid fence along a side lot line. \n    31→Reference: 25-2-775\n    32→\n    33→SUBCHAPTER E: DESIGN STANDARDS\n    34→SP4 - Current Status: Cleared\n    35→U1: Comment cleared. \n    36→U0: Include the following note with Figure 34 on the site plan page: \"All exterior lighting will be full cut-off and fully shielded in compliance with Subchapter E 2.5 and will be reviewed during building plan review. Any change or substitution of lamp/light fixtures shall be submitted to the Director for approval in accordance with Section 2.5.2.E.\" \n    37→\n    38→ADMINISTRATIVE \n    39→SP5 - Current Status: Cleared\n    40→U1: Comment cleared. \n    41→U0: Confirm that all amenities such as walls, fences, sidewalks, swimming pools, and all other land improvements are shown on each site plan sheet.\n    42→\n    43→SP6 - Current Status: Cleared\n    44→U1: Comment cleared. \n    45→U0: Please remove all City of Pflugerville Notes and show the following City of Austin site plan release notes on the site plan:\n    46→a. All improvements shall be made in accordance with the released site plan. Any additional improvements will require site plan amendment and approval of the Development Services Department.\n    47→b. Approval of this Site Plan does not include Building and Fire Code approval nor building permit approval. \n    48→c. All signs must comply with requirements of the Land Development Code (Chapter 25-10).\n    49→d. Additional electric easements may be required at a later date. \n    50→e. Water and wastewater service will be provided by the City of Austin (or identify the service provider if other than the City of Austin). \n    51→f. All existing structures shown to be removed will require a demolition permit from the City of Austin Development Services Department.\n    52→g. No certificate of occupancy may be issued for the proposed residential condominium project until the owner or owners of the property have complied with Chapter 81 and 82 of the Property Code of the State of Texas or any other statutes enacted by the State concerning condominiums.\n    53→h. For driveway construction: The owner is responsible for all costs for relocation of, or damage to utilities. \n    54→i. For construction within the right-of-way, a ROW excavation permit is required.\n    55→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"33f519bd-bced-4a7a-aae5-831dbf134acc","uuid":"1e1ad07e-9e3c-4de4-8392-3b615be355f0","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/vercel/sandbox/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/supplementary-docs/master-comment-report/09-site-plan-review.md","content":"# Site Plan Review\n\n*Requires updates to unit counts, site area calculations, building data tables, lighting notes, and administrative notes.*\n\nSite Plan Review – Kate Castles (512) 978-4555 - kate.castles@austintexas.gov\n\nLAND USE / ZONING \nSP1 – Current Status: Pending\n* U1: Thank you for providing the unit counts. According to 25-2-561, the minimum site area is 2400 sf for 2+ bedroom dwelling units, making the minimum site area for the site 93,600. Please update the Site Area Calculation (MF-2) table accordingly.\n* U0: For Multi-Family Projects, please include the following table:\n\n| Unit type | Count |\n| --- | --- |\n| studio/eff | |\n| 1 bedroom | |\n| 2 bedroom | |\n| 3 bedroom | |\n| Total | |\n\nSP2 – Current Status: Pending\n* U1: Please ensure that each building height is calculated correctly. The height of each building is calculated from the average of the highest and lowest grades adjacent to the building to the top of the coping. Therefore, the building height could be different for each building.\n* U0: Show the following building information (show proposed and allowed) for each building and the total for all buildings in a Building Data Table:\n  o gross floor area for each building (in sq. ft.)\n  o building coverage for each building (in sq. ft.)\n  o building height for each building (in feet and stories)\n  o foundation type and finished floor elevation for each building\n\nSP3 – Current Status: Cleared\n* U1: Multifamily use confirmed. Please let the Case Manager know if you would like to change the project name. Comment cleared. \n* U0: Please confirm that you are proposing Townhouse use. FYI – Townhouses will need to plat a townhouse subdivision as not more than one townhouse is permitted on a townhouse lot. A townhouse lot must include a private yard with a wall or solid fence along a side lot line. \nReference: 25-2-775\n\nSUBCHAPTER E: DESIGN STANDARDS\nSP4 - Current Status: Cleared\nU1: Comment cleared. \nU0: Include the following note with Figure 34 on the site plan page: \"All exterior lighting will be full cut-off and fully shielded in compliance with Subchapter E 2.5 and will be reviewed during building plan review. Any change or substitution of lamp/light fixtures shall be submitted to the Director for approval in accordance with Section 2.5.2.E.\" \n\nADMINISTRATIVE \nSP5 - Current Status: Cleared\nU1: Comment cleared. \nU0: Confirm that all amenities such as walls, fences, sidewalks, swimming pools, and all other land improvements are shown on each site plan sheet.\n\nSP6 - Current Status: Cleared\nU1: Comment cleared. \nU0: Please remove all City of Pflugerville Notes and show the following City of Austin site plan release notes on the site plan:\na. All improvements shall be made in accordance with the released site plan. Any additional improvements will require site plan amendment and approval of the Development Services Department.\nb. Approval of this Site Plan does not include Building and Fire Code approval nor building permit approval. \nc. All signs must comply with requirements of the Land Development Code (Chapter 25-10).\nd. Additional electric easements may be required at a later date. \ne. Water and wastewater service will be provided by the City of Austin (or identify the service provider if other than the City of Austin). \nf. All existing structures shown to be removed will require a demolition permit from the City of Austin Development Services Department.\ng. No certificate of occupancy may be issued for the proposed residential condominium project until the owner or owners of the property have complied with Chapter 81 and 82 of the Property Code of the State of Texas or any other statutes enacted by the State concerning condominiums.\nh. For driveway construction: The owner is responsible for all costs for relocation of, or damage to utilities. \ni. For construction within the right-of-way, a ROW excavation permit is required.\n","numLines":55,"startLine":1,"totalLines":55}}}
{"level":30,"time":1776974041787,"pid":123,"hostname":"844f2260-bff","step":"review-runs","item":"15.md","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QukEM1eZqZC2stMtoNk7n3","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# General Information and Case Manager Review\n     2→\n     3→*Provides project details, update deadlines, submittal requirements, and the case manager's initial site plan comments.*\n     4→\n     5→This Master Comment Report includes all staff comments received to date about your most recent site plan submittal. The comments may include requirements, recommendations, or information. The requirements in this report must be addressed by an updated site plan submittal.\n     6→\n     7→Case Number: SP-2025-0126C\n     8→Revision #: 00 Update: U1\n     9→Case Manager: Jim Gobel\n    10→Phone #: (512) 978-6414 Email: Jim.Gobel@austintexas.gov\n    11→\n    12→Project Name: Valley View Townhomes\n    13→Location: 3759 VALLEY VIEW RD \n    14→\n    15→Submittal Date: September 18, 2025\n    16→Report Due Date: October 2, 2025\n    17→Final Report Date: October 2, 2025\n    18→\n    19→Update Deadline (Expiration Date): May 26, 2026\n    20→\n    21→Final Update Deadline [LDC § 25-5-113]:\n    22→* Failure to submit a final update by the deadline will result in the automatic denial of the application, unless:\n    23→  (1) The site plan application has been approved; or \n    24→  (2) A request for an extension has been granted. [LDC § 25-1-82(F)]\n    25→* If the deadline falls on a weekend or City of Austin holiday, the next City of Austin workday will be the deadline.\n    26→* The applicant or their agent is responsible for updating this site plan application and clearing all comments.\n    27→\n    28→Update Submittals: \n    29→* A formal update submittal is required. Updates can be submitted through the Site Plan Update and Formal Web Form. Updates submitted after 3:00 p.m. may be processed on the following business day.\n    30→* A written response to every comment is required in addition to the updated plan set.\n    31→* More comments may be generated as a result of information or design changes provided in your update.\n    32→\n    33→Site Plan Approval:\n    34→* The site plan will be approved when all requirements from each review discipline have been addressed.\n    35→\n    36→REVIEWERS:\n    37→Case Manager: Jim Gobel\n    38→Electric: Rosemary Avila\n    39→TPW-TDS: Suzy Riley\n    40→Drainage Engineering: Amy Papa\n    41→City Arborist: Alexander DeRoehn\n    42→Fire For Site Plan: Constantino Mendoza\n    43→PARD / Planning & Design: Suzannah DesRoches\n    44→Site Plan: Kate Castles\n    45→Site Plan Plumbing: Cory Harmon\n    46→AW Utility Development Services: Derek Tucker\n    47→Water Quality: Amy Papa\n    48→AW Pipeline Engineering: Daniel Lofton\n    49→AW OWB Review: Natalie Ortiz\n    50→\n    51→Case Manager Review - Jim Gobel - (512) 978-6414 jim.gobel@austintexas.gov\n    52→\n    53→The following case manager comments still need to be addressed or applied to each sheet in the plan set:\n    54→\n    55→CM 8 – Current Status: Not Cleared\n    56→* U0: Please indicate the case number (SP-2025-0126C) in the lower right margin of each sheet.\n    57→* U1: There are several sheets that the site plan number does not appear as required.\n    58→\n    59→CM 10 – Current Status: Not Cleared\n    60→* U0: Provide a blank 1\" x 1\" space in the lower right-hand corner on each sheet for batch stamping at time of permitting. Note: No signature blocks should be within the space.\n    61→* U1: It appears that an undefined area is provided on some of the sheets but these areas to be on all pages, including the landscape pages.\n    62→ \n    63→CM 11 – Current Status: Partially Cleared\n    64→* U0: Add the following approval block to lower right of coversheet only:\n    65→* U1: Please change Development Services Department to Austin Development Services as highlighted below. This change is permanent as of October 1, 2025.\n    66→\n    67→SITE PLAN APPROVAL\n    68→CASE NUMBER SP-2025-0126C            APPLICATION DATE May 20, 2025\n    69→APPROVED ON ________________ ☐ ADMINISTRATIVELY ☐ BY COMMISSION \n    70→UNDER SECTION ☐112 ☐142 OF CHAPTER  25-5 OF THE CITY OF AUSTIN CODE \n    71→EXPIRATION DATE (LDC 25-5-81) ___________ CASE MANAGER Jim Gobel\n    72→_____________________________________________________________________ \n    73→AUSTIN DEVELOPMENT SERVICES\n    74→RELEASED FOR GENERAL COMPLIANCE______________ZONING____________ \n    75→____________________________________________________________________ \n    76→APPROVAL STAMPS: \n    77→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"33f519bd-bced-4a7a-aae5-831dbf134acc","uuid":"1cccf88d-dfac-48a5-a353-e5db88c7bdb3","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/vercel/sandbox/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/supplementary-docs/master-comment-report/01-general-information-and-case-manager-review.md","content":"# General Information and Case Manager Review\n\n*Provides project details, update deadlines, submittal requirements, and the case manager's initial site plan comments.*\n\nThis Master Comment Report includes all staff comments received to date about your most recent site plan submittal. The comments may include requirements, recommendations, or information. The requirements in this report must be addressed by an updated site plan submittal.\n\nCase Number: SP-2025-0126C\nRevision #: 00 Update: U1\nCase Manager: Jim Gobel\nPhone #: (512) 978-6414 Email: Jim.Gobel@austintexas.gov\n\nProject Name: Valley View Townhomes\nLocation: 3759 VALLEY VIEW RD \n\nSubmittal Date: September 18, 2025\nReport Due Date: October 2, 2025\nFinal Report Date: October 2, 2025\n\nUpdate Deadline (Expiration Date): May 26, 2026\n\nFinal Update Deadline [LDC § 25-5-113]:\n* Failure to submit a final update by the deadline will result in the automatic denial of the application, unless:\n  (1) The site plan application has been approved; or \n  (2) A request for an extension has been granted. [LDC § 25-1-82(F)]\n* If the deadline falls on a weekend or City of Austin holiday, the next City of Austin workday will be the deadline.\n* The applicant or their agent is responsible for updating this site plan application and clearing all comments.\n\nUpdate Submittals: \n* A formal update submittal is required. Updates can be submitted through the Site Plan Update and Formal Web Form. Updates submitted after 3:00 p.m. may be processed on the following business day.\n* A written response to every comment is required in addition to the updated plan set.\n* More comments may be generated as a result of information or design changes provided in your update.\n\nSite Plan Approval:\n* The site plan will be approved when all requirements from each review discipline have been addressed.\n\nREVIEWERS:\nCase Manager: Jim Gobel\nElectric: Rosemary Avila\nTPW-TDS: Suzy Riley\nDrainage Engineering: Amy Papa\nCity Arborist: Alexander DeRoehn\nFire For Site Plan: Constantino Mendoza\nPARD / Planning & Design: Suzannah DesRoches\nSite Plan: Kate Castles\nSite Plan Plumbing: Cory Harmon\nAW Utility Development Services: Derek Tucker\nWater Quality: Amy Papa\nAW Pipeline Engineering: Daniel Lofton\nAW OWB Review: Natalie Ortiz\n\nCase Manager Review - Jim Gobel - (512) 978-6414 jim.gobel@austintexas.gov\n\nThe following case manager comments still need to be addressed or applied to each sheet in the plan set:\n\nCM 8 – Current Status: Not Cleared\n* U0: Please indicate the case number (SP-2025-0126C) in the lower right margin of each sheet.\n* U1: There are several sheets that the site plan number does not appear as required.\n\nCM 10 – Current Status: Not Cleared\n* U0: Provide a blank 1\" x 1\" space in the lower right-hand corner on each sheet for batch stamping at time of permitting. Note: No signature blocks should be within the space.\n* U1: It appears that an undefined area is provided on some of the sheets but these areas to be on all pages, including the landscape pages.\n \nCM 11 – Current Status: Partially Cleared\n* U0: Add the following approval block to lower right of coversheet only:\n* U1: Please change Development Services Department to Austin Development Services as highlighted below. This change is permanent as of October 1, 2025.\n\nSITE PLAN APPROVAL\nCASE NUMBER SP-2025-0126C            APPLICATION DATE May 20, 2025\nAPPROVED ON ________________ ☐ ADMINISTRATIVELY ☐ BY COMMISSION \nUNDER SECTION ☐112 ☐142 OF CHAPTER  25-5 OF THE CITY OF AUSTIN CODE \nEXPIRATION DATE (LDC 25-5-81) ___________ CASE MANAGER Jim Gobel\n_____________________________________________________________________ \nAUSTIN DEVELOPMENT SERVICES\nRELEASED FOR GENERAL COMPLIANCE______________ZONING____________ \n____________________________________________________________________ \nAPPROVAL STAMPS: \n","numLines":77,"startLine":1,"totalLines":77}}}
{"level":30,"time":1776974044106,"pid":123,"hostname":"844f2260-bff","step":"review-runs","item":"16.md","index":8,"runIndex":"run-3","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":9,"prompt":"Please carefully examine the North and South property boundaries on Sheet 9 (Site Plan) and provide: (1) What land use descriptions or property names are labeled on the North side of the property boundary (if any)? (2) What land use descriptions or property names are labeled on the South side of the property boundary (if any)? (3) Are there any building footprints shown on the North side within approximately 50 feet of the subject site boundary? (4) Are there any building footprints shown on the South side within approximately 50 feet of the subject site boundary? (5) What zoning labels, if any, appear for the North and South properties? (6) Is there any note that says \"no buildings exist on adjoining lots within 50 feet\" on any of the property boundaries?","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a careful examination of Sheet 9 (Site Plan), here are the details regarding the North and South property boundaries (with North oriented towards the top of the page, as indicated by the North arrow on the right side):\n\n**(1) Land use descriptions or property names labeled on the North side:**\nThere are no specific property names or general land use descriptions labeled on the North side of the boundary. The text visible immediately above the North property line consists only of a zoning label and easement/record information: \"5' P.U.E.\", \"Vol. 73, Pg. 76\", and \"P.R.T.C.Tx.\"\n\n**(2) Land use descriptions or property names labeled on the South side:**\nThe property on the South side of the boundary is labeled with the name `\"William John Tinnin, Jr.\"` along with deed record information `\"Vol. 69, Pg. 14\"` and `\"F.R.T.C.Tx.\"`\n\n**(3) Building footprints shown on the North side within approximately 50 feet:**\nThere are no building footprints drawn on the North side of the subject site boundary.\n\n**(4) Building footprints shown on the South side within approximately 50 feet:**\nThere are no building footprints drawn on the South side of the subject site boundary.\n\n**(5) Zoning labels for the North and South properties:**\n*   **North:** There is a zoning label visible just above the North property line (near the top center of the site plan) that reads `\"Zoning: MF-4-CO\"`. \n*   **South:** There is no zoning label visible for the property on the South side of the boundary.\n\n**(6) Specific note about adjoining lots:**\nNo. A review of the property boundaries and all general notes on the page confirms that there is no note stating `\"no buildings exist on adjoining lots within 50 feet\"`.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1476,"outputTokens":405,"totalTokens":4161,"reasoningTokens":2280},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 2702484]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just because you do not find evidence for a requirement on this page does not mean it will not be present on another