{"level":30,"time":1776974056843,"pid":123,"hostname":"844f2260-bff","step":"review-runs","item":"16.md","index":2,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_0187Ls5HYfyQffiy7VSQ17zH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Important finding: The site plan shows NO central trash receptacles/dumpster on the drawing. Instead, the Trash Collection Notes indicate that trash containers shall not be left at curbside unattended - implying roll-away bins per unit.\n\nThis is relevant to ZLU-16.27, which requires \"Dumpster or permanently placed refuse receptacle located within 20 feet of a property used or zoned SF-5 or more restrictive\" to be flagged.\n\nIf there are NO permanently placed refuse receptacles shown on the site plan, then ZLU-16.27 cannot be marked as \"fail\" or even \"not-verifiable\" - it would be N/A or the condition doesn't apply. However, the grouping defines ZLU-16.27 with applicability \"All sites with a dumpster or permanently placed refuse receptacle.\" Since none is shown, the applicability condition is not met, so this item is N/A.\n\nNow let me compile my findings. First, let me create a summary of what I've researched:\n\n**RESEARCH SUMMARY:**\n\n**Site Profile:**\n- Valley View Townhomes, 3759 Valley View Road, Austin TX 78704\n- Site Zoning: MF-2 (Multi-Family Low Density)\n- Proposed Use: 39 multi-family townhome units (8 buildings)\n- Adjacent Zoning: SF-3 (immediate neighbor), GO, MF-3, MF-3-CO, MF-2-CO\n\n**Article 10 Applicability:**\n- Site is MF-2, which is MORE restrictive than MF-4\n- Article 10 applies only to sites zoned MF-4 or LESS restrictive (more intensive)\n- **CONCLUSION: Article 10 DOES NOT APPLY** to this site\n- Items ZLU-16.14 through ZLU-16.26 are all N/A\n\n**General Documentation Items (Apply to All Sites):**\n\n\nLooking at the site plan, I can see that adjoining land uses are only documented on the east side—\"Existing Apartment Building\" and \"Clarion Ridge Condominiums\" are clearly labeled. The north side shows only zoning designation (MF-4-CO) without identifying the actual land use type. The south and west sides lack explicit land use documentation as well, with only faint references to \"Valley View\" and \"Creek Pointe\" that don't clearly identify what those properties are used for. This means ZLU-16.1 fails because not all four sides have their adjoining land uses properly noted. For ZLU-16.2, I need to examine what land uses exist across the street from the south side of the property.\n\nThe text on the drawing for properties across the street to the south is too faint and unclear to determine their actual land use type, making ZLU-16.2 not verifiable from the drawing alone. I also cannot tell from the site plan which adjacent properties, if any, are vacant, so ZLU-16.3 is not verifiable. Regarding zoning, the north side shows MF-4-CO and the east shows MF-2-CO, but the south and west sides have no zoning labels at all—this is a failure for ZLU-16.4. Additionally, there's an inconsistency between what the site plan indicates (MF-4-CO to the north) and what facts.md lists as adjacent zoning (SF-3, GO, MF-3, MF-3-CO, MF-2-CO), suggesting a discrepancy that needs clarification for ZLU-16.5. The parcel IDs in facts.md don't specify directional locations, so I can't directly cross-reference which zoning applies to which side. However, facts.md lists MF-2-CO as adjacent but doesn't mention MF-4-CO, yet the site plan shows MF-4-CO on the north side. This gap suggests either the site plan incorrectly identifies the northern zoning, or there's an unlisted property. I need to verify whether the zoning designations on the site plan actually correspond to the parcels documented in facts.md, particularly for the north side discrepancy.\n\nFor ZLU-16.5, the mismatch between what's shown and what's documented raises concerns about accuracy against current City records. The site plan displays zoning on only the north and east boundaries while the south and west sides remain unlabeled, despite the property abutting multiple districts including SF-3, GO, MF-3, MF-3-CO, and MF-2-CO. This incomplete labeling makes it difficult to confirm all boundary conditions are properly documented.\n\nZLU-16.8 requires checking the mylars themselves to verify zoning designations appear there. For ZLU-16.9, existing building footprints are only shown on the east side with dashed outlines for the apartment building, but the north, south, and west boundaries lack any building representations despite neighbors existing on those sides. Since adjacent structures are documented to exist nearby, their absence from the plan is problematic.\n\nZLU-16.10 doesn't apply here—buildings do exist on neighboring lots, so the note requirement for when no adjacent buildings are present isn't triggered. The proposed building dimensions pass verification through the plan's width/depth notation and the height table. The perimeter boundary also passes, shown as a solid dark outline around all structures. For ZLU-16.13, I need to assess whether the site meets the criteria for identifying property connections—specifically whether it's 3+ acres in a non-residential zone or has parking between the building and principal street, with the site currently zoned MF-2. (b) more carefully. The vision output describes \"internal driveways and concrete/decomposed granite walkways,\" which indicates parking and access are routed within the site rather than positioned between buildings and the principal street. This means condition (b) doesn't apply either.\n\nFor the parking screening requirements, ZLU-16.29 doesn't apply since the site is zoned MF-2 (residential), not non-residential. ZLU-16.30 is potentially relevant given the site has over 10 parking spaces in a residential zone, so I need to evaluate whether it adjoins a residential district.\n\nThe adjacent properties are zoned SF-3, MF-3, MF-3-CO, and MF-2-CO—all residential. With 88 total parking spaces (10 surface plus 78 garage), the requirement for 6-foot minimum screening applies. The vision tool shows a wood fence on the east boundary and retaining walls, but I need to confirm these meet the height requirement. ZLU-16.31 and 16.32 don't apply since there's no Waterfront Overlay designation. ZLU-16.33 addresses service station screening, which isn't relevant here.\n\nFor exterior lighting, the site plan explicitly states all fixtures will be full cut-off and fully shielded per Subchapter E 2.5, satisfying ZLU-16.34. Regarding ZLU-16.35, the three-story building and site notes reference the same shielding standard, though this focuses on hooding rather than floor-level restrictions for residential adjacency.\n\nThe site plan avoids repealed code sections, instead citing current standards like Subchapter E 2.5 and LDC 25-2-1007(F)(4). For mechanical equipment noise limits, I need to examine what the site plan specifies regarding the 70 dB(A) threshold.\n\nSince this is a residential MF-2 property with adjacent residential uses, mechanical equipment noise standards apply. However, the available documentation doesn't include a mechanical equipment schedule or noise specifications, making this requirement unverifiable from the submitted materials.\n\nRegarding trash collection, the site plan shows no central dumpster or permanently placed refuse receptacle. The notes indicate containers won't remain at curbside, suggesting the project uses individual collection rather than a centralized system. Since no permanently placed receptacle exists, the 20-foot setback requirement from SF-5+ zoning doesn't apply.\n\nNow checking the mylars for ZLU-16.8 compliance.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":10,"cache_creation_input_tokens":914,"cache_read_input_tokens":67458,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":914,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_t