{"level":30,"time":1776974059268,"pid":123,"hostname":"844f2260-bff","step":"review-runs","item":"15.md","index":6,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FChohB5MYW2R7jRWWdPVK4","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Sheet 38 — Wall Plan\n     2→\n     3→Plan view, section details, and notes for retaining walls.\n     4→\n     5→## Reading Guide\n     6→\n     7→This sheet provides the structural details, plan view, and specifications for retaining walls, including a 14'-0\" maximum height retaining wall section. Its primary purpose is to guide the construction, reinforcement, and inspection of the site's retaining walls, footings, and associated slab tie-ins.\n     8→\n     9→**Key values**:\n    10→* Maximum retaining wall height: 14'-0\"\n    11→* Concrete compressive strength: 3,000 PSI (minimum 28-day)\n    12→* Allowable soil bearing: 4,000 PSF\n    13→* Active soil pressure (heel): 45.5 PSF\n    14→* Passive pressure: 290 PSF\n    15→* Soil weight: 130 PSF\n    16→* Reinforcing steel grades: Grade 60 (for #4 rebar and larger), Grade 40 (for #3 rebar)\n    17→* Wall vertical reinforcement: #7 @ 10\" O.C.\n    18→* Wall horizontal reinforcement: #3 @ 12\" O.C. (each face)\n    19→* Minimum concrete clear cover: 3\" for surfaces in contact with earth; 1 1/2\" for walls/footings adjacent to exterior/interior surfaces; 1 1/2\" above sub-grade for slabs\n    20→* Dowel embedment: 6\" embedment for #6 rebar dowels into existing concrete\n    21→\n    22→**Content blocks on this sheet**:\n    23→\n    24→* **Block 2**: diagram — 14'-0\" Max Retaining Wall cross-section showing rebar spacing, gravel backfill, weep pipes, and geotextile placement. READ for exact rebar sizing and material specifications, VISION for structural layout and dimensions.\n    25→* **Block 4**: drawing — Plan View showing the layout of the new and existing retaining walls, pond walls, and specific doweling instructions for an existing buttress. Use VISION to understand the spatial relationship, alignment, and construction phasing between new and existing walls.\n    26→* **Block 1**: diagram — Dowel Detail showing a cross-section for tying a new slab to an existing slab with #6 rebar. READ for drill bit sizing (7/8\" for #4), epoxy installation instructions, and hand-installation notes.\n    27→* **Block 3**: diagram — Typical Step in Footing elevation view showing standard 2'-0\" horizontal and 12\" vertical step dimensions. Use VISION for step geometry and reinforcement continuity.\n    28→* **Block 10**: table — Design Criteria outlining IBC 2015 soil bearing and lateral pressure requirements. READ for the exact engineering design values.\n    29→* **Block 6**: notes — General and structural notes detailing concrete specifications, clear cover minimums, and reinforcement rules. READ for material grades, cover depths, and corner bar requirements (24\"x24\").\n    30→* **Block 9**: table — Required Inspections list. READ to confirm the three key inspection milestones (footings, walls, backfill/drainage).\n    31→* **Blocks 5, 7, 8**: various — Boilerplate & Administrative. Contains a general schematic disclaimer (Block 5), title block data for project 3759 Valley View (Block 7), and engineer seals for MLAW Engineers (Block 8).\n    32→\n    33→---\n    34→\n    35→All other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n    36→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"67c41a7e-de71-427c-8abb-98ffa8658f39","uuid":"3c542d15-cd30-42e4-a860-71ebf1fc22a8","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/vercel/sandbox/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-38/guide.md","content":"# Sheet 38 — Wall Plan\n\nPlan view, section details, and notes for retaining walls.\n\n## Reading Guide\n\nThis sheet provides the structural details, plan view, and specifications for retaining walls, including a 14'-0\" maximum height retaining wall section. Its primary purpose is to guide the construction, reinforcement, and inspection of the site's retaining walls, footings, and associated slab tie-ins.\n\n**Key values**:\n* Maximum retaining wall height: 14'-0\"\n* Concrete compressive strength: 3,000 PSI (minimum 28-day)\n* Allowable soil bearing: 4,000 PSF\n* Active soil pressure (heel): 45.5 PSF\n* Passive pressure: 290 PSF\n* Soil weight: 130 PSF\n* Reinforcing steel grades: Grade 60 (for #4 rebar and larger), Grade 40 (for #3 rebar)\n* Wall vertical reinforcement: #7 @ 10\" O.C.\n* Wall horizontal reinforcement: #3 @ 12\" O.C. (each face)\n* Minimum concrete clear cover: 3\" for surfaces in contact with earth; 1 1/2\" for walls/footings adjacent to exterior/interior surfaces; 1 1/2\" above sub-grade for slabs\n* Dowel embedment: 6\" embedment for #6 rebar dowels into existing concrete\n\n**Content blocks on this sheet**:\n\n* **Block 2**: diagram — 14'-0\" Max Retaining Wall cross-section showing rebar spacing, gravel backfill, weep pipes, and geotextile placement. READ for exact rebar sizing and material specifications, VISION for structural layout and dimensions.\n* **Block 4**: drawing — Plan View showing the layout of the new and existing retaining walls, pond walls, and specific doweling instructions for an existing buttress. Use VISION to understand the spatial relationship, alignment, and construction phasing between new and existing walls.\n* **Block 1**: diagram — Dowel Detail showing a cross-section for tying a new slab to an existing slab with #6 rebar. READ for drill bit sizing (7/8\" for #4), epoxy installation instructions, and hand-installation notes.\n* **Block 3**: diagram — Typical Step in Footing elevation view showing standard 2'-0\" horizontal and 12\" vertical step dimensions. Use VISION for step geometry and reinforcement continuity.\n* **Block 10**: table — Design Criteria outlining IBC 2015 soil bearing and lateral pressure requirements. READ for the exact engineering design values.\n* **Block 6**: notes — General and structural notes detailing concrete specifications, clear cover minimums, and reinforcement rules. READ for material grades, cover depths, and corner bar requirements (24\"x24\").\n* **Block 9**: table — Required Inspections list. READ to confirm the three key inspection milestones (footings, walls, backfill/drainage).\n* **Blocks 5, 7, 8**: various — Boilerplate & Administrative. Contains a general schematic disclaimer (Block 5), title block data for project 3759 Valley View (Block 7), and engineer seals for MLAW Engineers (Block 8).\n\n---\n\nAll other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n","numLines":36,"startLine":1,"totalLines":36}}}
{"level":30,"time":1776974061703,"pid":123,"hostname":"844f2260-bff","step":"review-runs","item":"16.md","index":5,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01YWiDkq26834G17LinS3sS5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Let me continue evaluating the remaining checklist items. I'll assess items 16.1, 16.3, 16.5, 16.6, 16.7, 16.10, 16.11, 16.12, 16.13, and the remaining general applicability items.\n\nFor **ZLU-16.1** (Adjoining land uses noted on all four sides):\n- North: MF-2-CO labeled ✓\n- East: MF-2-CO labeled ✓  \n- South: SF (Single Family) labeled ✓\n- West: NOT labeled ✗\n- **STATUS: FAIL** (west side missing)\n\nFor **ZLU-16.3** (Vacant properties identified):\n- No vacant properties indicated on any side\n- **STATUS: PASS** (not applicable as no vacant properties noted)\n\nFor **ZLU-16.5** (Zoning accuracy vs GIS):\n- Cannot verify from submitted plans; would require GIS comparison\n- **STATUS: NOT-VERIFIABLE**\n\nFor **ZLU-16.6** & **ZLU-16.7** (PUD boundaries):\n- Site is not in a PUD; no PUD shown on site plan\n- **STATUS: N/A** (not in/adjacent to PUD)\n\nFor **ZLU-16.10** (Note absent when no buildings within 50 feet):\n- Sheet 4 (Existing Conditions Survey) shows NO buildings on adjoining properties\n- Site Plan Sheet 9 shows \"Existing Apartment Building\" on east\n- Discrepancy makes it unclear if note is required\n- No note present stating \"no buildings exist on adjoining lots within 50 feet\"\n- **STATUS: NOT-VERIFIABLE** (due to building discrepancy)\n\nFor **ZLU-16.11** (Proposed building dimensions shown):\n- Sheet 9 Site Data Table shows building heights and coverage\n- Building Data Table shows square footages\n- Dimension lines visible on site plan\n- **STATUS: PASS**\n\nFor **ZLU-16.12** (Continuous perimeter boundary line for complete building footprint):\n- Site plan shows buildings with footprint outlines\n- **STATUS: PASS**\n\nFor **ZLU-16.13** (Property connections to adjacent lots):\n- Applicability trigger: (a) net site area ≥3 acres in non-residential, OR (b) parking between building and principal street\n- Site area: 2.16 acres (not ≥3 acres)\n- Parking location: Mixed (10 surface + 78 garage in multi-story structures)\n- Principal street is Valley View Road (west side)\n- Parking appears to be internal to site and not between buildings and street\n- **STATUS: N/A** (does not meet applicability thresholds)\n\nFor **ZLU-16.14 through ZLU-16.28** (Article 10 items):\n- Site zoning is MF-2 (NOT MF-4 or less restrictive)\n- Per grouping: \"Sites zoned MF-3 or more restrictive...are NOT subject to Article 10\"\n- MF-2 is more restrictive than MF-4\n- **STATUS: N/A** for all Article 10-specific items\n\nFor **ZLU-16.27** (Dumpster 20 ft from SF-5 or more restrictive):\n- South adjacent property: SF-3 (which is SF-5 or more restrictive)\n- Site plan shows trash note but no specific dumpster location marked\n- Trash containers noted as \"shall not be left at curbside unattended\"\n- No dimension or distance measurement shown for dumpster location relative to south property line\n- **STATUS: NOT-VERIFIABLE** (dumpster location not specified on plans)\n\nFor **ZLU-16.29** (Parking screening for non-residential adjacent to residential):\n- Site parking is residential (multi-family townhomes)\n- Even though adjacent to SF-3, this item applies to \"non-residential parking\" in non-residential zones adjacent to residential\n- Site is MF-2 (residential zone), not non-residential\n- **STATUS: N/A**\n\nFor **ZLU-16.30** (Residential parking >10 spaces adjacent to residential):\n- Site has 88 parking spaces (>10)\n- Adjacent properties: SF-3 (south), MF-2-CO (north/east)\n- Item requires residential parking >10 spaces \"in a residential district adjoining another residential-district property\"\n- Site is MF-2 (residential); south is SF-3 (also residential)\n- This item applies when parking is adjacent to another residential property\n- Parking is interior to site; would need to verify proximity to SF-3 boundary\n- Vision showed 10 surface spaces but location not precisely detailed\n- **STATUS: NOT-VERIFIABLE** (parking layout and proximity to SF-3 boundary not clearly detailed enough to determine if screening requirement applies and if met)\n\nFor **ZLU-16.33** (Service station screening):\n- Proposed use is 39 townhome units (multi-family residential)\n- Not a service station\n- **STATUS: N/A**\n\nFor **ZLU-16.34** (Exterior lighting hooded/shielded adjacent to residential):\n- Sheet 9 Block 1 states: \"All exterior lighting will be full cut-off and fully shielded in compliance with Subchapter E 2.5\"\n- Adjacent to residential uses (SF-3 south, MF-2-CO north/east)\n- Requirement is stated as general note\n- However, this is stated generally for \"Subchapter E 2.5\" compliance, which is broader than Article 10\n- The General Site Plan Notes require this for \"all sites\"\n- **STATUS: PASS** (note indicates compliance, though details on fixture locations/cut sheets not provided)\n\nFor **ZLU-16.35** (No exterior lighting above second floor facing residential):\n- Proposed buildings are max 3 stories\n- Note states lighting \"to be reviewed during building plan review\" and \"will be in compliance with Subchapter E 2.5\"\n- Specific prohibition of third-floor fixtures facing residential not explicitly stated on site plan\n- **STATUS: NOT-VERIFIABLE** (fixture locations and third-floor specifications deferred to building plan review)\n\nFor **ZLU-16.36** (No citations to repealed sections):\n- Sheet 9 Block 1 cites \"Subchapter E 2.5\" (not repealed Article 10 sections)\n- No citations to 25-2-1064, 25-2-1066, or 25-2-1067 found\n- **STATUS: PASS** (no repealed sections cited)\n\nFor **ZLU-16.37** (Mechanical equipment noise ≤70 dB(A)):\n- No mechanical equipment schedule provided\n- No noise ratings documented\n- Equipment locations not specified\n- **STATUS: NOT-VERIFIABLE** (no mechanical equipment schedule or noise ratings provided)\n\nNow let me output all the remaining findings:"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":9,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1728,"cache_read_input_tokens":65667,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1728,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f8d013d8-a941-49c2-99ab-d6f637200362","uuid":"d525ae9a-5e24-4ce0-8e9f-a9c3f65cca8b"}
