{"level":30,"time":1776974073224,"pid":123,"hostname":"844f2260-bff","step":"review-runs","item":"15.md","index":9,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01YFS5z3vDqmcUCsy5Mc8XPB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I don't see mention of dumpsters in the landscape plan blocks. Let me check the site plan to see if trash/dumpster areas are shown. Actually, I remember from sheet 9 blocks that there were \"Trash Collection Notes\" in Block 7 of the site plan. Let me check the fire protection plan or site plan more carefully to see if trash enclosures are shown.\n\nActually, I should focus on completing my evaluation now. Based on my research, here are the key deficiencies I've found:\n\nFINDINGS - FAIL or NOT VERIFIABLE ONLY:\n\n1. **ZLU-15.7: Compatibility standards (Article 10) applicability incorrectly determined**\n   - STATUS: FAIL\n   - The site is MF-2 (less restrictive than MF-4) and adjacent to an SF-3 zoned parcel (triggering property) within 75 feet\n   - The consolidated site plan application form marked \"Subject to Compatibility Standards? NO\" - this is incorrect\n   - Article 10 § 25-2-1051 and § 25-2-1053 ARE triggered\n   - The site plan contains NO reference to Article 10 compatibility standards\n   - CODE: LDC § 25-2-1051; LDC § 25-2-1052; LDC § 25-2-1053\n\n2. **ZLU-15.10: Compatibility buffer not shown at the correct width**\n   - STATUS: FAIL\n   - A 25-foot compatibility buffer is required along the shared property line per § 25-2-1062(B)\n   - The site plan shows NO compatibility buffer line\n   - Building 6 is positioned at 24.8 feet from the southern property line, encroaching into the required buffer zone\n   - CODE: LDC § 25-2-1062(B); LDC § 25-8-700\n\n3. **ZLU-15.13: Triggering property not clearly identified on site plan**\n   - STATUS: FAIL\n   - The William James Estate parcel (SF-3 zoned) is not labeled on the site plan, making it impossible to verify Article 10 applicability per § 25-2-1053\n   - CODE: LDC § 25-2-1053; LDC § 25-2-1063\n\n4. **ZLU-15.26: Separate compatibility exhibit not provided**\n   - STATUS: FAIL\n   - No standalone compatibility exhibit sheet exists showing property boundaries, zoning boundaries, distances to triggering property, and building locations as required by Reviewer Convention\n   - CODE: Reviewer Convention\n\n5. **ZLU-15.27: Compatibility cross\n\n-sections not provided**\n   - STATUS: FAIL\n   - Missing cross-section sheets demonstrating height compliance at the 50-ft and 75-ft thresholds from the triggering property, which is required since buildings fall within 75 feet and must meet § 25-2-1061 height limits\n   - CODE: LDC § 25-2-1061\n\n6. **ZLU-15.1: Required zoning district setback lines**\n   - STATUS: FAIL\n   - The site plan shows only scattered dimension lines (28.8', 25', 26.1') without clear labeling as setback lines; no distinctly marked \"Zoning Setback\" or \"Building Setback\" lines are provided for the MF-2 district\n   - CODE: LDC setback requirements per § 25-2-492 require front, rear, interior side, and street side yard setbacks to be clearly identified\n   - The complete absence of labeled setback lines specific to zoning compliance indicates this requirement is not met\n   - STATUS: FAIL - MF-2 zoning setback requirements must be shown on the site plan per the regulatory standards, and they are not clearly labeled or identified\n   - The vision analysis confirms no dashed lines are marked as setback or compatibility lines\n   - While dimension lines to property boundaries exist, they lack the required labeling to verify compliance with MF-2 setback standards\n   - This constitutes a failure for ZLU-15.1, as the site plan must explicitly show and dimension all required setbacks","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":11,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1903,"cache_read_input_tokens":74