{"level":30,"time":1776974077282,"pid":123,"hostname":"844f2260-bff","step":"review-runs","item":"32.md","index":4,"runIndex":"run-2","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":2,"prompt":"Examine the plat map and provide: 1) Whether this is a single lot (Lot 1) or whether there are multiple subdivided townhouse lots; 2) What the legal description and lot structure is; 3) Any notation about subdivision into individual townhouse lots; 4) The overall structure of the plat recording","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a visual analysis of the provided plat map document, here are the detailed findings regarding your specific questions:\n\n**1) Whether this is a single lot (Lot 1) or whether there are multiple subdivided townhouse lots:**\nThe historical plat map depicted in the center of the page does not show a single lot, nor does it show multiple subdivided individual townhouse lots. Instead, it shows the property subdivided into exactly two lots, clearly labeled as \"**LOT 1**\" and \"**LOT 2**\". \n\n**2) What the legal description and lot structure is:**\n*   **Legal Description:** According to the \"KNOW ALL MEN BY THESE PRESENTS\" dedication text block on the top right, the original property is described as: *\"Lot A, Trico Subdivision, a subdivision out of the Isaac Decker League according to a map or plat of record in Book 69, Page 14, in the Plat Records of Travis County, Texas\"*.\n*   **Lot Structure:** The plat adopts this tract to be known and designated as the \"**MECEY SUBDIVISION**\". The visual map structures this subdivision by splitting the original tract into two adjacent lots: \"LOT 1\" (bordering \"VALLEY VIEW ROAD\" to the west) and \"LOT 2\" (bordering \"CLAWSON ROAD\" to the east).\n\n**3) Any notation about subdivision into individual townhouse lots:**\nThere is **no notation** anywhere on the historical plat map, owner's dedication, surveyor's notes, or city approval text regarding subdivision into individual townhouse lots. The word \"townhouse\" or \"townhome\" does not appear in any of the historical recording text. \n*Note:* The only reference to townhomes is found in the modern title block added to the far right margin by the engineering firm, which labels the overall project as \"**Valley View Townhomes**\".\n\n**4) The overall structure of the plat recording:**\nThe document is a reproduction of a historical plat recording, specifically labeled at the top as \"**TRAVIS COUNTY PLAT VOLUME 73 PAGE 76**\" for the \"**MECEY SUBDIVISION**\". Its structure includes standard municipal and county recording elements:\n*   **City Approvals (Top Left):** Contains blocks for \"APPROVED FOR ACCEPTANCE\" by the Director of Planning (signed Richard R. Lillie) and \"ACCEPTED AND AUTHORIZED FOR RECORD BY THE CITY PLANNING COMMISSION, CITY OF AUSTIN, TEXAS\" (signed by the Vice Chairman), both dated \"12-11-75\".\n*   **County Clerk Recording (Left):** Two text blocks from \"THE STATE OF TEXAS COUNTY OF TRAVIS\" certifying the filing for record by \"Doris Shropshire, Clerk of County Court\" on the \"11 day of Dec. A.D. 1975\" and recorded in \"Book 73, Page 76\". Signed by \"Mike Kilgore, Deputy\".\n*   **Owner's Dedication (Top Right):** A formal declaration (\"KNOW ALL MEN BY THESE PRESENTS...\") by the owner, \"Louis Mecey\", dedicating streets and easements and adopting the plat, witnessed and dated \"11th day of September A.D. 1975\".\n*   **Notary Public Certification (Right):** A seal and signature block certifying Louis Mecey's appearance before a notary on the \"11th day of September A.D. 1975\".\n*   **Surveyor's Certification (Bottom Right):** A note reading \"C8s-75-160 This is to certify that Austin City Code Chapter 23-27 of 1954 has been complied with. Surveyed Aug. 20, 1975 By: Forrest B. Scott Reg. Public Surveyor #339 Austin, Texas\".\n*   **Map Features (Center):** The drawn map includes boundary lines with bearings and distances, adjacent subdivisio