{"level":30,"time":1776974083705,"pid":123,"hostname":"844f2260-bff","step":"review-runs","item":"32.md","index":4,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01PX1aKvGLMqv1D7xqWfPA7k","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"CRITICAL FINDING on ZLU-32.31!\n\nThe current site plan shows **Lot 1 only** from the Mecey Subdivision. The plat was created in 1975 and divided a larger tract into **Lot 1** and **Lot 2**.\n\nBut for the townhomes project to comply with LDC § 25-2-775 (Townhouse use), according to the regulation and the Master Comment Report:\n\"Townhouses will need to plat a townhouse subdivision as not more than one townhouse is permitted on a townhouse lot. A townhouse lot must include a private yard with a wall or solid fence along a side lot line.\"\n\nThis means:\n1. For a 39-unit townhome project, there should be 39 separate townhouse lots\n2. Each lot should have a private yard with wall or solid fence on the side lot line\n3. This would require a NEW subdivision plat creating 39 townhouse lots\n\nThe current site plan shows:\n- Single Lot 1 from Mecey Subdivision (1975)\n- 8 multi-unit buildings on one lot\n\nThis FAILS the townhouse requirement under ZLU-32.31. The project would need to either:\n1. Create a new townhouse subdivision plat with 39 individual townhouse lots (each with their own private yards and walls/fences along side lines)\n2. OR redesignate the project as \"Multifamily Residential\" instead of \"Townhouse\"\n\nThe fact that the Master Comment Report shows a comment asking for this clarification suggests the reviewer also identified this issue.\n\nNow let me check the remaining items:\n\n**ZLU-32.35 - Multifamily Transit Proximity:** The requirement is that multifamily residential projects must be within one-half mile walking distance of a public transit route. The applicant can request a director's waiver if not within that distance.\n\nLet me check if the site plan includes a transit route map and documentation of transit proximity.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1255,"cache_read_input_tokens":79016,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1255,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4e7b1c1f-9804-4a61-b82e-41dbab740236","uuid":"c2cff0d8-369a-401d-b322-0efb41486979"}
