{"level":30,"time":1776974085449,"pid":123,"hostname":"844f2260-bff","step":"review-runs","item":"32.md","index":4,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Jm3SXq9CvSux7YpNb2HiBs","type":"tool_result","content":"workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/facts.md:191:The surrounding context is predominantly multi-family and office, consistent with infill development. The single SF-3 parcel is the critical zoning transition requiring Subchapter F compliance.\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/supplementary-docs/property-tax-documentation/03-tax-request-payment-receipt.md:33:If you have any questions regarding this transaction, you may call Government Payments - EZNETPAY at 956-682-3466 during our business hours of 8:00 AM to 5:00 PM CST Monday through Friday.\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/supplementary-docs/master-comment-report/04-drainage-engineering-review.md:109:* U0: Due to the proximity of proposed retaining wall to the ROW, public easement, and/or the neighboring property, this plan needs to be reviewed by the Land Development Engineering division of the Transportation and Public Works Department. Please email PDFs of the plan set to elizabeth.robinson@austintexas.gov and copy this reviewer. This comment will be cleared once an approval memo is provided.\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/supplementary-docs/master-comment-report/03-transportation-public-works-tpw-tds-review.md:53:* U0: On-street parallel parking stalls width shall be measured from the edge of the traveled way to the face of curb. The combination of travel and parking stall next to one another shall be no less than 18 ft. In areas adjacent to transit routes, the minimum shall be 19 ft. Parking is assumed to be 8 ft in width. Dimension the stall width and the width of lane on the site plan. Reference: TCM 9.2.2.A.\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/supplementary-docs/master-comment-report/03-transportation-public-works-tpw-tds-review.md:107:* U1: Comment remains. Waiver request approved, please pay waiver fee. Please ensure sidewalk meets TCM 4.1.3, “Meandering paths should avoid sharp turns or transitions and gradually transition no more than 1 ft. off path per 5 ft. of sidewalk length and maintain a straight section no less than the width of the sidewalk between transitions.”\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/supplementary-docs/master-comment-report/01-general-information-and-case-manager-review.md:29:* A formal update submittal is required. Updates can be submitted through the Site Plan Update and Formal Web Form. Updates submitted after 3:00 p.m. may be processed on the following business day.\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-26/guide.md:35:    Use VISION to examine the acceptable repair couplings and transition couplings for connecting SDR 26 PVC to existing PVC, concrete, clay, and AC mains.\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-26/blocks.md:223:## Block 5: diagram — Details on replacements for existing PVC main and concrete, clay, and AC mains. Shows pipes and joints along with necessary repair and transition couplings.\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-24/blocks.md:103:## Block 15: notes — List of materials required for water service installation, including pipe, saddles, stops, valves, couplings, tubing, meter boxes, and bushings. It distinguishes between items provided by the city and those installed by the plumber.\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-21/guide.md:28:[Omitted long matching line]\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-20/guide.md:7:This sheet contains the public plan and profile for a proposed utility tap (Water Line A) for the Valley View Townhomes project. Its primary purpose is to detail the connection to an existing AC water main, the transition to new DI pipe, and the installation of a new fire demand meter, vault, and fire hydrant.\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-20/guide.md:19:* **Block 1**: drawing — Profile View of Water Line A (Wtr-Ln-A). Shows the vertical alignment of the proposed water line from station 0+00 to 0+75, including the transition from AC to DI pipe, reducers, and the meter vault. Use VISION to examine the pipe slopes and relationship to the existing/proposed ground surfaces, and READ for exact flowline elevations, lengths, and the 52' restraint dimension.\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-16/guide.md:26:    Cross-sectional profile showing the transition from existing ground to proposed surfaces, including an existing retaining wall designated for removal.\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-20/blocks.md:3:## Block 1: drawing — A profile view of the proposed water line installation, showing elevations, pipe slopes, fittings, and existing ground surface. It details the transition from an existing AC pipe to a new DI pipe, including a reducer, vault, and meter.\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-22/guide.md:29:*   **Block 9: diagram — Furnishing Location for Bicycle Racks (COA 710S-6C)**. Shows linear and parallel rack installation footprints. READ for strict spacing rules, utility clearances, and building entry proximity limits; VISION for spatial arrangement diagrams.\n\n[Showing results with pagination = limit: 15, offset: 0]"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4e7b1c1f-9804-4a61-b82e-41dbab740236","uuid":"13795825-b2e0-4f88-9f55-645b25eee6bd","tool_use_result":{"mode":"content","numFiles":0,"filenames":[],"content":"workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/facts.