{"level":30,"time":1776974091762,"pid":123,"hostname":"844f2260-bff","step":"review-runs","item":"32.md","index":4,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011dDXvqrYcJ2RY3kkaYE3Qv","type":"tool_result","content":"workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/supplementary-docs/master-comment-report/04-drainage-engineering-review.md:109:* U0: Due to the proximity of proposed retaining wall to the ROW, public easement, and/or the neighboring property, this plan needs to be reviewed by the Land Development Engineering division of the Transportation and Public Works Department. Please email PDFs of the plan set to elizabeth.robinson@austintexas.gov and copy this reviewer. This comment will be cleared once an approval memo is provided.\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/supplementary-docs/master-comment-report/03-transportation-public-works-tpw-tds-review.md:53:* U0: On-street parallel parking stalls width shall be measured from the edge of the traveled way to the face of curb. The combination of travel and parking stall next to one another shall be no less than 18 ft. In areas adjacent to transit routes, the minimum shall be 19 ft. Parking is assumed to be 8 ft in width. Dimension the stall width and the width of lane on the site plan. Reference: TCM 9.2.2.A.\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/supplementary-docs/master-comment-report/03-transportation-public-works-tpw-tds-review.md:107:* U1: Comment remains. Waiver request approved, please pay waiver fee. Please ensure sidewalk meets TCM 4.1.3, “Meandering paths should avoid sharp turns or transitions and gradually transition no more than 1 ft. off path per 5 ft. of sidewalk length and maintain a straight section no less than the width of the sidewalk between transitions.”"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4e7b1c1f-9804-4a61-b82e-41dbab740236","uuid":"2f5ef5bb-cdad-43a3-8b41-57742fa037ea","tool_use_result":