{"level":30,"time":1776974096187,"pid":123,"hostname":"844f2260-bff","step":"review-runs","item":"16.md","index":2,"runIndex":"run-1","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":31,"prompt":"Looking at the Landscape Plan (Sheet 31), please examine:\n\n1. Are screening fences shown on the landscape plan, particularly along property boundaries adjacent to residential properties (east, north, west)?\n2. What type of screening materials are indicated (wood fence, living vegetation, retaining walls, etc.)?\n3. Are fence/screening heights specified on the plan or in any detail drawings?\n4. Are there any notes on the landscape plan regarding screening or fences and their compliance with setback or height requirements?\n5. Specifically look for any screening between the parking areas and adjacent residential properties\n6. Check if the fence/screening is shown as at least 6 feet in height as required for residential parking adjacent to residential properties\n\nPlease be detailed about what screening materials and heights are specified or shown.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a careful visual analysis of the provided Landscape Plan (labeled Sheet 28 of 35, despite the prompt mentioning Sheet 31), here are the detailed findings regarding your questions:\n\n**1. Are screening fences shown on the landscape plan, particularly along property boundaries adjacent to residential properties (east, north, west)?**\nYes, screening fences are shown on the landscape plan. A continuous line symbol containing 'x' marks (`---x---`) traces the North, East, and South property boundaries. The West boundary (which borders \"Valley View Road\") does not show this fence symbol along the street frontage. \n\n**2. What type of screening materials are indicated (wood fence, living vegetation, retaining walls, etc.)?**\nThe indicated screening materials include a combination of a wooden fence and living vegetation:\n*   **Wooden Fence:** The `---x---` line symbol shown along the boundaries corresponds to \"KEY NOTES\" item **\"H-6\"**, which is explicitly labeled as exactly **\"WOODEN PRIVACY FENCE\"**.\n*   **Living Vegetation:** Trees are shown planted between the parking/drive areas and the property boundaries. The Key Notes indicate specific trees designated for buffering: **\"P - PARKING BUFFER POINT TREE\"**. \n\n**3. Are fence/screening heights specified on the plan or in any detail drawings?**\nNo, there are no fence or screening heights specified anywhere on this specific sheet. The Key Note \"H-6\" identifies the material but does not state a height. There are no detail drawings on this page.\n\n**4. Are there any notes on the landscape plan regarding screening or fences and their compliance with setback or height requirements?**\nNo, there are no notes on this page regarding fence or screening setbacks, heights, or compliance. The notes provided on this sheet (\"IRRIGATION NOTES\" and \"NOTE\") strictly pertain to irrigation system requirements (TCEQ Chapter 344), water budgets, drought staging, and the finished elevation of topsoil in parking lot islands relative to the parking lot elevation.\n\n**5. Specifically look for any screening between the parking areas and adjacent residential properties.**\nAlong the eastern, northern, and southern boundaries, the plan shows the **\"WOODEN PRIVACY FENCE\"** (`---x---`) separating the outer perimeter of the site from the internal drive aisles and parking spaces. Inside this fence line, bordering the parking areas, there are numerous trees plotted. Many of these are explicitly designated as buffering vegetation per the Key Notes (e.g., **\"P - PARKING BUFFER POINT TREE\"** and **\"M - MITIGATION TREE\"**).\n\n**6. Check if the fence/screening is shown as at least 6 feet in height as required for residential parking adjacent to residential properties.**\nBecause no height is specified in the annotations, key notes, or plan view on this sheet, it is **not possible to verify** from this page alone if the wooden privacy fence is at least 6 feet in height.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1476,"outputTokens":620,"totalTokens":4070,"reasoningTokens":1974},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 1755680]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just because you do not find evidence for a requirement on this page does not mean it will not be present on another page.\n\nReport back precisely on what you see, using exact quotes for any text you transcribe from forms, tables, or labels.\n\nThe final review agent will not be able to look at this document directly, so you must be their eyes. Ensure you describe everything relevant in full detail with perfect accuracy.\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Looking at the Landscape Plan (Sheet 31), please examine:\n\n1. Are screening fences shown on the landscape plan, particularly along property boundaries adjacent to residential properties (east, north, west)?\n2. What type of screening materials are indicated (wood fence, living vegetation, retaining walls, etc.)?\n3. Are fence/screening heights specified on the plan or in any detail drawings?\n4. Are there any notes on the landscape plan regarding screening or fences and their compliance with setback or height requirements?\n5. Specifically look for any screening between the parking areas and adjacent residential properties\n6. Check if the fence/screening is shown as at least 6 feet in height as required for residential parking adjacent to residential properties\n\nPlease be detailed about what screening materials and heights are specified or shown."}]}],"headers":{"user-agent":"ai/5.0.152"}}},"response":{"id":"aitxt-MPkNKbIt6Q7r3bwaOA0cQZvt","timestamp":{},"modelId":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","headers":{"access-control-allow-headers":"Content-Type, Authorization, ai-gateway-auth-method, ai-gateway-protocol-version, ai-model-id, ai-language-model-id, ai-language-model-specification-version, ai-image-model-specification-version, ai-embedding-model-specification-version, ai-language-model-streaming, ai-reporting-tags, ai-reporting-user, http-referer, x-title, anthropic-beta","access-control-allow-methods":"GET, POST, PUT, PATCH, DELETE, OPTIONS","access-control-allow-origin":"*","cache-control":"public, max-age=0, must-revalidate","content-encoding":"br","content-type":"application/json","date":"Thu, 23 Apr 2026 19:54:56 GMT","server":"Vercel","strict-transport-security":"max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains; preload","transfer-encoding":"chunked","vary":"rsc, next-router-state-tree, next-router-prefetch, next-router-segment-prefetch","x-matched-path":"/v1/ai/language-model","x-vercel-cache":"MISS","x-vercel-id":"iad1::iad1::7pgn6-1776974073288-2885452d38d2"},"body":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a careful visual analysis of the provided Landscape Plan (labeled Sheet 28 of 35, despite the prompt mentioning Sheet 31), here are the detailed findings regarding your questions:\n\n**1. Are screening fences shown on the landscape plan, particularly along property boundaries adjacent to residential properties (east, north, west)?**\nYes, screening fences are shown on the landscape plan. A continuous line symbol containing 'x' marks (`---x---`) traces the North, East, and South property boundaries. The West boundary (which borders \"Valley View Road\") does not show this fence symbol along the street frontage. \n\n**2. What type of screening materials are indicated (wood fence, living vegetation, retaining walls, etc.)?**\nThe indicated screening materials include a combination of a wooden fence and living vegetation:\n*   **Wooden Fence:** The `---x---` line symbol shown along the boundaries corresponds to \"KEY NOTES\" item **\"H-6\"**, which is explicitly labeled as exactly **\"WOODEN PRIVACY FENCE\"**.\n*   **Living Vegetation:** Trees are shown planted between the parking/drive areas and the property boundaries. The Key Notes indicate specific trees designated for buffering: **\"P - PARKING BUFFER POINT TREE\"**. \n\n**3. Are fence/screening heights specified on the plan or in any detail drawings?**\nNo, there are no fence or screening heights specified anywhere on this specific sheet. The Key Note \"H-6\" identifies the material but does not state a height. There are no detail drawings on this page.\n\n**4. Are there any notes on the landscape plan regarding screening or fences and their compliance with setback or height requirements?**\nNo, there are no notes on this page regarding fence or screening setbacks, heights, or compliance. The notes provided on this sheet (\"IRRIGATION NOTES\" and \"NOTE\") strictly pertain to irrigation system requirements (TCEQ Chapter 344), water budgets, drought staging, and the finished elevation of topsoil in parking lot islands relative to the parking lot elevation.\n\n**5. Specifically look for any screening between the parking areas and adjacent residential properties.**\nAlong the eastern, northern, and southern boundaries, the plan shows the **\"WOODEN PRIVACY FENCE\"** (`---x---`) separating the outer perime