{"level":30,"time":1776974102441,"pid":123,"hostname":"844f2260-bff","step":"review-runs","item":"16.md","index":2,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01AepJWTtvY3agA5FowaKHAt","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Perfect! This is a key finding. The landscape plan shows wooden privacy fences along property boundaries (north, east, south), but NO HEIGHT IS SPECIFIED. The checklist item ZLU-16.30 requires that \"Off-street parking of more than 10 spaces in a residential district adjoining another residential-district property [must be] screened by a wall, fence, or landscape screen at least 6 feet in height along the common boundary.\"\n\nSince no height is specified on the landscape plan, we cannot verify that the fence is 6 feet high. This is a NOT-VERIFIABLE or FAIL finding depending on how you interpret it:\n- If we consider that a fence shown without height specifications cannot be verified to meet the 6-foot minimum, this is NOT-VERIFIABLE\n- If we consider that the applicant must provide evidence of 6-foot compliance and absence of this evidence is a deficiency, this is FAIL\n\nThe checklist item specifically requires the screening to be \"at least 6 feet in height\". Since this is not documented, it cannot be verified.\n\nSTATUS: **NOT-VERIFIABLE** - Wooden privacy fence shown along property lines, but height not specified; cannot verify compliance with 6-foot minimum height requirement.\n\nActually, let me reconsider. The item is asking if the screening IS \"at least 6 feet\". If the height is not shown, then we cannot confirm it meets the requirement. This is arguably a FAIL - the applicant must demonstrate that the fence is 6 feet. The fact that they haven't specified the height in the plans is a deficiency.\n\nHowever, the conservative approach is to mark it as NOT-VERIFIABLE - meaning we cannot determine if the requirement is met from the plans, but it might be verified through field inspection or detailed plans.\n\nI'll go with NOT-VERIFIABLE to be fair to the applicant, noting that fence heights are not specified on the landscape plan.\n\nNow let me compile all my findings into the final output.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":9,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2382,"cache_read_input_tokens":73064,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2382,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"158c3787-95dd-4091-81cc-891db6165072","uuid":"72b0d052-072e-4e08-9593-60eb09ea7039"}
{"level":30,"time":1776974102864,"pid":123,"hostname":"844f2260-bff","step":"review-runs","item":"15.md","index":9,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01LP8emTbVBJjL6REjbf9Ti2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good. Now let me verify I've captured all the necessary findings. Let me review the key deficiencies I found:\n\n1. ZLU-15.1: Zoning setback lines not shown - FAIL ✓\n2. ZLU-15.7: Compatibility applicability incorrectly determined - FAIL ✓\n3. ZLU-15.10: Compatibility buffer not shown at correct width - FAIL ✓\n4. ZLU-15.13: Triggering property not identified - FAIL ✓\n5. ZLU-15.26: No compatibility exhibit - FAIL ✓\n6. ZLU-15.27: No compatibility cross-sections - FAIL ✓\n\nThese are the major issues I found. Let me verify I haven't missed anything critical:\n\n- ZLU-15.8: Compatibility height limits - These are not shown because no cross-sections exist, so this is covered by 15.27\n- ZLU-15.9: Compatibility exhibit showing existing structures on triggering property - This is part of 15.26\n- ZLU-15.11: Buffer line mislabeled - N/A, no buffer shown\n- ZLU-15.12: Buffer incorrectly applied - N/A, no buffer shown\n- ZLU-15.14-ZLU-15.25: Various Article 10 screening/design items - Can't evaluate without buffer being shown\n\nOther standard setbacks and items:\n- ZLU-15.2: Zoning setbacks not maintained - Can't fully determine without clear setback lines, but related to 15.1\n- ZLU-15.3: Shoreline setbacks - NOT APPLICABLE (no Lady Bird Lake or Lake Austin shoreline, not zoned LA)\n- ZLU-15.4: Through lot - NOT APPLICABLE (not a through lot)\n- ZLU-15.5: Dumpster enclosures - NOT APPLICABLE (no dumpster enclosures proposed on site or if they are, they appear to be within proper distances)\n\n\n- ZLU-15.6: Fences within setback lines - NOT APPLICABLE (site has fences but they appear to be along property lines or within setback areas that are shown)\n- ZLU-15.28-34: Waterfront overlay, shoreline, special ordinance - NOT APPLICABLE (no waterfront overlay, no shoreline, no special ordinance setbacks noted)\n- ZLU-15.35-37: Hazardous pipeline, open waterway - The cover sheet AFD Fire Analysis Table shows \"City of Austin Pipeline Ordinance Applies to Project: No\" so NOT APPLICABLE\n- ZLU-15.38: Fire department access setback - Valley View Road is a local street classified as \"Local Street\" with not less than 58 ft ROW requirement. The code specifies 30 feet from centerline for streets under 60-foot ROW, but I lack documentation of actual ROW width and building setback distances from centerline, making this NOT VERIFIABLE.\n- ZLU-15.39: Patios/balconies in rear yard - Cannot determine rear yard setback requirements without clear setback lines shown on plans.\n- ZLU-15.40: Transformer clearances - No clearance dimensions provided on electrical plan, so compliance with Austin Energy Design Criteria 1.10.4 cannot be verified.\n- ZLU-15.41-48: Fence height/design - Various fence-related requirements that depend on specific site conditions.\n\nFor the transformer pads specifically, the electrical plan shows 4 units but provides no clearance information, which means I cannot verify compliance and should mark this NOT VERIFIABLE. Regarding ZLU-15.2 on maintaining zoning setback distances, I'm unable to determine the required setback distances or confirm they're labeled on the plans, so this also cannot be verified.\n\nLooking at the relationship between items 15.1 and 15.2: the first requires showing setback lines while the second requires not encroaching into those setbacks. If the reference lines aren't clearly marked, I can't measure against them to assess whether setbacks are actually maintained. This makes 15.2 NOT VERIFIABLE rather than a failure.\n\nMy six primary findings appear to be the most significant issues. For ZLU-15.2, the lack of clear labeling prevents verification of compliance, though I should examine the dimensions shown (28.8' and others) to see if they provide enough information to assess setback maintenance. The most significant issue is that Article 10 compatibility requirements are triggered but entirely missing from the site plan documentation. This stands out as the primary concern among the findings, particularly given the emphasis on identifying missing or unverifiable elements.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":11,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3250,"cache_read_input_tokens":76100,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3250,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d203a61d-b956-4bf7-a62f-71a0e7d71a2a","uuid":"6d160c8b-5c76-4b69-ab32-f77a73a417da"}
{"level":30,"time":1776974105755,"pid":123,"hostname":"844f2260-bff","step":"review-runs","item":"15.md","index":9,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01LP8emTbVBJjL6REjbf9Ti2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Summary\n\nI have completed the review of grouping 15 (Setback Requirements and Compatibility Provisions) for the Valley View Townhomes site plan. \n\n**Critical Finding:** The site plan application incorrectly determined that Article 10 Compatibility Standards do not apply. However, the site is **MF-2 zoned and is located within 75 feet of an SF-3 triggering property**, which triggers mandatory Article 10 compliance per LDC § 25-2-1051.\n\n**Evidence of Trigger:**\n- Site zoning: MF-2 (less restrictive than MF-4 threshold)\n- Adjacent property: SF-3 (explicit triggering property zone per § 25-2-1053)\n- Distance measured: Building 6 at 24.8 feet; Building 8 at 31.2 feet from property line\n- Required compatibility buffer: 25 feet along shared property line\n- **Building 6 encroaches into the required buffer zone**\n\n**Six major deficiencies identified:**\n1. **ZLU-15.1**: Required zoning district setback lines not shown, labeled, or clearly dimensioned\n2. **ZLU-15.7**: Compatibility standards applicability incorrectly determined as \"No\" when they clearly apply\n3. **ZLU-15.10**: Compatibility buffer (25 feet) not shown; Building 6 violates buffer at 24.8 feet\n4. **ZLU-15.13**: Triggering property (SF-3 parcel) not identified on plans\n5. **ZLU-15.26**: No compatibility exhibit sheet provided (required to show zoning, distances, building locations)\n6. **ZLU-15.27**: No compatibility cross-sections provided (required to verify height compliance at 50-ft and 75-ft thresholds per § 25-2-1061)\n\nAll findings have been submitted in the structured output above."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":11,"cache_creat