{"level":30,"time":1776974111005,"pid":123,"hostname":"844f2260-bff","step":"review-runs","item":"32.md","index":4,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01Jsr2JUvj1RgR3CuYFM92qm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"No results. So the site plan does not appear to include any documentation of transit proximity per LDC § 25-1-703(B)(4), and there are no comments from the city staff requiring such documentation. This might be a NOT-VERIFIABLE situation - the requirement exists, but there's no documentation showing compliance or a waiver.\n\nLet me also check on the signage and nonconforming signs area requirements:\n\n**ZLU-32.44 - Sign Compliance Note**: The site plan on Sheet 9 Block 5 includes: \"All signs must comply with requirements of the Land Development Code (Chapter 25-10).\" This appears to address the general requirement. ✓ PASS\n\n**ZLU-32.47 - Nonconforming Signs Ordinance area**: The facts confirm the site is in a Nonconforming Signs Ordinance area. The site plan should include a note specifically addressing nonconforming signs area compliance. I haven't seen a specific note mentioning § 25-10-152 yet. Let me check if there's a more specific signage note.\n\n**ZLU-32.40 - Trip Generation Limits**: Need to check if there's a CO with trip limits. The facts don't mention a CO, and the PRF doesn't indicate a CO. So this may be NOT APPLICABLE.\n\nLet me now summarize my findings:\n\n**APPLICABLE ITEMS WITH STATUS:**\n\n1. **ZLU-32.20** (Neighborhood plan statement) - **N/A** - South Lamar NPA is SUSPENDED\n2. **ZLU-32.21** (Article 10 Compatibility Standards) - **FAIL** - Site is MF-2 adjacent to SF-3, triggering Article 10 applicability. Site plan does not demonstrate compliance; applicant even checked \"No\" to compatibility standards question.\n3. **ZLU-32.22** (Compatibility notes with current Article 10 ordinance) - **FAIL** - No compatibility notes referencing current Article 10 ordinance (Ord. \n\n20240516-004, eff. July 15, 2024) on site plan\n4. **ZLU-32.24** (On-site amenity within 25 ft) - **PASS** - BBQ pit/picnic table are 197.2 feet away\n5. **ZLU-32.26** (Outdoor noise sources) - **NOT-VERIFIABLE** - No noise analysis provided, but amenities are far enough that this may be moot\n6. **ZLU-32.28** (Rain garden in amenity) - **N/A** - No rain garden proposed as amenity\n7. **ZLU-32.29** (Article 10 exception documentation) - **FAIL** - No documentation showing any exception or variance to Article 10 requirements, which would be necessary given the compatibility standard failures and the fact that the proposed multifamily use doesn't qualify for the listed exceptions (CBD, DMU, or structural alteration only).\n8. **ZLU-32.31** (Townhouse lots) - **FAIL** - The project labels 39 units as \"townhomes\" but the site plan depicts a single Lot 1 without the required individual townhouse lot subdivision.\n9. **ZLU-32.35** (Multifamily transit proximity) - **NOT-VERIFIABLE** - Missing transit proximity documentation or director's waiver.\n10. **ZLU-32.40** (Trip generation limits) - **N/A** - No CO with trip limits identified.\n11. **ZLU-32.44** (Sign compliance note) - **PASS** - Sheet 9 Block 5 includes \"All signs must comply with requirements of the Land Development Code (Chapter 25-10)\".\n12. **ZLU-32.47** (Nonconforming Signs Ordinance area) - **FAIL** - Site is in the Nonconforming Signs Ordinance area, but the site plan lacks a specific note addressing § 25-10-152 nonconforming signs compliance.\n\nReconsidering ZLU-32.21: the deficiency focuses on demonstrating compliance through documentation, not whether the structures themselves meet Article 10 standards. The buildings appear compliant with height limits (33 feet, under the 40-foot threshold), so this might warrant reconsideration from FAIL to PASS if the compliance can be shown through plan notes.\n\nHowever, the site plan doesn't document this compliance, making it a FAIL. ZLU-32.22 similarly fails because the plan references outdated Subchapter F language rather than current Article 10 ordinance requirements.\n\nFor the townhouse designation, the Vision analysis labels these as multi-unit buildings (4-Plex, 5-Plex, 6-Plex) rather than individual townhouse lots. Since § 25-2-775 requires each townhouse unit on its own lot, this configuration doesn't meet that standard, so ZLU-32.31 is also a FAIL. Now I need to compile the complete list of failures and items that can't be verified.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":985,"cache_read_input_tokens":83609,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":985,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4e7b1c1f-9804-4a61-b82e-41dbab740236","uuid":"8ffb9907-91ef-48fc-a2d0-d8db5917cbd6"}
