{"level":30,"time":1776974128876,"pid":123,"hostname":"844f2260-bff","step":"review-runs","item":"32.md","index":4,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_018kHLqmExYK2Sn6B89dXsFT","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good, I can see that Block 5 includes \"All signs must comply with requirements of the Land Development Code (Chapter 25-10)\" which addresses ZLU-32.44. However, there is NO specific note about the Nonconforming Signs Ordinance area (ZLU-32.47). The general sign compliance note doesn't specifically reference § 25-10-152 for nonconforming signs areas.\n\nNow let me prepare my final findings. I'll output only the FAIL and NOT-VERIFIABLE items:\n\n**FAIL Items:**\n1. ZLU-32.21 - Article 10 Compatibility Standards not demonstrated on site plan\n2. ZLU-32.22 - Compatibility notes not included or don't reflect current Article 10 ordinance\n3. ZLU-32.29 - Article 10 exception not documented (doesn't appear to apply anyway)\n4. ZLU-32.31 - Townhouse lots not properly subdivided\n5. ZLU-32.47 - Nonconforming Signs Ordinance area specific note not included\n\n**NOT-VERIFIABLE Items:**\n1. ZLU-32.35 - Multifamily transit proximity not documented; no waiver provided\n2. ZLU-32.26 - Outdoor noise sources compliance not demonstrated (though may not be critical given amenity distance)\n\nWait, I need to reconsider ZLU-32.26. The deficiency is about \"outdoor noise sources (including amplified music) on the side of the building or site adjacent to a triggering property\" that \"may cause sound levels exceeding 70 decibels.\" The BBQ pit is 197 feet away, so outdoor noise from there would be very unlikely to exceed 70 dB at the SF-3 property boundary. But the requirement is still that if there ARE outdoor uses that could generate noise, compliance must be demonstrated.\n\nLooking at the site plan, the BBQ pit and picnic table are the only identified outdoor uses. \n\nThe BBQ pit sits far enough from the SF-3 boundary that noise compliance is reasonably presumed, but without an actual noise analysis, I can't formally verify it. The requirement specifically asks whether noise sources adjacent to the triggering property exceed 70 dB at the shared line, and the BBQ pit is located on the eastern side rather than the southern boundary where the SF-3 property sits. Buildings 7 and 8 occupy the southern edge, but they're residential structures without identified outdoor noise-generating uses. The southern property line appears to have a concrete retaining wall and landscaping that would further buffer sound. This suggests ZLU-32.26 likely passes since no outdoor noise sources are positioned directly adjacent to the SF-3 boundary. -3), this wouldn't trigger the requirement. I'll mark ZLU-32.26 as PASS since no outdoor noise sources exist on the side adjacent to SF-3.\n\nFor ZLU-32.29, I need to determine if the site qualifies for any Article 10 exceptions. The three categories are CBD/DMU sites, structural alterations without increased square footage or height, and specific residential uses like duplexes or care facilities. This project doesn't fit any of these, so no exception applies. The checklist indicates the site plan should note applicable exceptions, but when none exist, documentation may not be necessary.\n\nHowever, the core problem remains: Article 10 compliance itself isn't documented anywhere on the site plan. This means ZLU-32.21, which requires demonstrating Article 10 compatibility standards, is still a clear failure.\n\nMy findings break down into several categories. The main failures are missing Article 10 documentation, absent compatibility notes, improperly subdivided townhouse lots, and a missing nonconforming signs ordinance area note. For ZLU-32.35, I can't verify the multifamily transit proximity requirement since there's no documentation and no waiver on file. I should also flag ZLU-32.29 as a failure since the site doesn't document whether any Article 10 exceptions apply—this ties directly to the broader Article 10 compliance gap.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1850,"cache_read_input_tokens":84594,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1850,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4e7b1c1f-9804-4a61-b82e-41dbab740236","uuid":"0151b241-383d-49ec-9292-cc728c47c0d4"}
