collection addressed (Block 7), though central dumpster location isn't specifically marked\n9. ✓ Fence and wall details provided on site plan, including retaining wall locations\n\n**What is NOT Present or Unclear:**\n1. ✗ Adjacent zoning labels for SOUTH and WEST properties (not shown)\n2. ✗ Adjacent land uses for NORTH and WEST not clearly labeled (beyond zoning)\n3. ✗ NO note stating \"no buildings exist on adjoining lots within 50 feet\" - but this note may not be needed since buildings ARE shown on east side\n4. ✗ NO verification of adjacent dwelling unit counts (needed for Article 10 triggering property determination - though Article 10 doesn't apply since site is MF-2)\n5. ✗ NO central refuse/dumpster pad shown with distance measurements\n6. ✗ NO mechanical equipment schedule provided with noise ratings\n7. ✗ NO photometric/lighting plan with specific fixture details\n8. ✗ NO separate labeled screening/restricted zones if compatibility buffer were required (but not applicable due to MF-2 zoning)\n9. ✗ NO property connection to adjacent lots (though may not be required - need to check if site meets Subchapter E triggers)\n10. ✗ NO zoning shown on mylars (haven't checked mylars)\n11. ✗ Unclear if adjacent zoning designations are accurate\n\n/consistent with current City GIS\n\nNow checking each requirement against what's actually documented. For ZLU-16.1, the north boundary only identifies zoning without describing the actual use, the south shows an owner name but lacks use classification, while the east side properly identifies Chateaux Ridge Condominiums as a land use. This is incomplete. For ZLU-16.2, Valley View Road borders the west side, so I need to confirm whether properties across that right-of-way appear on the plan—the vision analysis suggests they don't.\n\nProperties across the street to the west aren't depicted. On ZLU-16.3, none of the adjacent parcels are marked as vacant, and the east side shows active apartment buildings. For ZLU-16.4, the east and north sides have their zoning districts labeled (MF-2-CO and MF-4-CO respectively), but the south and west properties lack zoning designations. The final item, ZLU-16.5, requires comparing the adjacent zoning against what the City GIS records actually show. are shown on the plans.\n\nFor PUD overlays, the site has no PUD designation or adjacent PUD areas, so this requirement doesn't apply. Regarding zoning designations on mylars, I haven't examined those documents yet—this would need verification against the actual mylar sheets. For adjoining building footprints within 50 feet, the existing apartment buildings to the east are depicted, and there are no structures within that distance to the north.\n\nChecking the remaining sides: south and west show no buildings within 50 feet, so the requirement is satisfied. However, the required note indicating \"no buildings exist on adjoining lots within 50 feet\" is missing from the plan where it should appear on the north and south sides. For proposed building dimensions, the data tables provide GFA, building coverage, and height information, though I should verify whether explicit dimensional callouts appear on the drawing itself.\n\nThe site plan depicts building outlines and footprints. Property connections to adjacent lots would only apply if the site were 3+ acres in a non-residential district or had parking between the building and principal street. At 2.16 acres in a multi-family residential zone, this requirement likely doesn't apply, though the parking layout on the west and south sides warrants closer examination. For condition (b), parking does appear on the west side where Valley View Road is located. If that parking sits between the building and the principal street, then connections to adjacent properties would be required—but the vision analysis shows none exist, which would be a failure.\n\nRegarding Article 10 compatibility, the site's MF-2 zoning means those requirements only apply if adjacent to SF-5 or more restrictive districts. The surrounding properties are zoned MF-2-CO, MF-4-CO, GO, MF-3, and MF-3-CO—none of which trigger the requirement. the applicability was documented on the plans. Looking at the site plan, there's no note confirming or denying Article 10's applicability, and no compatibility exhibit or discussion. However, the grouping criteria specifies this item only applies when the site is adjacent to SF-5 or more restrictive zoning, or when an Article 10 checklist item is triggered. Since the adjacent properties are zoned MF-2-CO and MF-4-CO (neither SF-5 or more restrictive), the applicability trigger isn't met, making this item N/A. I should verify the triggering property definition to confirm—a triggering property requires at least one but fewer than four dwelling units and SF-5 or more restrictive zoning.\n\nUpon reviewing the definition more carefully, \"SF-5 or more restrictive\" includes eight base residential districts: LA, RR, SF-1, SF-2, SF-3, SF-4A, SF-4B, and SF-5. The adjacent properties include an SF-3 parcel (0406100210), which is on this list and is an immediate neighbor. This SF-3 adjacency triggers the LDC Subchapter F compatibility standards, requiring multi-family development within 25 feet of that lot line to comply with a 2-story/30-foot height cap and step-back requirements.\n\nHowever, I need to distinguish between what's being triggered here. The facts reference Subchapter F restrictions, but Article 10 has its own triggering criteria: the subject site must be zoned MF-4 or less restrictive AND located within 75 feet of a qualifying property. Since the subject is zoned MF-2, I should verify whether Article 10 actually applies or if only Subchapter F applies to this SF-3 adjacency. So MF-2 is more restrictive than MF-4, which means it doesn't fall within the \"MF-4 or less restrictive\" category that triggers Article 10. The zoning alone would exclude this site from those requirements.\n\nHowever, the adjacent SF-3 property