{"level":30,"time":1776974192780,"pid":123,"hostname":"844f2260-bff","step":"review-runs","item":"15.md","index":6,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016QiB2Rv6QB4YjsAzrph8dM","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Site Plan Review\n     2→\n     3→*Requires updates to unit counts, site area calculations, building data tables, lighting notes, and administrative notes.*\n     4→\n     5→Site Plan Review – Kate Castles (512) 978-4555 - kate.castles@austintexas.gov\n     6→\n     7→LAND USE / ZONING \n     8→SP1 – Current Status: Pending\n     9→* U1: Thank you for providing the unit counts. According to 25-2-561, the minimum site area is 2400 sf for 2+ bedroom dwelling units, making the minimum site area for the site 93,600. Please update the Site Area Calculation (MF-2) table accordingly.\n    10→* U0: For Multi-Family Projects, please include the following table:\n    11→\n    12→| Unit type | Count |\n    13→| --- | --- |\n    14→| studio/eff | |\n    15→| 1 bedroom | |\n    16→| 2 bedroom | |\n    17→| 3 bedroom | |\n    18→| Total | |\n    19→\n    20→SP2 – Current Status: Pending\n    21→* U1: Please ensure that each building height is calculated correctly. The height of each building is calculated from the average of the highest and lowest grades adjacent to the building to the top of the coping. Therefore, the building height could be different for each building.\n    22→* U0: Show the following building information (show proposed and allowed) for each building and the total for all buildings in a Building Data Table:\n    23→  o gross floor area for each building (in sq. ft.)\n    24→  o building coverage for each building (in sq. ft.)\n    25→  o building height for each building (in feet and stories)\n    26→  o foundation type and finished floor elevation for each building\n    27→\n    28→SP3 – Current Status: Cleared\n    29→* U1: Multifamily use confirmed. Please let the Case Manager know if you would like to change the project name. Comment cleared. \n    30→* U0: Please confirm that you are proposing Townhouse use. FYI – Townhouses will need to plat a townhouse subdivision as not more than one townhouse is permitted on a townhouse lot. A townhouse lot must include a private yard with a wall or solid fence along a side lot line. \n    31→Reference: 25-2-775\n    32→\n    33→SUBCHAPTER E: DESIGN STANDARDS\n    34→SP4 - Current Status: Cleared\n    35→U1: Comment cleared. \n    36→U0: Include the following note with Figure 34 on the site plan page: \"All exterior lighting will be full cut-off and fully shielded in compliance with Subchapter E 2.5 and will be reviewed during building plan review. Any change or substitution of lamp/light fixtures shall be submitted to the Director for approval in accordance with Section 2.5.2.E.\" \n    37→\n    38→ADMINISTRATIVE \n    39→SP5 - Current Status: Cleared\n    40→U1: Comment cleared. \n    41→U0: Confirm that all amenities such as walls, fences, sidewalks, swimming pools, and all other land improvements are shown on each site plan sheet.\n    42→\n    43→SP6 - Current Status: Cleared\n    44→U1: Comment cleared. \n    45→U0: Please remove all City of Pflugerville Notes and show the following City of Austin site plan release notes on the site plan:\n    46→a. All improvements shall be made in accordance with the released site plan. Any additional improvements will require site plan amendment and approval of the Development Services Department.\n    47→b. Approval of this Site Plan does not include Building and Fire Code approval nor building permit approval. \n    48→c. All signs must comply with requirements of the Land Development Code (Chapter 25-10).\n    49→d. Additional electric easements may be required at a later date. \n    50→e. Water and wastewater service will be provided by the City of Austin (or identify the service provider if other than the City of Austin). \n    51→f. All existing structures shown to be removed will require a demolition permit from the City of Austin Development Services Department.\n    52→g. No certificate of occupancy may be issued for the proposed residential condominium project until the owner or owners of the property have complied with Chapter 81 and 82 of the Property Code of the State of Texas or any other statutes enacted by the State concerning condominiums.\n    53→h. For driveway construction: The owner is responsible for all costs for relocation of, or damage to utilities. \n    54→i. For construction within the right-of-way, a ROW excavation permit is required.\n    55→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"67c41a7e-de71-427c-8abb-98ffa8658f39","uuid":"3088356c-d49a-42dd-a1ba-2fab281d9846","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/vercel/sandbox/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/supplementary-docs/master-comment-report/09-site-plan-review.md","content":"# Site Plan Review\n\n*Requires updates to unit counts, site area calculations, building data tables, lighting notes, and administrative notes.*\n\nSite Plan Review – Kate Castles (512) 978-4555 - kate.castles@austintexas.gov\n\nLAND USE / ZONING \nSP1 – Current Status: Pending\n* U1: Thank you for providing the unit counts. According to 25-2-561, the minimum site area is 2400 sf for 2+ bedroom dwelling units, making the minimum site area for the site 93,600. Please update the Site Area Calculation (MF-2) table accordingly.\n* U0: For Multi-Family Projects, please include the following table:\n\n| Unit type | Count |\n| --- | --- |\n| studio/eff | |\n| 1 bedroom | |\n| 2 bedroom | |\n| 3 bedroom | |\n| Total | |\n\nSP2 – Current Status: Pending\n* U1: Please ensure that each building height is calculated correctly. The height of each building is calculated from the average of the highest and lowest grades adjacent to the building to the top of the coping. Therefore, the building height could be different for each building.\n* U0: Show the following building information (show proposed and allowed) for each building and the total for all buildings in a Building Data Table:\n  o gross floor area for each building (in sq. ft.)\n  o building coverage for each building (in sq. ft.)\n  o building height for each building (in feet and stories)\n  o foundation type and finished floor elevation for each building\n\nSP3 – Current Status: Cleared\n* U1: Multifamily use confirmed. Please let the Case Manager know if you would like to change the project name. Comment cleared. \n* U0: Please confirm that you are proposing Townhouse use. FYI – Townhouses will need to plat a townhouse subdivision as not more than one townhouse is permitted on a townhouse lot. A townhouse lot must include a private yard with a wall or solid fence along a side lot line. \nReference: 25-2-775\n\nSUBCHAPTER E: DESIGN STANDARDS\nSP4 - Current Status: Cleared\nU1: Comment cleared. \nU0: Include the following note with Figure 34 on the site plan page: \"All exterior lighting will be full cut-off and fully shielded in compliance with Subchapter E 2.5 and will be reviewed during building plan review. Any change or substitution of lamp/light fixtures shall be submitted to the Director for approval in accordance with Section 2.5.2.E.\" \n\nADMINISTRATIVE \nSP5 - Current Status: Cleared\nU1: Comment cleared. \nU0: Confirm that all amenities such as walls, fences, sidewalks, swimming pools, and all other land improvements are shown on each site plan sheet.\n\nSP6 - Current Status: Cleared\nU1: Comment cleared. \nU0: Please remove all City of Pflugerville Notes and show the following City of Austin site plan release notes on the site plan:\na. All improvements shall be made in accordance with the released site plan. Any additional improvements will require site plan amendment and approval of the Development Services Department.\nb. Approval of this Site Plan does not include Building and Fire Code approval nor building permit approval. \nc. All signs must comply with requirements of the Land Development Code (Chapter 25-10).\nd. Additional electric easements may be required at a later date. \ne. Water and wastewater service will be provided by the City of Austin (or identify the service provider if other than the City of Austin). \nf. All existing structures shown to be removed will require a demolition permit from the City of Austin Development Services Department.\ng. No certificate of occupancy may be issued for the proposed residential condominium project until the owner or owners of the property have complied with Chapter 81 and 82 of the Property Code of the State of Texas or any other statutes enacted by the State concerning condominiums.\nh. For driveway construction: The owner is responsible for all costs for relocation of, or damage to utilities. \ni. For construction within the right-of-way, a ROW excavation permit is required.\n","numLines":55,"startLine":1,"totalLines":55}}}
{"level":30,"time":1776974225854,"pid":123,"hostname":"844f2260-bff","step":"review-runs","item":"15.md","index":6,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01UDEbYG6RyHthLgtuPYfMuq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I don't see any City comments about compatibility standards, Article 10, setbacks, or transformer clearances in the Site Plan Review section. This is notable - if the City has reviewed the plans, they haven't flagged compatibility issues yet. But that doesn't mean they don't exist; the City review might not have been thorough or the review comments might be pending.\n\nLet me now compile my final research findings and make determinations for each checklist item.\n\nMy research phase findings:\n\n**CONFIRMED DEFICIENCIES:**\n\n1. **Compatibility Buffer Not Shown** (ZLU-15.10):\n   - Vision analysis of both Site Plan (Sheet 9) and Landscape Plan (Sheet 31) found NO compatibility buffer lines, zones, or labels\n   - § 25-2-1062(B) requires 25-ft landscaped buffer along shared SF-3 property line\n   - FAIL\n\n2. **Compatibility Exhibit Not Provided** (ZLU-15.26):\n   - Sheet list (Sheets 1-39) does not include a separate \"Compatibility Exhibit\" sheet\n   - § 25-2-1051 requires separate exhibit showing property boundaries, zoning, distances, existing structures\n   - FAIL\n\n3. **Compatibility Cross-Sections Not Provided** (ZLU-15.27):\n   - No cross-section sheets identified in the plan set\n   - § 25-2-1061 requires cross-sections showing height vs. distance relationships at 50-ft and 75-ft thresholds\n   - FAIL\n\n4. **Transformer Clearances Not Dimensioned** (ZLU-15.40):\n   - Vision analysis of Electrical Plan (Sheet 21) found 4 transformer pads with NO clearance dimensions or labels\n   - Austin Energy Design Criteria 1.10.4 requires specific clearances (10 ft, 5 ft, 12 ft, etc.) depending on building construction\n   - FAIL\n\n**ITEMS THAT CANNOT BE VERIFIED:**\n\n1. **Zoning Setbacks Not Maintained** (ZLU-15.2):\n   - MF-2 required setbacks from § 25-2-492 not provided in the available documents\n   - Cannot determine if shown distances (25.0', 21.3', 44.2', 46.9') meet requirements\n   - NOT-VERIFIABLE\n\n2. **Height Limits Not Shown/Maintained** (ZLU-15.8):\n   - Article 10 height zones (< 50 ft = 40 ft max; 50-74 ft = 60 ft max; ≥ 75 ft = base height) not clearly mapped on plans\n   - Proposed building height not explicitly labeled against these thresholds\n   - NOT-VERIFIABLE\n\n3. **Triggering Property Existing Structures Not Shown** (ZLU-15.9):\n   - Compatibility exhibit missing, preventing documentation of existing SF-3 structures\n   - NOT-VERIFIABLE (requires exhibit)\n\n4. **Triggering Property Not Clearly Identified** (ZLU-15.13):\n   - SF-3 zoning labeled on site plan\n   - Parcel number (0406100210) and dwelling unit count absent from documentation\n   - § 25-2-1053 requires explicit identification\n   - NOT-VERIFIABLE\n\n5. **Prohibited Improvements in Screening Zone** (ZLU-15.15):\n   - Parking/driveway distance from SF-3 property line not documented\n\n, making it impossible to confirm whether parking falls within the prohibited 10-ft screening zone\n   - NOT-VERIFIABLE\n\n**POSSIBLE DEFICIENCIES (MARGINAL):**\n\n1. **Setback Lines Not Explicitly Labeled** (ZLU-15.1):\n   - Dimensions and dashed lines parallel to boundaries are present, but the lines themselves lack \"Setback Line\" labels\n   - The dimensioning could satisfy requirements, though explicit labeling is ambiguous\n   - Marking as NOT-VERIFIABLE due to this ambiguity\n\n2. **Compatibility Applicability Incorrectly Determined** (ZLU-15.7):\n   - Article 10 is not cited anywhere in the plans, suggesting it may not have been evaluated or applied\n   - The adjacent SF-3 property clearly triggers Article 10 requirements, yet no compatibility analysis appears\n   - This is a FAIL—the applicability determination seems absent or incorrect\n\nActually, reconsidering ZLU-15.7: the checklist asks whether applicability was \"incorrectly determined.\" If no determination was made at all, that's undocumented rather than incorrect. But the real issue is whether they're using outdated frameworks (the repealed § 25-2-1081/1082 thresholds of 50/100/300/540 ft instead of the current 75 ft standard) or misapplying compatibility rules to wrong zoning categories.\n\nThe submission doesn't cite any of these specific errors—it simply omits Article 10 entirely. So the determination isn't actively wrong, just missing from the record. Yet this omission cascades: without addressing Article 10 applicability, none of the required elements (buffer zones, height restrictions, cross-sections, exhibits) are documented. The actual deficiencies get captured elsewhere in ZLU-15.10, ZLU-15.26, and ZLU-15.27.\n\nI'll mark ZLU-15.7 as NOT-VERIFIABLE—Cannot determine if applicability was correctly evaluated since the plans don't reference Article 10 or provide the compatibility documentation needed to verify it.\n\nMy final assessment breaks down into four failures and six items I cannot verify. The failures are the missing compatibility buffer, the absent compatibility exhibit, missing cross-sections, and undimensioned transformer clearances. The not-verifiable items stem from missing documentation: no setback table for verification, no Article 10 applicability analysis, height limits without distance zones, no exhibit showing triggering structures, missing unit counts or parcel identification for triggering properties, and incomplete screening details. The clearance dimensions are absent from the electrical plan, confirming these are legitimate failures rather than verification gaps.\n\nFor items I cannot verify: the setback dimensions are provided (25.0', 21.3'), but without access to the specific MF-2 minimums from § 25-2-492, I can't confirm compliance. The compatibility determination presents ambiguity—either they made an incorrect assessment or simply didn't document their reasoning, making it difficult to classify definitively as a failure versus an information gap.\n\nHeight documentation exists for the buildings themselves, yet the Article 10 distance-based zones aren't mapped, preventing verification of those particular limits. The triggering property structures should be shown in the missing ZLU-15.26 exhibit, so without it I cannot assess this requirement. Similarly, while SF-3 zoning appears on the plan, the dwelling unit count for the adjacent property isn't stated, so I cannot confirm it meets the 1-3 unit threshold under § 25-2-1053. The screening zone requirements also lack sufficient documentation to verify compliance.\n\nFor the setback lines themselves, I need to distinguish between what's actually present. The dashed lines parallel to the property boundaries are visible and dimensioned with distance callouts, but they lack explicit labeling as \"Setback Line\" or similar designation. The requirement appears to demand all three elements—visibility, labeling, and dimensioning—so the absence of clear labels means this still falls short of full compliance. there are dashed lines running parallel to the property boundaries with dimension lines showing exact distances (25.0', 21.3', 44.2', 46.9'). The setback information is present and understandable from context, even without explicit \"Setback Line\" labels. This seems more like an ambiguity issue than a substantive failure—the practical intent is clear to a reviewer.\n\nI'm settling on NOT-VERIFIABLE for ZLU-15.1 since the setback concept is demonstrated but lacks formal labeling. Moving forward with the final assessment: four items fail, including the missing compatibility buffer along the SF-3 boundary and the absent exhibit/cross-section requirements.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":10,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1531,"cache_read_input_tokens":76552,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1531,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"67c41a7e-de71-427c-8abb-98ffa8658f39","uuid":"1a047d41-fdc1-4dc1-8e96-ac7c99ff9be0"}
{"level":30,"time":1776974230283,"pid":123,"hostname":"844f2260-bff","step":"review-runs","item":"15.md","index":6,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01UDEbYG6RyHthLgtuPYfMuq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on my comprehensive research phase, I have identified clear deficiencies in the site plan's documentation of setback and compatibility standards. Let me now prepare the final structured findings.\n\n## RESEARCH SUMMARY\n\n**Site Profile:**\n- Zoning: MF-2 (Multi-Family Residence)\n- Triggering Property: Adjacent SF-3 parcel (0406100210) within 75 ft of site boundary\n- Applicable Code: LDC §§ 25-2-1051 through 25-2-1063 (Article 10 Compatibility Standards, effective July 15, 2024)\n- Submittal Date: May 20, 2025 (after effective date of new Article 10)\n\n**Required Elements NOT Found:**\n- Article 10 compatibility standards not referenced or cited on cover sheet\n- Compatibility buffer lines not shown on site plan or landscape plan (Vision: \"No lines, hatched areas, or zones explicitly labeled as a 'Compatibility Buffer' anywhere on the visible site plan\")\n- Separate compatibility exhibit sheet not in plan set (39 total sheets listed; none titled \"Compatibility Exhibit\")\n- Compatibility cross-section sheets not in plan set showing height-distance relationships at 50-ft and 75-ft thresholds\n- Transformer pad clearance dimensions not shown (Vision: \"No dimensions shown for clearances around any of the transformer pads on this specific sheet\")\n- Triggering property dwelling unit count and parcel number not explicitly identified on plans\n- Setback lines shown with dimensions but not explicitly labeled as \"Setback Lines\"\n\n**Elements Requiring Further Clarification:**\n- MF-2 required setback minimums not provided in accessible documents (cannot verify shown distances against code requirements)\n- Article 10 height-distance zones not documented on plans (cannot verify compliance with 40-ft limit < 50 ft from SF-3 boundary, etc.)\n- Parking/driveway distance from SF-3 property line not dimensioned (cannot verify if within prohibited 10-ft screening zone)\n\n---"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":10,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1531,"cache_read_input_tokens":76552,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1531,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"67c41a7e-de71-427c-8abb-98ffa8658f39","uuid":"639afdb1-0fee-4aa9-88da-249b1c65464f"}
{"level":30,"time":1776974253066,"pid":123,"hostname":"844f2260-bff","step":"review-runs","item":"15.md","index":6,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01UDEbYG6RyHthLgtuPYfMuq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01B7cPCURRfuBGZ1oZUKYD81","name":"StructuredOutput","input":{"grouping":"15","findings":[{"deficiencyId":"ZLU-15.1","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["LDC § 25-2-492"],"applicableAreas":["All property boundaries"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Setback dimensions are provided on the site plan (e.g., 25.0', 21.3', 44.2', 46.9' from buildings to property lines), and dashed lines appear to indicate setback boundaries. However, these lines are not explicitly labeled as 'Setback Lines' or 'Building Setback,' making it ambiguous whether formal setback line designation has been met per requirements for explicit labeling. Additionally, without access to the required MF-2 setback minimums from LDC § 25-2-492, cannot verify that shown distances meet code minimums."},{"deficiencyId":"ZLU-15.2","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["LDC § 25-2-492"],"applicableAreas":["All setback areas"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"The required setback table from LDC § 25-2-492 for MF-2 district (front yard, rear yard, interior side, street side minimums) is not provided in the submitted documents. Although the site plan shows setback dimensions, cannot verify that these distances meet or exceed the code-required minimums without access to the applicable setback table."},{"deficiencyId":"ZLU-15.7","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["LDC § 25-2-1051","LDC § 25-2-1052","LDC § 25-2-1053"],"applicableAreas":["Site boundary and adjacent SF-3 property"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":1},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"The site is zoned MF-2 (less restrictive than MF-4), and an adjacent SF-3 property exists within the site boundary (Vision confirms 'SF-3' zoning labeled on site plan). Article 10 compatibility standards should apply per § 25-2-1051. However, neither the cover sheet nor the site plan documentation references Article 10, compatibility standards, or the applicability determination. Without explicit documentation of the applicability analysis, cannot verify whether the site's Article 10 applicability has been correctly determined."},{"deficiencyId":"ZLU-15.8","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["LDC § 25-2-1061"],"applicableAreas":["Buildings 6, 7, and 8 (closest to SF-3 property line); structures within 75 feet of SF-3 boundary"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Article 10 height limits require: structures < 50 ft from triggering property boundary ≤ 40 ft; 50–74 ft ≤ 60 ft; ≥ 75 ft = base zoning (§ 25-2-1061). Vision analysis confirms Building 8 is 46.9' from SF-3 boundary and Building 6 is 21.3' from SF-3 boundary, both within the 50-ft zone requiring 40-ft max height. Building heights shown (36'-1\" max, 33'-4.75\" for Buildings 6 and 8) appear numerically compliant. However, the site plan does not depict the distance-based height limit zones (50-ft and 75-ft thresholds) or demonstrate height compliance with the distance bands. Cannot fully verify compliance without these documented height limit zones."},{"deficiencyId":"ZLU-15.9","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["LDC § 25-2-1051"],"applicableAreas":["Adjacent SF-3 property (0406100210)"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"The required separate compatibility exhibit (per ZLU-15.26) must document the approximate location and extent of existing structures on the triggering SF-3 property to verify distance measurements for height limit and buffer compliance. No separate compatibility exhibit is provided in the plan set. Therefore, the location of existing structures on the triggering property cannot be documented or verified."},{"deficiencyId":"ZLU-15.10","status":"fail","codeCitations":["LDC § 25-2-1062(B)","LDC § 25-8-700"],"applicableAreas":["Southern property line shared with SF-3 property"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Article 10 requires a 25-foot landscaped buffer along the shared triggering property line, or 15 feet if the development site measures less than 75 feet wide from the shared boundary (LDC § 25-2-1062(B)). Vision analysis of both the site plan (Sheet 9) and landscape plan (Sheet 31) confirms: 'No lines, hatched areas, or zones explicitly labeled as a Compatibility Buffer anywhere on the visible site plan' and 'No compatibility buffer zones labeled' on the landscape plan. The required compatibility buffer is not shown, labeled, or dimensioned on either the site plan or landscape plan."},{"deficiencyId":"ZLU-15.13","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["LDC § 25-2-1053"],"applicableAreas":["Adjacent SF-3 property"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"A triggering property under § 25-2-1053 must have 1–3 dwelling units and be zoned SF-5 or more restrictive (including SF-3). The site plan labels the adjacent property as 'SF-3' zoning, but does not identify the specific parcel number (0406100210) or provide documentation of the dwelling unit count. Without clear identification including parcel designation and dwelling unit count, cannot verify the triggering property meets the statutory definition."},{"deficiencyId":"ZLU-15.15","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["LDC § 25-8-700"],"applicableAreas":["Southern property line shared with SF-3 property (10-foot screening zone from boundary)"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"The 10-foot screening zone from the shared triggering property line is prohibited from containing vertical structures, parking areas, driveways, or mechanical equipment per § 25-8-700. Vision analysis notes: 'A driveway/parking access lane runs parallel to the southern property line. It is separated from the property line by a landscape strip' with observation that 'while this paved area is visibly close to the southern boundary, there are no explicit dimension lines provided in this specific area to confirm whether the distance is exactly 10 feet or less.' Without dimensioned distances showing the parking/driveway edge location relative to the southern property line, cannot verify compliance with the screening zone prohibition."},{"deficiencyId":"ZLU-15.26","status":"fail","codeCitations":["LDC § 25-2-1051"],"applicableAreas":["Entire site plan with compatibility exhibit requirements"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":1}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"A separate compatibility exhibit is required to document property boundaries, on-site and off-site zoning boundaries (all triggering properties and applicable combining districts), distances from the triggering property boundary to existing and proposed structures, distances to surface improvements (parking, driveways, drainage features), and the location of existing structures on triggering properties. The sheet index lists 39 total sheets but includes no separate compatibility exhibit. This required documentation is not provided."},{"deficiencyId":"ZLU-15.27","status":"fail","codeCitations":["LDC § 25-2-1061"],"applicableAreas":["Structures proposed within 75 feet of SF-3 property boundary"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":1}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Compatibility cross-sections are required to show: (1) the triggering property boundary, (2) distance measurements from the triggering property boundary to proposed structures at the 50-foot and 75-foot thresholds, (3) proposed building heights at each distance band, and (4) elevation of triggering property grade. These cross-sections demonstrate compliance with § 25-2-1061 height limit bands (< 50 ft = 40-ft max; 50–74 ft = 60-ft max). The plan set (39 sheets) includes no cross-section sheets labeled for compatibility analysis. This required documentation is not provided."},{"deficiencyId":"ZLU-15.40","status":"fail","codeCitations":["Austin Energy Design Criteria 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pad locations on site (northwest, mid-west, east, and south-central areas per electrical plan)"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Four transformer pads are shown on the electrical design plan but without any clearance dimensions or specifications per Austin Energy Design Criteria 1.10.4. Vision analysis confirms: 'There are no dimensions shown for clearances around any of the transformer pads on this specific sheet' and 'No labels specifying required clearance distances around the transformer pads.' Required clearances vary by construction type (e.g., 10 feet to hot-stick sides, 5 feet to masonry, 12 feet to non-masonry buildings, etc.). Without dimensioned clearances and identification of building construction types, transformer pad compliance cannot be verified."}]},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":10,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1531,"cache_read_input_tokens":76552,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1531,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"67c41a7e-de71-427c-8abb-98ffa8658f39","uuid":"1250548d-8dc0-468e-a387-60e35fce7e10"}
